{"parentUuid":"c5875905-c693-4f0e-8d67-dbd5924a4fd6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"eb6cbe51-8dc5-48b8-b7ae-d7d6e1fb6b02","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nLinked sessions now (status, not an instruction): collect-jusprin-v1-usage = local_a7a1196e-7a91-4c40-8f96-177e81f5d1d4 (idle); jusprin-pricing-model-11 = local_aa11def1-46cb-4722-affe-13a9a32d9cb4 (idle); measure-3-user-journeys = local_aea26300-e25d-4c38-8bbf-7b402507987f (idle); fix-plan-journey-on-the = local_3a672aa9-be93-4897-b8d5-2370a20742e4 (idle, started by measure-3-user-journeys); measure-the-3-user-journ = local_e777a6fc-f059-43ec-b618-24dc7d55170b (idle); draw-the-credits-and-pla = local_b14d4c8e-5962-47f4-93d0-a36258ec6863 (idle). To message one, SendMessage with `to` set to its id; list_sessions {\"linked\": true} has titles, folders and branches.\n</system-reminder>\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n<pasted_content id=\"eef2\">\nIt is a commit in the tsd-enterprise repository, the gateway:\n\n* “Keep JusPrin v2 chats for future fine-tuning”, 2026-10-29 at 15:02, 9 files, mostly web_ent/jusprin/v2/capture.py and its tests. The gateway keeps each chat’s newest request and reply in Redis, then writes it to storage once the chat is quiet.\n* It was made by a different Claude session you opened in the JusPrin project that day. Its first message asked to find the recent work wiring the client to the server as the model provider. That session built the capture on a tsd-enterprise branch, then squashed and cherry-picked it onto local master. Its memory note says the opt-out was folded into that same commit at your decision.\n* It is now on origin/master and origin/release in tsd-enterprise, so it has been pushed since. Whether it is deployed I did not check.\n\nis this true? why is it specific to openrouter?\n</pasted_content id=\"eef2\">\n"}]},"uuid":"31771a14-b14a-46a7-9a12-1ede49c7590c","timestamp":"2026-11-02T16:10:05.921Z","permissionMode":"b