{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","hash":"50a8f22abaa4ccf8a168eacf087c75de77030af77eaf4cf72ae063dabdf45495","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JzvPfxM5E8yHBBmC53DQo3","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan","input":{"items":[{"content":"Check the pasted commit claims in git","status":"in_progress"},{"content":"Read how the gateway collects replies per provider","status":"pending"}],"scope":"continuation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KGgXBrmjnXtPTqJqvh3LBE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"R=/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise; git -C $R log --all --format='%h %ad %an %s' --date=iso --grep='Keep JusPrin v2 chats' | cut -c1-140; git -C $R log --all --format='%h %ad %s' --date=iso -- web_ent/jusprin/v2/capture.py | cut -c1-120 | head; C=906752ee3e; git -C $R show --stat --format='%h %ad %an%n%s%n%n%b' --date=iso $C | cut -c1-120 | head -40; echo --- branches; git -C $R branch -a --contains $C | cut -c1-80; git -C $R log -1 --format='%h %ad' --date=iso origin/release; git -C $R log -1 --format='%h %ad' --date=iso origin/master","description":"Check the commit's date, files, and which branches contain it","timeout":30000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R8CQ2XfM1XEpRBJDQNTbF3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"M=/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory; cat $M/jusprin-chat-capture-design.md | cut -c1-400; R=/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise/.claude/worktrees/credits-ledger; G=$R/web_ent/jusprin/v2/gateway.py; grep -n \"_collect\\|DONE\\|json.loads\\|could not keep\\|capture\\|anthropic\\|openrouter\\|def \" $G | cut -c1-130 | head -90","description":"Read the capture memory note and locate reply collection in the gateway","timeout":20000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","hash":"e492cd0bb90e870428ddc5583fb43d53d21c6bf264ae2332dd301eb717d8599c","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JzvPfxM5E8yHBBmC53DQo3","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan shown (2 steps)."}]},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KGgXBrmjnXtPTqJqvh3LBE","type":"tool_result","content":"906752ee3e 2026-10-29 15:02:28 -0700 Kenneth Jiang Keep JusPrin v2 chats for future fine-tuning\n906752ee3e 2026-10-29 15:02:28 -0700 Keep JusPrin v2 chats for future fine-tuning\n906752ee3e 2026-10-29 15:02:28 -0700 Kenneth Jiang\nKeep JusPrin v2 chats for future fine-tuning\n\nThe gateway now keeps each chat's newest request and its reply, so the\nchats can later be used as training data. The app sends the whole chat in\nevery request, so the newest request plus its reply is the whole chat.\nEvery chat is kept; sharing chats for a reward will be arranged with people\ncase by case, so there is no per-account switch.\n\n- Naming a chat: the app may send X-JusPrin-Chat, a random-looking\n  32-hex-digit id per chat. Any other value is a 400. A request without it\n  is kept as a chat of its own turn. Records are keyed by user id too, so\n  no one can write into another person's chat.\n- Buffering: after a reply completes, the gateway stores the gzipped record\n  in Redis and marks the chat pending. A Celery task every 5 minutes writes\n  chats with no request for 15 minutes to long-term storage as\n  <user id>/<chat>.json.gz, overwriting the earlier copy. That is about one\n  storage write per chat per sitting.\n- Branches: a request whose messages do not extend the kept ones (a retry,\n  an edit, a revert) first writes the version it replaces as\n  <user id>/<chat>/branch-<ms>.json.gz. cache_control is ignored when\n  comparing, because the app moves its breakpoint on every request.\n- Deletion: deleting an account deletes its kept chats, and the flush task\n  drops chats of accounts deleted since.\n- Off unless JUSPRIN_V2_CAPTURE_CONTAINER names a container. Titles and\n  failed replies are not kept. A reply over 4 MiB is cut there and the\n  record is marked truncated.\n- A failure to keep a chat is reported to Sentry and dropped, because the\n  person already has the reply. This is the gateway's one swallowed error.\n- Langfuse metadata now includes request_bytes, to size Redis and storage.\n- gcp_file_storage gains delete_dir.\n\n\n web_ent/app_ent/lib/gcp_file_storage.py  |   7 +\n web_ent/app_ent/tasks/jusprin_tasks.py   |  13 ++\n web_ent/app_ent/test_gcp_file_storage.py |  15 +-\n web_ent/jusprin/apps.py                  |  17 ++-\n web_ent/jusprin/v2/capture.py            | 182 ++++++++++++++++++++++++\n web_ent/jusprin/v2/gateway.py            |  69 ++++++++-\n web_ent/jusprin/v2/tests/test_capture.py | 231 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n--- branches\n+ claude/awesome-benz-66231b\n+ claude/credits-ledger\n* master\n  release\n  remotes/origin/HEAD -> origin/master\n  remotes/origin/master\n  remotes/origin/release\ne0e5d8aaea 2026-10-29 20:11:45 -0700\n7edf2085c0 2026-10-29 20:10:25 -0700","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R8CQ2XfM1XEpRBJDQNTbF3","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: jusprin-chat-capture-design\ndescription: \"2026-10-29 server-side chat capture for future fine-tuning — design draft 2 (untracked in tsd-enterprise root), Kenneth's decisions, open questions\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: da2359ba-b0d6-437d-947e-825dd8c3efed\n  modified: 2026-10-29T19:16:01.744Z\n---\n\nDesign doc: `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise/jusprin-v2-chat-capture-design.md` (untracked, draft 2).\n\n**Built 2026-10-29; cherry-picked the same day to local tsd-enterprise master (906752ee3e after squashing, on unpushed a22082b0cb) and local jusprin-newui (30ae01eae0, one commit: chat_key plumbing copied byte-for-byte from a08d17471f without prompt_cache_key, plus the header). Nothing pushed or deployed.** Originally (branches and worktrees deleted 2026-10-29 after squashing): gateway on tsd-ente\n\nKenneth's decisions (2026-10-29):\n- **Chat id:** the app sends its own random `chatUid` in an `X-JusPrin-Chat` header. The turn id (`<project>-<conversation>-<message>-attempt-n`) can't be split reliably, because conversation ids are `c-1` and restart per project.\n- **No trimming:** the app removes history trimming, so the newest request of a chat is the whole chat.\n- **Buffered saves:** keep the newest request plus its reply per chat in Redis, and have a Celery beat task write it to GCS once the chat is quiet. Kenneth called saving every request \"pretty dumb\".\n- **Consent:** opt-out was decided, then removed the same day (folded into 906752ee3e): keep every chat; sharing for a reward is arranged case by case. No account field or toggle. Account deletion still deletes kept chats.\n- **Retention:** kept until the person opts out or deletes their account; no age limit.\n\n**Why:** Kenneth wants the stored chats usable as fine-tuning data later.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Still open: a legal read on the vendor terms. Anthropic's and OpenAI's terms forbid training competing models on their output.\n- The privacy policy (last updated 2022-04-05) has to be updated and people notified before capture starts.\n- Related: [[jusprin-cloud-provider]].\n33:from . import capture\n54:def _loop_state():\n65:def upstream_client() -> httpx.AsyncClient:\n76:async def _large_request_slot(scope):\n105:    def __init__(self, fmt: str):\n108:    def __call__(self, request, *args, **kwargs):\n116:    async def asgi(self, scope, receive, send):\n131:    async def _handle(self, scope, receive, send):\n135:    async def _handle_in(self, scope, receive, send, stack):\n150:            if chat_id is not None and not capture.CHAT_ID.match(chat_id):\n178:        keep = request_kind != 'title' and capture.enabled()\n180:                     capture.chat_key(chat_id, turn_id) if keep else None, chat_id)\n199:    if its chat is kept (keep_key is the chat's key in jusprin.v2.capture, or\n202:    def __init__(self, fmt, upstream: UpstreamRequest, user_id, turn_id, request_kind, keep_key=None,\n218:    async def relay(self, send):\n224:    async def keep(self):\n233:            sentry_sdk.capture_exception()\n234:            logger.exception('JusPrin v2 could not keep a chat request')\n236:    def _keep_sync(self):\n238:        capture.keep(self.user_id, self.keep_key, self.fmt, {\n249:            'request': json.loads(self.upstream.body),\n250:            'events': [json.loads(data) for data in self.events],\n254:    def _collect(self, event):\n264:    async def _relay(self, send):\n291:                        self._collect(event)\n307:    def _upstream_failed(self, what, status, request_id):\n314:            sentry_sdk.capture_message(text, level='error')\n317:    def _log(self):\n319:        No prompt or output is captured.\"\"\"\n351:def _release_connection():\n360:def _finish_request(sender):\n365:def _authenticate_scope(scope):\n371:def _headers(scope):\n375:async def _read_body(receive, limit):\n392:async def _wait_for_disconnect(receive):\n397:async def _send_error(send, error: GatewayError):\n405:def _request_id(response):","is_error":false}]}}
