{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","id":"aaf2fa6e-499a-43e5-aa70-7ceb79063f0f","timestamp":"2026-11-02T16:11:22.102Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"8d45efdc67b5065b826b225c6fae0a4acb4aba598709c43f8feaca22fa764775","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"5af21670-c5d7-49d9-ab8f-9587f1deded8","keep":98,"tail":["05fe80e5339f169a854bbaa132c87bfa0550185f2fbf3b29d6cae8e24a731081","2671e027cb84b7151d8c4125de7180b6d5d767321bf2c1e8ade690bd540ef265","8d5417819870814c986d7076932ad2dcad28287bdd05a674772b4c6ce5fb42e5"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",100,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"92aeef5142612fcc019e816e434d72d3d63e340b77f0ae3b710d6d5290ad73cd"}
{"parentUuid":"2dc4552d-32d9-4679-ab50-575a54b5599c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgePqfZcT5tJKUeHaoSYP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The pasted description is mostly true, but it has two errors. The bug isn't really about OpenRouter as a company: it hits any provider whose stream ends with a `[DONE]` line, and of the providers I checked, only OpenRouter documents one.\n\n## Is the description true?\n\n| Claim | Verdict |\n|---|---|\n| Commit title, 2026-10-29 at 15:02, 9 files | True (`906752ee3e`) |\n| Mostly `capture.py` and its tests | True: 413 of the 541 added lines |\n| Keeps the newest request and reply in Redis, writes to storage once the chat is quiet | True: it writes after 15 quiet minutes, and the job runs every 5 |\n| Made by a session that started by asking to find the client-to-server wiring work | True: my memory note about the capture points to that session, and its first message matches |\n| That session was opened \"that day\" | **False:** it started on 2026-10-27, two days before the commit |\n| \"The opt-out was folded into that same commit\" | **Misleading:** the opt-out's *removal* was folded in. The commit message says every chat is kept and there is no per-account switch |\n| On `origin/master` and `origin/release` | True |\n\n- **Stale memory note:** my note on the capture says \"Nothing pushed\", which is out of date. It also still says chats are kept \"until the person opts out\", which contradicts the no-opt-out decision.\n- **Deployment:** I didn't check this either. Capture only runs if `JUSPRIN_V2_CAPTURE_CONTAINER` is set. I found no mention of it in the main `ops` checkout, which suggests it may be off, but I didn't look at the running servers.\n\n## Why it only hits OpenRouter\n\nThe code doesn't treat any provider differently. To keep a chat, `_keep_sync` in `web_ent/jusprin/v2/gateway.py` parses every saved stream event as JSON, so one non-JSON event makes it fail.\n\n- **OpenRouter:** its docs show its streaming Responses API ending with `data: [DONE]`, which isn't JSON. Standard uses OpenRouter (`deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash`), so every Standard chat fails.\n- **Anthropic:** Expert chats ran through it in the live test without this error, and I don't expect its stream to end with `[DONE]`.\n- **OpenAI direct:** I expect this to be fine too, since I don't believe its Responses API sends `[DONE]`. That comes from memory, not from a test or from reading its docs.\n\n**How sure this is:** running `json.loads('[DONE]')` gives exactly the logged error, `Expecting value: line 1 column 2`. Together with OpenRouter's docs, that makes this a strong inference, but I didn't read the raw stream, because that would have meant another paid model call.\n\n**Why the tests missed it:** nothing in the gateway code or its tests mentions `[DONE]`, so the fake streams in the tests never send it. The code that forwards replies to the app didn't crash on the same line in the live chats; only the code that keeps chats does.\n\n**Effect:** the person still gets their reply, but the whole record for that request is lost, not just the last line. If capture is on in production, no Standard chats are being kept for fine-tuning.\n\nSources:\n- [OpenRouter Responses API, basic usage](https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/reference/responses/basic-usage)\n- [OpenRouter API reference, create a response (mirror)](https://openrouter.helicone.ai/docs/api/api-reference/responses/create-a-response.md)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1425,"cache_read_input_tokens":200852,"output_tokens":1187,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1425,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1187,"cache_read_input_tokens":200852,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1425,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1425},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgePqfFG8aaS5qUb5ZFNj","requestRef":"aaf2fa6e-499a-43e5-aa70-7ceb79063f0f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"002bb532-25eb-4bec-821a-efee21521893","timestamp":"2026-11-02T16:11:33.111Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
