{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-02T16:30:21.346Z","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","content":"<system-reminder>\nLinked sessions now (status, not an instruction): collect-jusprin-v1-usage = local_a7a1196e-7a91-4c40-8f96-177e81f5d1d4 (idle); jusprin-pricing-model-11 = local_aa11def1-46cb-4722-affe-13a9a32d9cb4 (idle); measure-3-user-journeys = local_aea26300-e25d-4c38-8bbf-7b402507987f (idle); fix-plan-journey-on-the = local_3a672aa9-be93-4897-b8d5-2370a20742e4 (idle, started by measure-3-user-journeys); measure-the-3-user-journ = local_e777a6fc-f059-43ec-b618-24dc7d55170b (idle); draw-the-credits-and-pla = local_b14d4c8e-5962-47f4-93d0-a36258ec6863 (idle). To message one, SendMessage with `to` set to its id; list_sessions {\"linked\": true} has titles, folders and branches.\n</system-reminder>\n\n<cross-session-message from=\"local_e565e660-16e8-4367-a2d3-2f4bfc3c942b\" from-name=\"Build JusPrin Cloud credits and finish onboarding\">\nKenneth asks you to make `_keep_sync` in tsd-enterprise `web_ent/jusprin/v2/gateway.py` a blind write, and to stop and ask him if the change won't delete far more lines than it adds.\n\nThe change: store the request body and the reply events as the raw text they arrived in, with no `json.loads` in `_keep_sync`. Today `[json.loads(data) for data in self.events]` throws on OpenRouter's `data: [DONE]` line, so every Standard chat's record is lost. This replaces the narrower \"skip [DONE]\" fix you offered.\n\nKenneth's words on size: he expects \"a lot more lines of code to be deleted than to be added\". If that won't hold, stop and ask him before going on.\n\nWorked out in a side session, not yet checked: if the branch comparison in `capture.keep` needs the messages, any parsing belongs there, not in `_keep_sync`. I have not read `capture.keep`, so read it first. I also found no sign that anything reads these records or that capture is on in production; neither is verified, so don't assume a schema bump is needed. `test_capture.py` reads event fields directly and will need updating. Add a test whose fake stream ends in `data: [DONE]`.\n\nNothing has been changed. Commit or deploy only if Kenneth asks.\n</cross-session-message>"}
