{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","id":"feb78ef2-a2f6-48fa-9617-6308c0d6efb1","timestamp":"2026-11-02T16:31:30.680Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"8d45efdc67b5065b826b225c6fae0a4acb4aba598709c43f8feaca22fa764775","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"c39cee74-b7f2-41cf-a277-e3b5bb079449","keep":113,"tail":["cb8884cb903d960bf1af57b7e70f4f9fd26a526ff7fa362c25661282750b482a","7ae202ac32d5fd2cea88408a7a330e450581b86381783e81983c771aadf80e56","8d5417819870814c986d7076932ad2dcad28287bdd05a674772b4c6ce5fb42e5"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",115,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"203b83782d269db485254a2f3ccc6909b22d8713e6b35f6fda5479fcd757a8bb"}
{"parentUuid":"1e61613f-50f1-4d4a-a3b3-31e1a27d1922","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgeRNkcCrQhXZnBgGFfNe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I stopped before changing anything, because a blind write in `_keep_sync` on its own deletes no lines. Your expectation of far more deleted than added only holds if branch-keeping goes too, and that decision is yours.\n\n**Why it doesn't shrink:** `_keep_sync` has only two parsing lines, and storing raw text just edits them. `capture.keep` then has to parse the request itself, because it compares messages to spot when a chat stopped extending the earlier version. That comparison is the branch-keeping: it saves the old version before a retry, an edit or a revert overwrites it.\n\n**The two options** (line counts are from reading the code, not from making the change):\n\n| | Keep branches | Remove branches too |\n|---|---|---|\n| Source lines | About 3 edited, none deleted | About 44 deleted, about 3 edited |\n| Test lines | About 10 added | About 30 deleted, about 10 added or edited |\n| Standard chats kept | Yes | Yes |\n| Parsing when a chat is kept | One `json.loads` in `capture.keep`, on the request only | None |\n| Retried, edited or reverted versions | Saved as branch files | Overwritten and lost |\n\n**What removing branches costs:** the capture design doc (`jusprin-v2-chat-capture-design.md`) gives the reason for keeping them: a discarded attempt \"is useful training signal (it shows what the person rejected)\". It also counts on branches to show reverts and retries, which it lists among the outcomes that make fine-tuning data more useful. I found no message from you asking for branches. They came from that doc's design and aren't among the decisions recorded as yours, so you may never have weighed them. Your stated goal was only that the stored chats be usable for fine-tuning.\n\n**My pick: keep branches.** Once a retried or reverted version is overwritten it can't be recovered, and those are the examples of what people rejected. It misses your expectation on size, but it still removes the bug's cause, since reply events would no longer be parsed at all. A malformed request body can't cause a similar failure, because the gateway already parses the body before it sends the request upstream. That's from my earlier read of the request path, and I didn't re-check it for this answer.\n\n**In both options:**\n- The stored format changes: `request` becomes a text string and `events` a list of strings, so anything reading these records must parse them. I found no code in the gateway that reads them back. Whether capture is on in production is still unverified, so any existing records could differ from new ones.\n- I'd add a test whose fake stream ends in `data: [DONE]`, and update the `test_capture.py` checks that read event fields directly.\n\nNothing gets committed or deployed unless you ask."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":447,"cache_read_input_tokens":229478,"output_tokens":879,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":447,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":879,"cache_read_input_tokens":229478,"cache_creation_input_tokens":447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":447},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgeRNkH7aXfA7nRLTyXGq","requestRef":"feb78ef2-a2f6-48fa-9617-6308c0d6efb1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"1b52b407-6ff3-4ca4-ae