{"parentUuid":"f321bee4-9fdc-4332-9454-a457e3f897d3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c0272bdf-178f-4df7-9a79-10287f7ef82d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AeNUXrHXg7ahDAV53jjgN5","type":"tool_result","content":"<system-reminder>This memory is 3 days old. Memories are point-in-time observations, not live state — claims about code behavior or file:line citations may be outdated. Verify against current code before asserting as fact.</system-reminder>\n1\t---\n2\tname: jusprin-chat-capture-design\n3\tdescription: \"2026-10-29 server-side chat capture for future fine-tuning — design draft 2 (untracked in tsd-enterprise root), Kenneth's decisions, open questions\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: da2359ba-b0d6-437d-947e-825dd8c3efed\n8\t  modified: 2026-10-29T19:16:01.744Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tDesign doc: `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise/jusprin-v2-chat-capture-design.md` (untracked, draft 2).\n12\t\n13\t**Built 2026-10-29; cherry-picked the same day to local tsd-enterprise master (906752ee3e after squashing, on unpushed a22082b0cb) and local jusprin-newui (30ae01eae0, one commit: chat_key plumbing copied byte-for-byte from a08d17471f without prompt_cache_key, plus the header). Nothing pushed or deployed.** Originally (branches and worktrees deleted 2026-10-29 after squashing): gateway on tsd-enterprise `claude/jusprin-chat-capture` (6d10075718, worktree `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/chat-capture`, tests via docker compose project `chat-capture` with a ports-reset override; obico-server submodule must be at eb0f29c3 there). App header on JusPrin `claude/chat-uid-header` (on `claude/chat-history-cache`). Chat id = sha256(`<projectId>/<conversationId>`)[:32], not a stored chatUid. Trimming removal and the context-limit rule belong to the chat-history-cache programme (R3a done, R3b pending), not to this work.\n14\t\n15\tKenneth's decisions (2026-10-29):\n16\t- **Chat id:** the app sends its own random `chatUid` in an `X-JusPrin-Chat` header. The turn id (`<project>-<conversation>-<message>-attempt-n`) can't be split reliably, because conversation ids are `c-1` and restart per project.\n17\t- **No trimming:** the app removes history trimming, so the newest request of a chat is the whole chat.\n18\t- **Buffered saves:** keep the newest request plus its reply per chat in Redis, and have a Celery beat task write it to GCS once the chat is quiet. Kenneth called saving every request \"pretty dumb\".\n19\t- **Consent:** opt-out was decided, then removed the same day (folded into 906752ee3e): keep every chat; sharing for a reward is arranged case by case. No account field or toggle. Account deletion still deletes kept chats.\n20\t- **Retention:** kept until the person opts out or deletes their account; no age limit.\n21\t\n22\t**Why:** Kenneth wants the stored chats usable as fine-tuning data later.\n23\t\n24\t**How to apply:**\n25\t- Still open: a legal read on the vendor terms. Anthropic's and OpenAI's terms forbid training competing models on their output.\n26\t- The privacy policy (last updated 2022-04-05) has to be updated and people notified before capture starts.\n27\t- Related: [[jusprin-cloud-provider]].\n28\t"}]},"uuid":"d8d1dfce-c9f2-4e46-94e1-fc52524169fe","timestamp":"2026-11-02T16:35:42.359Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/jusprin-chat-capture-design.md","content":"---\nname: jusprin-chat-capture-design\ndescription: \"2026-10-29 server-side chat capture for future fine-tuning — design draft 2 (untracked in tsd-enterprise root), Kenneth's decisions, open questions\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: da2359ba-b0d6-437d-947e-825dd8c3efed\n  modified: 2026-10-29T19:16:01.744Z\n---\n\nDesign doc: `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise/jusprin-v2-chat-capture-design.md` (untracked, draft 2).\n\n**Built 2026-10-29; cherry-picked the same day to local tsd-enterprise master (906752ee3e after squashing, on unpushed a22082b0cb) and local jusprin-newui (30ae01eae0, one commit: chat_key plumbing copied byte-for-byte from a08d17471f without prompt_cache_key, plus the header). Nothing pushed or deployed.** Originally (branches and worktrees deleted 2026-10-29 after squashing): gateway on tsd-enterprise `claude/jusprin-chat-capture` (6d10075718, worktree `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/chat-capture`, tests via docker compose project `chat-capture` with a ports-reset override; obico-server submodule must be at eb0f29c3 there). App header on JusPrin `claude/chat-uid-header` (on `claude/chat-history-cache`). Chat id = sha256(`<projectId>/<conversationId>`)[:32], not a stored chatUid. Trimming removal and the context-limit rule belong to the chat-history-cache programme (R3a done, R3b pending), not to this work.\n\nKenneth's decisions (2026-10-29):\n- **Chat id:** the app sends its own random `chatUid` in an `X-JusPrin-Chat` header. The turn id (`<project>-<conversation>-<message>-attempt-n`) can't be split reliably, because conversation ids are `c-1` and restart per project.\n- **No trimming:** the app removes history trimming, so the newest request of a chat is the whole chat.\n- **Buffered saves:** keep the newest request plus its reply per chat in Redis, and have a Celery beat task write it to GCS once the chat is quiet. Kenneth called saving every request \"pretty dumb\".\n- **Consent:** opt-out was decided, then removed the same day (folded into 906752ee3e): keep every chat; sharing for a reward is arranged case by case. No account field or toggle. Account deletion still deletes kept chats.\n- **Retention:** kept until the person opts out or deletes their account; no age limit.\n\n**Why:** Kenneth wants the stored chats usable as fine-tuning data later.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Still open: a legal read on the vendor terms. Anthropic's and OpenAI's terms forbid training competing models on their output.\n- The privacy policy (last updated 2022-04-05) has to be updated and people notified before capture starts.\n- Related: [[jusprin-cloud-provider]].\n","numLines":28,"startLine":1,"totalLines":28}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f321bee4-9fdc-4332-9454-a457e3f897d3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise/.claude/worktrees/credits-ledger","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
