{"parentUuid":"516d40bd-4b76-46d7-b534-9cf17fb4ad22","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgeRhJvfJXuMjbyWECeCn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fp6KNd9npEdotMf1dBi9MT","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/jusprin-chat-capture-design.md","old_string":"- **Retention:** kept until the person opts out or deletes their account; no age limit.\n","new_string":"- **Retention:** kept until the person deletes their account; no age limit.\n- **Blind write, no branches (2026-11-02):** `_keep_sync` stores the request and reply events as raw text, and a retry, edit or revert overwrites the earlier version. Kenneth chose this over keeping branch files, knowing rejected attempts are lost. `[json.loads(data) for data in self.events]` had thrown on OpenRouter's `data: [DONE]`, losing every Standard chat. Uncommitted in the tsd-enterprise `credits-ledger` worktree until committed. The design doc's Branches section is out of date.\n\nState on 2026-11-02: 906752ee3e is on origin/master and origin/release. No deployment's `env` on the clusters names `JUSPRIN_V2_CAPTURE_CONTAINER`, and neither does the ops repo, so capture looks off; a value from a secret via `envFrom` was not checked.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3277,"cache_read_input_tokens":244635,"output_tokens":2206,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":481},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3277,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2206,"cache_read_input_tokens":244635,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3277,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3277},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Fp6KNd9npEdotMf1dBi9MT":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/jusprin-chat-capture-design.md","old_string":"- **Retention:** kept until the person opts out or deletes their account; no age limit.\n","new_string":"- **Retention:** kept until the person deletes their account; no age limit.\n- **Blind write, no branches (2026-11-02):** `_keep_sync` stores the request and reply events as raw text, and a retry, edit or revert overwrites the earlier version. Kenneth chose this over keeping branch files, knowing rejected attempts are lost. `[json.loads(data) for data in self.events]` had thrown on OpenRouter's `data: [DONE]`, losing every Standard chat. Uncommitted in the tsd-enterprise `credits-ledger` worktree until committed. The design doc's Branches section is out of date.\n\nState on 2026-11-02: 906752ee3e is on origin/master and origin/release. No deployment's `env` on the clusters names `JUSPRIN_V2_CAPTURE_CONTAINER`, and neither does the ops repo, so capture looks off; a value from a secret via `envFrom` was not checked.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgeRhJeHYBGZjcJP1YqyT","requestRef":"e17e4ef1-901d-4714-8c71-0c4af8005e45","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"bcb01444-a298-469d-9b62-f1b3cd8beb62","timestamp":"2026-11-02T16:35:53.043Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise/.claude/worktrees/credits-ledger","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
{"parentUuid":"bcb01444-a298-469d-9b62-f1b3cd8beb62","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c0272bdf-178f-4df7-9a79-10287f7ef82d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fp6KNd9npEdotMf1dBi9MT","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/jusprin-chat-capture-design.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"71b02ac5-8d4f-4586-8473-d53baf295059","timestamp":"2026-11-02T16:35:53.098Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/jusprin-chat-capture-design.md","oldString":"- **Retention:** kept until the person opts out or deletes their account; no age limit.\n","newString":"- **Retention:** kept until the person deletes their account; no age limit.\n- **Blind write, no branches (2026-11-02):** `_keep_sync` stores the request and reply events as raw text, and a retry, edit or revert overwrites the earlier version. Kenneth chose this over keeping branch files, knowing rejected attempts are lost. `[json.loads(data) for data in self.events]` had thrown on OpenRouter's `data: [DONE]`, losing every Standard chat. Uncommitted in the tsd-enterprise `credits-ledger` worktree until committed. The design doc's Branches section is out of date.\n\nState on 2026-11-02: 906752ee3e is on origin/master and origin/release. No deployment's `env` on the clusters names `JUSPRIN_V2_CAPTURE_CONTAINER`, and neither does the ops repo, so capture looks off; a value from a secret via `envFrom` was not checked.\n","originalFile":"---\nname: jusprin-chat-capture-design\ndescription: \"2026-10-29 server-side chat capture for future fine-tuning — design draft 2 (untracked in tsd-enterprise root), Kenneth's decisions, open questions\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: da2359ba-b0d6-437d-947e-825dd8c3efed\n  modified: 2026-10-29T19:16:01.744Z\n---\n\nDesign doc: `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise/jusprin-v2-chat-capture-design.md` (untracked, draft 2).\n\n**Built 2026-10-29; cherry-picked the same day to local tsd-enterprise master (906752ee3e after squashing, on unpushed a22082b0cb) and local jusprin-newui (30ae01eae0, one commit: chat_key plumbing copied byte-for-byte from a08d17471f without prompt_cache_key, plus the header). Nothing pushed or deployed.** Originally (branches and worktrees deleted 2026-10-29 after squashing): gateway on tsd-enterprise `claude/jusprin-chat-capture` (6d10075718, worktree `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/chat-capture`, tests via docker compose project `chat-capture` with a ports-reset override; obico-server submodule must be at eb0f29c3 there). App header on JusPrin `claude/chat-uid-header` (on `claude/chat-history-cache`). Chat id = sha256(`<projectId>/<conversationId>`)[:32], not a stored chatUid. Trimming removal and the context-limit rule belong to the chat-history-cache programme (R3a done, R3b pending), not to this work.\n\nKenneth's decisions (2026-10-29):\n- **Chat id:** the app sends its own random `chatUid` in an `X-JusPrin-Chat` header. The turn id (`<project>-<conversation>-<message>-attempt-n`) can't be split reliably, because conversation ids are `c-1` and restart per project.\n- **No trimming:** the app removes history trimming, so the newest request of a chat is the whole chat.\n- **Buffered saves:** keep the newest request plus its reply per chat in Redis, and have a Celery beat task write it to GCS once the chat is quiet. Kenneth called saving every request \"pretty dumb\".\n- **Consent:** opt-out was decided, then removed the same day (folded into 906752ee3e): keep every chat; sharing for a reward is arranged case by case. No account field or toggle. Account deletion still deletes kept chats.\n- **Retention:** kept until the person opts out or deletes their account; no age limit.\n\n**Why:** Kenneth wants the stored chats usable as fine-tuning data later.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Still open: a legal read on the vendor terms. Anthropic's and OpenAI's terms forbid training competing models on their output.\n- The privacy policy (last updated 2022-04-05) has to be updated and people notified before capture starts.\n- Related: [[jusprin-cloud-provider]].\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":7,"newStart":5,"newLines":7,"lines":["   node_type: memory","   type: project","   originSessionId: da2359ba-b0d6-437d-947e-825dd8c3efed","-  modified: 2026-10-29T19:16:01.744Z","+  modified: 2026-11-02T16:35:53.073Z"," ---"," "," Design doc: `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise/jusprin-v2-chat-capture-design.md` (untracked, draft 2)."]},{"oldStart":17,"oldLines":8,"newStart":17,"newLines":11,"lines":[" - **No trimming:** the app removes history trimming, so the newest request of a chat is the whole chat."," - **Buffered saves:** keep the newest request plus its reply per chat in Redis, and have a Celery beat task write it to GCS once the chat is quiet. Kenneth called saving every request \"pretty dumb\"."," - **Consent:** opt-out was decided, then removed the same day (folded into 906752ee3e): keep every chat; sharing for a reward is arranged case by case. No account field or toggle. Account deletion still deletes kept chats.","-- **Retention:** kept until the person opts out or deletes their account; no age limit.","+- **Retention:** kept until the person deletes their account; no age limit.","+- **Blind write, no branches (2026-11-02):** `_keep_sync` stores the request and reply events as raw text, and a retry, edit or revert overwrites the earlier version. Kenneth chose this over keeping branch files, knowing rejected attempts are lost. `[json.loads(data) for data in self.events]` had thrown on OpenRouter's `data: [DONE]`, losing every Standard chat. Uncommitted in the tsd-enterprise `credits-ledger` worktree until committed. The design doc's Branches section is out of date."," ","+State on 2026-11-02: 906752ee3e is on origin/master and origin/release. No deployment's `env` on the clusters names `JUSPRIN_V2_CAPTURE_CONTAINER`, and neither does the ops repo, so capture looks off; a value from a secret via `envFrom` was not checked.","+"," **Why:** Kenneth wants the stored chats usable as fine-tuning data later."," "," **How to apply:**"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bcb01444-a298-469d-9b62-f1b3cd8beb62","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise/.claude/worktrees/credits-ledger","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
