{"parentUuid":"1dd394fb-2e5f-4ae8-aa07-5d1c651c66aa","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"984766b3-abee-4a37-b61b-7bdc0139a255","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PHKH1bQpFUtdmG3Vw1FNTn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Credits and onboarding: everything the short report could not hold\n2\t\n3\tWritten 2026-11-02 by the side session that built steps 0, 1, 2, 4 and 5 of `pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md`. Nothing is committed.\n4\t\n5\t- App: `~/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding`, branch `claude/credits-onboarding`, base `de366d3618`.\n6\t- Gateway: `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise/.claude/worktrees/credits-ledger`, branch `claude/credits-ledger`.\n7\t- Deploy config: `~/Projects/ops/.claude/worktrees/credits-gateway-config`, branch `claude/credits-gateway-config`.\n8\t\n9\t## Before deploying the gateway\n10\t\n11\t1. The Kubernetes secret `JUSPRIN_OPENROUTER_API_KEY` must exist on `jusprin-v2-gateway-{stg,prod}` before the ops change is applied, or the pods will not start.\n12\t2. The gateway fails at startup without the new alias keys in the ops change, so the two must go together.\n13\t3. `GET /account` already reports `v1_subscription`. The app no longer shows it: `V1_PRICE_CARRIES_OVER = false` in `AgentUI/src/components/WelcomeBack.tsx` hides board 1d's kept-price box and board 1c's \"Subscribed to JusPrin v1?\" note until step 3 ships. Step 3 must turn the flag on. Gateway deploy is no longer blocked by this.\n14\t\n15\t## Bugs found by running the real app\n16\t\n17\tAll three came in with the onboarding branch `8f4588beae`; its tests use a fake backend and could not see them.\n18\t\n19\t1. Fixed. `save_onboarding` passed `const char*` to `AppConfig::set`, which resolves to the `bool` overload, so every field including `status` was saved as `true`. After the first press, the person saw \"Some settings need attention, Not imported, 0 items\". Reproduced in the real app, fixed in `OrcaHomeBackend.cpp`, guarded by harness check `onboarding_saves_each_value`. That check was not separately run against the broken code.\n20\t2. Fixed. Retrying failed presets when nothing more imports cleared the partial screen and jumped to Printer setup with \"could not be imported\", though one preset had imported. It now stays on the partial screen and says \"These profiles still could not be imported.\" Tested only by the real-app run, because no automated test reaches this code.\n21\t3. Fixed. On a truly fresh install, \"I don't have a printer here\" refused with \"No local printer profile is installed\", because no vendor is installed yet. It now installs the bundled \"Generic Klipper Printer\" 0.4, whose preset is \"MyKlipper 0.4 nozzle\". The example's 3MF does NOT carry printer or process settings: it holds only `3D/3dmodel.model`, `Metadata/model_settings.config` and `Metadata/slice_info.config`, so nothing in the file can say what to install. Harness mode `--fresh-example` guards it; it was run with the fix removed and fails with the old refusal. In the real app, the example opened with 3 objects and sliced: 3 filaments, 202 g, 7 h 8 min. The model uses filament slots 1 to 3 on a printer with one extruder, so a person who sends it to a real single-toolhead printer would get tool changes. The example step says no physical printer is required.\n22\t\n23\t## Found by the live local chats, 2026-11-02\n24\t\n25\t- Fixed, uncommitted in the `credits-ledger` worktree. The gateway logged \"could not keep a chat request\" for every Standard request through OpenRouter, because `_keep_sync` in `web_ent/jusprin/v2/gateway.py` parsed every reply event as JSON and OpenRouter's documented stream ends in `data: [DONE]`. Kenneth chose a blind write: the request and events are stored as raw text, and branch files are gone, so a retry, edit or revert overwrites the earlier version. A test with a stream ending in `[DONE]` failed before the change and passes now; all 122 `jusprin.v2` tests pass. The real OpenRouter stream was not rerun.\n26\t- Fixed, and this replaces item 3's example details above. The example no longer opens the OrcaSliced 3MF, which had three stacked objects, three filaments and a collision warning. It opens `resources/handy_models/3DBenchy.drc`. `resources/profiles` holds no printable model. The printer is now saved under its own name, \"Generic Klipper Printer\", the way normal printer setup does, so the chip shows no warning triangle or \"from the file\". There is no rule specific to onboarding. Real-app result on an empty data folder: one object, one filament, ~44 min, 12 g, $0.23, no print issue. Cost: Home shows a printer card \"Generic Klipper Printer, Not connected\".\n27\t- Fixed. Choosing a printer on an empty project wrote change rows, and Home listed any empty project with rows, so a blank \"Untitled\" card appeared beside the opened file. `authored_head` in `Workspace/ProjectAutosave.cpp` no longer lists an empty project whose only history is printer, filament or process choices. A chat on an empty plate stays listed. The empty project's folder stays on disk, hidden. This applies to every path that picks a printer on an empty project, not only the example. Only the example path was run; that other paths left a blank card before is inferred from the code.\n28\t\n29\t## Harness defects fixed to get the checks running\n30\t\n31\tAll in `tests/shell/shell_harness.cpp`. None of these came from this work: `--print-history` crashed on the Mac on the base commit too.\n32\t\n33\t- The Print history step read the title bar menu, which macOS does not have. Null pointer crash. Now skipped on macOS.\n34\t- A page read travels through the page title, which macOS cuts at about 1000 characters. Long reads now travel in pieces.\n35\t- The fake printer compares its control file's time in whole seconds, so a second write within one second was ignored and `print_history_finish_recorded` failed intermittently. Each write now gets a newer time. The cause comes from reading the code, and the failure did not recur in the runs after the change.\n36\t\n37\t## Choices I made where the plan left room\n38\t\n39\t- Cross-format chats use per-item `output_format` and deterministic conversion for account chats. Not checked against live Anthropic or OpenRouter. Cache misses at crossings are not costed.\n40\t- Returning users do not get the Home welcome. A person with an agent already configured skips it. `open_onboarding_example` kept.\n41\t- `project_attachment_read` left out for Standard. Pickers greyed for own-key chats too.\n42\t- Pricing URL is a placeholder (decision 10). \"See usage\" opens Preferences › Account, which shows no usage until step 3.\n43\t- The ring measures against the sum of what each lot was granted (decision 13).\n44\t- Low notice: threshold 5 messages, once per session past it.\n45\t- A polling turn stopped by the guard ends as Complete, not Stopped.\n46\t- Clawback leaves free Standard messages alone. Daily report cap is a rolling 24 hours. Photo caps 6 and 20 MB are my fill-in.\n47\t- `activity` rows give `chat_id`, not a title. No refund on upstream failure.\n48\t- Report button and Home line appear only when signed in to the account. `25` is hard-coded in the page because the gateway cannot tell Home before sending. The form takes one photo though the gateway allows six.\n49\t- Fill-in words: \"Choose a photo…\", \"N of 200 characters\", the failure sentence, the no-reward sentences, \"Done\", \"Sending…\". \"The form says so only when reached\" is an after-send message with 0 credits.\n50\t- HEIC not accepted. The thumbnail ignores EXIF rotation. The Agent ring updates on next focus or turn after a reward, not at once.\n51\t\n52\t## Not built\n53\t\n54\t- New-chat default after the first month and \"50 free Standard messages this month\" (board 6a, decision 1).\n55\t- The 7-day expiry notice.\n56\t- \"Also have OrcaSlicer settings? Import from OrcaSlicer\" row and header/footer chrome on boards 1c and 1d.\n57\t- The webview opening Account and pricing pages, Chargebee, v1 carry-over (step 3, as instructed).\n58\t- Setup diff with consent. Langfuse (plan section 10).\n59\t- Tokens `credits`, `modelMenu`, `tooltip.maxWidth`, `printReport` are not yet in the Claude design-system artifact.\n60\t\n61\t## Open in the design, built as placeholder\n62\t\n63\tThinking picker on Standard (shown). Two-week report limit and export-only button. Annual-plan lines on 1d other than the headline.\n64\t\n65\t## Where the docs and boards disagree\n66\t\n67\t- Implementation vs board 3c: after a 402 the app refreshes the balance, so the composer's \"You have 0 credits\" note and a second Get more credits appear under the card. Board 3c shows only the card. The board also leaves out the note that its own board 3b would show at 3 credits.\n68\t- `MANIFEST.md` is stale on report placement and still says \"Basic\".\n69\t- Plan 5.2 says 122 Expert, the board and arithmetic say 112.\n70\t- Design doc cites plan 5.3 for the webview; it is 5.4.\n71\t- Plan says the ledger migration is in obico-server; it is in `web_ent`.\n72\t- Board 3e capture vs design doc on New Expert chat: followed the doc.\n73\t- Board 2c caption says \"1 credit\" alone. Board 3d has no ring; 3b is unclear. Stray \"Your text here\" on board 1a.\n74\t- \"Resets 30 Nov\" in the panel vs board \"1 Dec\": the date is midnight UTC shown in local time.\n75\t\n76\t## Not verified\n77\t\n78\t- Screen control of the app was denied, so these were never exercised: pointer hover on the ring and pickers, the native file dialogs (the report's photo came through a test seam), the manual setup wizard, closing Preferences.\n79\t- Board 1d's box is hidden. The Welcome Back window was checked in the real app with a fake gateway reporting a v1 subscription: the subscription reached the page and no price showed. Its shown wording stays Vitest only.\n80\t- Board 3e, the picture row in a Standard chat, in the real app: Vitest only, because attaching needs the native dialog.\n81\t- \"Get more credits\" was never pressed in the real app, so as not to open a browser. Sign-in itself was not completed; the account was seeded in the conf.\n82\t- Real slice polling guard and 1-hour cache ttl against a live provider. The three approved chats ran on the local gateway with real models on 2026-11-02 instead of staging, at Kenneth's request; screenshots are in `live-check-2026-11-02/` in the app worktree.\n83\t- Windows and Linux: nothing run.\n84\t- Dark mode in the real app.\n85\t\n86\t## Leftovers I did not remove\n87\t\n88\tAn earlier scratch deletion was refused by a safety check, so these remain:\n89\t\n90\t- Harness data directories under `/var/folders/6y/fn1z996148dc7xjy2mxx5wkc0000gp/T/`: `jusprin-shell-13cd-48dc-0a4a`, `jusprin-shell-17b6-79ea-21aa`, `jusprin-shell-6ba6-b587-78a8`.\n91\t- This session's scratchpad, which holds runs, the scratch app copy and a local-only test token.\n92\t- A `caffeinate` of up to 30 minutes from 05:27, which ends by itself.\n93\t"}]},"uuid":"7aeafaea-8107-463c-92b4-da8caee8f1cd","timestamp":"2026-11-02T16:40:10.778Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md","content":"# Credits and onboarding: everything the short report could not hold\n\nWritten 2026-11-02 by the side session that built steps 0, 1, 2, 4 and 5 of `pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md`. Nothing is committed.\n\n- App: `~/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding`, branch `claude/credits-onboarding`, base `de366d3618`.\n- Gateway: `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise/.claude/worktrees/credits-ledger`, branch `claude/credits-ledger`.\n- Deploy config: `~/Projects/ops/.claude/worktrees/credits-gateway-config`, branch `claude/credits-gateway-config`.\n\n## Before deploying the gateway\n\n1. The Kubernetes secret `JUSPRIN_OPENROUTER_API_KEY` must exist on `jusprin-v2-gateway-{stg,prod}` before the ops change is applied, or the pods will not start.\n2. The gateway fails at startup without the new alias keys in the ops change, so the two must go together.\n3. `GET /account` already reports `v1_subscription`. The app no longer shows it: `V1_PRICE_CARRIES_OVER = false` in `AgentUI/src/components/WelcomeBack.tsx` hides board 1d's kept-price box and board 1c's \"Subscribed to JusPrin v1?\" note until step 3 ships. Step 3 must turn the flag on. Gateway deploy is no longer blocked by this.\n\n## Bugs found by running the real app\n\nAll three came in with the onboarding branch `8f4588beae`; its tests use a fake backend and could not see them.\n\n1. Fixed. `save_onboarding` passed `const char*` to `AppConfig::set`, which resolves to the `bool` overload, so every field including `status` was saved as `true`. After the first press, the person saw \"Some settings need attention, Not imported, 0 items\". Reproduced in the real app, fixed in `OrcaHomeBackend.cpp`, guarded by harness check `onboarding_saves_each_value`. That check was not separately run against the broken code.\n2. Fixed. Retrying failed presets when nothing more imports cleared the partial screen and jumped to Printer setup with \"could not be imported\", though one preset had imported. It now stays on the partial screen and says \"These profiles still could not be imported.\" Tested only by the real-app run, because no automated test reaches this code.\n3. Fixed. On a truly fresh install, \"I don't have a printer here\" refused with \"No local printer profile is installed\", because no vendor is installed yet. It now installs the bundled \"Generic Klipper Printer\" 0.4, whose preset is \"MyKlipper 0.4 nozzle\". The example's 3MF does NOT carry printer or process settings: it holds only `3D/3dmodel.model`, `Metadata/model_settings.config` and `Metadata/slice_info.config`, so nothing in the file can say what to install. Harness mode `--fresh-example` guards it; it was run with the fix removed and fails with the old refusal. In the real app, the example opened with 3 objects and sliced: 3 filaments, 202 g, 7 h 8 min. The model uses filament slots 1 to 3 on a printer with one extruder, so a person who sends it to a real single-toolhead printer would get tool changes. The example step says no physical printer is required.\n\n## Found by the live local chats, 2026-11-02\n\n- Fixed, uncommitted in the `credits-ledger` worktree. The gateway logged \"could not keep a chat request\" for every Standard request through OpenRouter, because `_keep_sync` in `web_ent/jusprin/v2/gateway.py` parsed every reply event as JSON and OpenRouter's documented stream ends in `data: [DONE]`. Kenneth chose a blind write: the request and events are stored as raw text, and branch files are gone, so a retry, edit or revert overwrites the earlier version. A test with a stream ending in `[DONE]` failed before the change and passes now; all 122 `jusprin.v2` tests pass. The real OpenRouter stream was not rerun.\n- Fixed, and this replaces item 3's example details above. The example no longer opens the OrcaSliced 3MF, which had three stacked objects, three filaments and a collision warning. It opens `resources/handy_models/3DBenchy.drc`. `resources/profiles` holds no printable model. The printer is now saved under its own name, \"Generic Klipper Printer\", the way normal printer setup does, so the chip shows no warning triangle or \"from the file\". There is no rule specific to onboarding. Real-app result on an empty data folder: one object, one filament, ~44 min, 12 g, $0.23, no print issue. Cost: Home shows a printer card \"Generic Klipper Printer, Not connected\".\n- Fixed. Choosing a printer on an empty project wrote change rows, and Home listed any empty project with rows, so a blank \"Untitled\" card appeared beside the opened file. `authored_head` in `Workspace/ProjectAutosave.cpp` no longer lists an empty project whose only history is printer, filament or process choices. A chat on an empty plate stays listed. The empty project's folder stays on disk, hidden. This applies to every path that picks a printer on an empty project, not only the example. Only the example path was run; that other paths left a blank card before is inferred from the code.\n\n## Harness defects fixed to get the checks running\n\nAll in `tests/shell/shell_harness.cpp`. None of these came from this work: `--print-history` crashed on the Mac on the base commit too.\n\n- The Print history step read the title bar menu, which macOS does not have. Null pointer crash. Now skipped on macOS.\n- A page read travels through the page title, which macOS cuts at about 1000 characters. Long reads now travel in pieces.\n- The fake printer compares its control file's time in whole seconds, so a second write within one second was ignored and `print_history_finish_recorded` failed intermittently. Each write now gets a newer time. The cause comes from reading the code, and the failure did not recur in the runs after the change.\n\n## Choices I made where the plan left room\n\n- Cross-format chats use per-item `output_format` and deterministic conversion for account chats. Not checked against live Anthropic or OpenRouter. Cache misses at crossings are not costed.\n- Returning users do not get the Home welcome. A person with an agent already configured skips it. `open_onboarding_example` kept.\n- `project_attachment_read` left out for Standard. Pickers greyed for own-key chats too.\n- Pricing URL is a placeholder (decision 10). \"See usage\" opens Preferences › Account, which shows no usage until step 3.\n- The ring measures against the sum of what each lot was granted (decision 13).\n- Low notice: threshold 5 messages, once per session past it.\n- A polling turn stopped by the guard ends as Complete, not Stopped.\n- Clawback leaves free Standard messages alone. Daily report cap is a rolling 24 hours. Photo caps 6 and 20 MB are my fill-in.\n- `activity` rows give `chat_id`, not a title. No refund on upstream failure.\n- Report button and Home line appear only when signed in to the account. `25` is hard-coded in the page because the gateway cannot tell Home before sending. The form takes one photo though the gateway allows six.\n- Fill-in words: \"Choose a photo…\", \"N of 200 characters\", the failure sentence, the no-reward sentences, \"Done\", \"Sending…\". \"The form says so only when reached\" is an after-send message with 0 credits.\n- HEIC not accepted. The thumbnail ignores EXIF rotation. The Agent ring updates on next focus or turn after a reward, not at once.\n\n## Not built\n\n- New-chat default after the first month and \"50 free Standard messages this month\" (board 6a, decision 1).\n- The 7-day expiry notice.\n- \"Also have OrcaSlicer settings? Import from OrcaSlicer\" row and header/footer chrome on boards 1c and 1d.\n- The webview opening Account and pricing pages, Chargebee, v1 carry-over (step 3, as instructed).\n- Setup diff with consent. Langfuse (plan section 10).\n- Tokens `credits`, `modelMenu`, `tooltip.maxWidth`, `printReport` are not yet in the Claude design-system artifact.\n\n## Open in the design, built as placeholder\n\nThinking picker on Standard (shown). Two-week report limit and export-only button. Annual-plan lines on 1d other than the headline.\n\n## Where the docs and boards disagree\n\n- Implementation vs board 3c: after a 402 the app refreshes the balance, so the composer's \"You have 0 credits\" note and a second Get more credits appear under the card. Board 3c shows only the card. The board also leaves out the note that its own board 3b would show at 3 credits.\n- `MANIFEST.md` is stale on report placement and still says \"Basic\".\n- Plan 5.2 says 122 Expert, the board and arithmetic say 112.\n- Design doc cites plan 5.3 for the webview; it is 5.4.\n- Plan says the ledger migration is in obico-server; it is in `web_ent`.\n- Board 3e capture vs design doc on New Expert chat: followed the doc.\n- Board 2c caption says \"1 credit\" alone. Board 3d has no ring; 3b is unclear. Stray \"Your text here\" on board 1a.\n- \"Resets 30 Nov\" in the panel vs board \"1 Dec\": the date is midnight UTC shown in local time.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- Screen control of the app was denied, so these were never exercised: pointer hover on the ring and pickers, the native file dialogs (the report's photo came through a test seam), the manual setup wizard, closing Preferences.\n- Board 1d's box is hidden. The Welcome Back window was checked in the real app with a fake gateway reporting a v1 subscription: the subscription reached the page and no price showed. Its shown wording stays Vitest only.\n- Board 3e, the picture row in a Standard chat, in the real app: Vitest only, because attaching needs the native dialog.\n- \"Get more credits\" was never pressed in the real app, so as not to open a browser. Sign-in itself was not completed; the account was seeded in the conf.\n- Real slice polling guard and 1-hour cache ttl against a live provider. The three approved chats ran on the local gateway with real models on 2026-11-02 instead of staging, at Kenneth's request; screenshots are in `live-check-2026-11-02/` in the app worktree.\n- Windows and Linux: nothing run.\n- Dark mode in the real app.\n\n## Leftovers I did not remove\n\nAn earlier scratch deletion was refused by a safety check, so these remain:\n\n- Harness data directories under `/var/folders/6y/fn1z996148dc7xjy2mxx5wkc0000gp/T/`: `jusprin-shell-13cd-48dc-0a4a`, `jusprin-shell-17b6-79ea-21aa`, `jusprin-shell-6ba6-b587-78a8`.\n- This session's scratchpad, which holds runs, the scratch app copy and a local-only test token.\n- A `caffeinate` of up to 30 minutes from 05:27, which ends by itself.\n","numLines":93,"startLine":1,"totalLines":93}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1dd394fb-2e5f-4ae8-aa07-5d1c651c66aa","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/ops/.claude/worktrees/credits-gateway-config","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
