{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","hash":"95befd78466204ef2304295badc5a23a1b1dcb7c932319bde285d5cf45be9500","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015QtdZqszCenvavQMaV9ZM4","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md","offset":264,"limit":14},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KLWweaWLDgbLhKmUpoEscc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding; git log -12 --format='%h %s' 8f4588beae 2>/dev/null | head -2 | cut -c1-100; git diff --stat -- src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ProviderAgent.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AnthropicCodec.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ToolExecutionCoordinator.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp | cut -c1-90; git diff -- src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AnthropicCodec.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ToolExecutionCoordinator.hpp | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-120 | head -24; wc -l src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/RecordConversion.hpp; sed -n 1,14p src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/RecordConversion.hpp | cut -c1-110; git log --format='%an' -1; git -C /Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise/.claude/worktrees/credits-ledger config user.name; ls .git 2>/dev/null | head -1; git diff --name-only | grep -vE '^(src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/|tests/|resources/jusprin/)' | head","description":"Gather facts for the app commit message","timeout":20000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","hash":"5f536ed3563b5f301dfab7efa158e2522b5d035d7dbdf009d597e77093ebd108","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015QtdZqszCenvavQMaV9ZM4","type":"tool_result","content":"264\t## 11. Order of work and tests\n265\t\n266\t0. **Port the onboarding branch onto `jusprin-newui`** (app only; no dependency on the ledger). The branch `onboarding-frontend-only` (one commit, `8f4588beae`, 2026-10-06, same on `origin`) adds the first-run path to Home: welcome, import presets from an OrcaSlicer install, confirm or choose a printer, open a project or the bundled example. It was built on `4389492239` and is 139 commits behind; a dry-run `git rebase jusprin-newui` on 2026-11-02 stopped with conflicts in 18 of its 27 files (`HomeBackend.hpp`, `HomeHost.cpp/.hpp`, `HomeSnapshot.hpp`, `OrcaHomeBackend.cpp/.hpp`, `home/protocol.json`, `App.tsx`, `App.test.tsx`, `bridge/protocol.ts` and its test, `store.ts`, `styles.css`, `styles.test.ts`, `tokens.ts`, `sources.cmake`, `test_home_host.cpp`, `test_home_snapshot.cpp`). The Home side changed under it: the Home v3 page (`dbec3e3a38`), Print history (`ebbb2f8894`), JusPrin's own Preferences window (`641c17f13e`), every opened file becomes a new project (`d921c4b3dd`), and the token sync (`7671e48504`). Rebase the one commit, resolve by keeping both sides' additions, then bring the screens to the current design: the canvas's \"On boarding experience\" page is the source of truth (Figma is retired), boards 1a to 1d put the first-month offer on the setup row, the welcome screen and the welcome-back window, and the branch's \"Set up JusPrin\" and \"Set up with Agent\" links to jusprin.com/account become the one setup flow in Preferences › Agent (decided 2026-10-23). Tests the branch carried (Home page Vitest, `test_home_host`, `test_home_snapshot`, `test_onboarding_model`, `test_brand_tokens`) must pass again; its two unverified paths (a partial preset import, staying on Home when the bundled example fails to open) still need to be shown in the real app.\n267\t1. **Ledger and charging** (gateway + obico-server migration): tables, `charge_turn`, draw order, lazy trickle, sign-up lot, `credits_exhausted` 402 body, `tier`/`credits`/`images` in aliases, `slicer-basic` alias with image stripping, `/account`. Tests in `web_ent/jusprin/v2/tests/`: draw order (expiring first, basic-only skipped for expert, never-expiring last), idempotent charge on a retried first request, two concurrent first requests of different turns against one lot (`select_for_update`), expiry at the boundary, free app turns and their daily cap, the 402 body, image stripping only for `images: false`, and a `/models` response carrying prices. Gateway test harness pattern: `test_gateway.py` with the MockTransport injection the file already uses.\n268\t2. **App:** `X-JusPrin-Request: note`, `credits` in `ModelOptionInfo` and the pickers with \"a message\", pickers greyed once a chat has a message from the person with the tooltip, app-started turns on the Expert alias without storing the chat's model, the attachment row's picture notice and \"New Expert chat\" button, picture tools left out of a Standard chat's tool list, the `/account` fetch, the ring and hover panel, the pre-send check with \"Get more credits\" and the conditional \"New Standard chat\", the failed card, the webview that opens the served Account and pricing page (5.4). Vitest for the page (`ModelPickers.test.tsx`, a new `BalancePanel.test.tsx`, a composer test for the disabled Send and its line), Catch2 for `ProviderAgent`'s header and 402 handling, a Catch2 test that an app-started turn in a fresh chat leaves `chat_model` unset and the next person's message sets it, a Vitest for the attachment row in a Standard chat, one live end-to-end run through the shell harness against staging (`app-stg.obico.io` runs the same image) at a stated spend.\n269\t3. **Chargebee and the served pages:** plans, add-ons, coupon, checkout views, webhook branches, the Account and pricing page with the `webview_session` login (5.4), v1-subscriber carry-over. Tests with recorded webhook payloads, including a repeated `subscription_renewed` (no double lot), a cancellation mid-term (lot keeps its expiry), an `invoice_generated` for the pack, and the Obico-cancel coupon removal. Staging run with Chargebee's test site before production.\n270\t4. **Cost prerequisites:** 1-hour ttl in `prepare()` (test: the body sent upstream carries `ttl` on every `cache_control`; live check of cache write counts across a 10-minute pause), then the polling guard (host test: third refused poll ends the turn; the slice-finished note turn still runs).\n271\t5. **Rewards:** endpoint, storage, admin, the Print history button and form, the Home card line. Tests: duplicate hash rejected, text too short rejected, daily cap, invalid review claws back once and shows its reason in `activity`.\n272\t6. **Alert and auto-reload and launch bonus:** suggestion maths with unit tests on the four cases (Pay as you go cheaper, Hobby cheaper, Workshop cheaper, Obico discount flips the answer); auto-reload task with a failed payment path; `JUSPRIN_LAUNCH_DOUBLE_UNTIL`.\n273\t\n274\t**Ready to hand off (assessed 2026-11-02):** steps 0, 1, 2 (except the Account and pricing webview), 4 and 5 are specified to the level a coding agent can build and test from this document plus the design doc and the boards. Step 3 waits on decision 12 (webview or in-app pages), decision 10 (the domain the app opens) and the open parts of decision 8 (when v1 subscribers move and how to word it); the webview part of step 2 waits with it. Decisions 1, 2, 4 to 7 and 13 to 16 have a recommended or placeholder answer written here and do not block the build. The handoff brief is `credits-and-onboarding-handoff-2026-11.md`.\n275\t\n276\tSteps 1, 3 and 4 touch `tsd-enterprise` and `ops` (the ConfigMap gains the second alias and the OpenRouter key env; both deployments restart). Step 2 touches the app. Steps 1 and 2 can be built in parallel once the `/account` shape and the 402 body are agreed, which this document is for.\n277\t"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KLWweaWLDgbLhKmUpoEscc","type":"tool_result","content":"8f4588beae Add the local first-run onboarding flow to Home\n4389492239 Bring the Agent UI to the approved Figma state matrices\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AnthropicCodec.cpp    |  10 +-\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ProviderAgent.cpp     |  23 +-\n .../GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ToolExecutionCoordinator.cpp |  21 +\n src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp    | 562 ++++++++++++++++++++-\n 4 files changed, 607 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)\n--- a/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AnthropicCodec.cpp\n+++ b/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AnthropicCodec.cpp\n+#include \"RecordConversion.hpp\"\n-            // The response's own content, thinking included, exactly as it came.\n-            push(messages, \"assistant\", item.output);\n+            // The response's own content, thinking included, exactly as it came;\n+            // a turn another format holds, as this format reads it.\n+            if (json output = assistant_output_as(item.output, item.output_format.empty() ? kFormatAnthropic : item.out\n+                !output.empty())\n+                push(messages, \"assistant\", std::move(output));\n-                json block{{\"type\", \"tool_result\"}, {\"tool_use_id\", result.call_id}};\n+                json block{{\"type\", \"tool_result\"}, {\"tool_use_id\", anthropic_tool_id(result.call_id)}};\n--- a/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ToolExecutionCoordinator.hpp\n+++ b/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ToolExecutionCoordinator.hpp\n+    // Whether two calls' correlation ids belong to one turn of the chat. A turn\n+    // spans several messages, which only the owner of the chat can tell.\n+    void set_same_turn(std::function<bool(const std::string&, const std::string&)> same_turn) { m_same_turn = std::move\n+    // The turn that started the slice now in flight has polled for it this many\n+    // times and been told not to; the owner ends the turn at the limit.\n+    bool slice_poll_limit_reached() const { return m_refused_slice_polls >= 3; }\n+    // A model checking on the slice its own turn started: answered with `busy`,\n+    // since the app starts a new turn with the outcome. An MCP client has no\n+    // such turn, so it polls, and a slice from an earlier turn may be read.\n+    bool refuse_slice_poll(ToolActivity& activity);\n      23 src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/RecordConversion.hpp\n#pragma once\n\n// A chat on a JusPrin account can hold turns in both wire formats: the turns\n// the app starts run on the Expert alias whatever the chat's model is, and the\n// two aliases may be served in different formats. A record item keeps the\n// provider's own output, so a codec reading another format's turn converts it\n// here. The same input always gives the same bytes, so a later request repeats\n// an earlier one's and the provider's cache still hits.\n\n#include <nlohmann/json.hpp>\n\n#include <string>\n\nnamespace Slic3r::GUI::JusPrin::Agent {\nKenneth Jiang\nKenneth Jiang\n.git","is_error":false}]}}
