{"parentUuid":"0e31c6b1-a068-4aec-a081-3113243b909d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgeS56e62i4McuqAs7o3p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5648,"cache_read_input_tokens":272804,"output_tokens":3022,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":55},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5648,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3022,"cache_read_input_tokens":272804,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5648,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5648},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":736,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgeS56Aonh1yXGMy3DCji","requestRef":"c1fbf90e-ffef-4821-90f4-1bfe3e69806c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"652803cf-f5e1-4d24-bc4f-dc6392ee495b","timestamp":"2026-11-02T16:40:39.585Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise/.claude/worktrees/credits-ledger","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
{"parentUuid":"652803cf-f5e1-4d24-bc4f-dc6392ee495b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgeS56e62i4McuqAs7o3p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017q4Adv41ic2qPvjuqrdBpQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c/scratchpad; mkdir -p $S/msg; cat > $S/msg/app.txt <<'EOF'\nAdd JusPrin Cloud credits and the first-run path on Home\n\nThe app now shows and spends JusPrin Cloud credits, and a new install starts\non Home with a first-run path. This is steps 0, 1, 2, 4 and 5 of the credits\nplan on the app side. Step 3 (Chargebee, the served Account and pricing pages,\nv1 carry-over) is not here. It needs the gateway change on tsd-enterprise\nbranch claude/credits-ledger.\n\nOnboarding, ported from 8f4588beae and brought to the current boards:\n- Home walks through the welcome, importing presets from an OrcaSlicer install,\n  choosing a printer, and opening a project or the bundled example.\n- save_onboarding passed const char* to AppConfig::set, which saved every field\n  as \"true\". It now saves each value.\n- \"I don't have a printer here\" refused on a fresh install, because no vendor\n  was installed. It now installs Generic Klipper Printer and saves it under its\n  own name, as normal printer setup does, so the chip shows no warning.\n- The example opens handy_models/3DBenchy.drc. The earlier example file had\n  three stacked objects, three filaments and a collision warning.\n- An empty project is no longer listed on Home when its only history is\n  printer, filament or process choices. A chat on an empty plate stays listed.\n- The welcome-back window's kept-price box is hidden behind\n  V1_PRICE_CARRIES_OVER until step 3 ships.\n\nCredits:\n- Model pickers show each model's price and are greyed once the person has sent\n  a message in the chat. The account's balance shows as a ring with a hover\n  panel, and the composer offers \"Get more credits\" when a message can't be paid\n  for. A 402 from the gateway ends in a failed card.\n- Turns the app starts itself send X-JusPrin-Request: note and run on Expert\n  without changing the chat's model. RecordConversion turns one format's stored\n  turn into the other's, the same bytes each time, so provider caches still hit.\n- A Standard chat leaves out the picture tools and says so on the attachment\n  row, with a \"New Expert chat\" button.\n\nCost and rewards:\n- A turn that polls for its own slice is answered with busy, and the third\n  refused poll ends the turn. The note turn that reports the slice still runs.\n- Print history has a report form with a photo, and Home shows the credit line\n  when signed in to the account.\n\nTests: AgentUI Vitest (651) and HomeUI Vitest (130) with tsc, jusprin_tests\n(151), agent_bridge_tests (506), shell_theme_tests (14), brand_tokens_tests and\nthe shell harness default run (600 checks) and --fresh-example pass on macOS.\nThe real app ran the fresh-install example on an empty data folder, and three\nlive chats ran through a local gateway. Windows and Linux were not run.\ntests/shell/shell_harness.cpp also fixes three harness defects on macOS that\nwere there before this work: a null title bar menu in --print-history, page\nreads cut at about 1000 characters, and fake-printer control writes within one\nsecond being ignored.\nEOF\ncat > $S/msg/gw1.txt <<'EOF'\nCharge JusPrin v2 turns from a credit ledger\n\nThe gateway now admits and charges each turn against a person's credits instead\nof the monthly AI quota. This is the gateway side of steps 1, 4 and 5 of the\ncredits plan. Chargebee and v1 carry-over (step 3) are not here.\n\n- Ledger: new CreditGrant, CreditAllocation and CreditCharge tables in\n  web_ent/jusprin/ledger, with migration 0002. Lots are drawn expiring first,\n  with the sign-up lot and a monthly trickle granted lazily. A retried request\n  of a turn is not charged twice.\n- Aliases gain tier, credits and images. slicer-basic is Standard through a\n  Responses backend; images: false strips pictures from its requests.\n- A turn that can't be paid for gets a 402 credits_exhausted body carrying what\n  the app needs to offer a way on. It replaces quota_exhausted.\n- X-JusPrin-Request: note marks a turn the app started. Note turns are free up\n  to a daily ceiling, and they are kept with the chat.\n- GET /ent/jusprin/v2/account reports balance, lots and activity.\n- POST /ent/jusprin/v2/print_reports stores a report and its photos and rewards\n  it, with duplicate, length and daily limits. An invalid report found in the\n  admin takes the reward back once.\n- prepare() sets a 1-hour ttl on every cache_control sent upstream.\n\nThe trickle, the free daily ceiling and the fair-use ceiling in settings_ent.py\nare launch placeholders.\n\nDeploying needs the ops change on branch claude/credits-gateway-config, because\nthe gateway fails at startup without the new alias keys, and the\nJUSPRIN_OPENROUTER_API_KEY secret must exist first.\nEOF\ncat > $S/msg/gw2.txt <<'EOF'\nKeep JusPrin v2 chats as raw text, without branch files\n\nEvery Standard chat was lost when it came to be kept. _keep_sync parsed each\nreply event as JSON, and OpenRouter's documented stream ends in data: [DONE],\nso the parse threw and the record was dropped.\n\nThe write is now blind: the request and the reply events are stored as the text\nthey came in, so no reply's format can lose a chat. capture.keep no longer needs\nthe messages, so branch-keeping goes too: a retried turn, an edited message or a\nrevert now overwrites the version it replaces. That was a deliberate choice;\nrejected attempts are no longer available as training data.\n\nIn a record, request is now a string and events a list of strings. schema stays\nat 1: nothing reads these records, and no deployment or ops file sets\nJUSPRIN_V2_CAPTURE_CONTAINER. A value supplied from a secret was not checked.\n\nA new test streams a reply ending in [DONE]; it failed before this change. The\nreal OpenRouter stream was not rerun.\nEOF\ncat > $S/msg/ops.txt <<'EOF'\nAdd the Standard model to the JusPrin v2 gateway config\n\nNot applied to any cluster. Apply it only together with the tsd-enterprise\ncredit ledger on branch claude/credits-ledger, because that gateway fails at\nstartup without these alias keys.\n\nThe alias list gains slicer-basic, shown as Standard at 1 credit a message:\nDeepSeek V4 Flash through OpenRouter, with no pictures. slicer-1 becomes Expert\nat 5 credits and defaults to thorough. tsdws in staging and production reads\nJUSPRIN_OPENROUTER_API_KEY from the gateway Secret, so that key must be added to\njusprin-v2-gateway-stg and jusprin-v2-gateway-prod first, or the pods won't\nstart.\nEOF\nL=/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise/.claude/worktrees/credits-ledger; cd $L; grep -n \"ttl\" web_ent/jusprin/v2/upstream.py | head -3 | cut -c1-110; grep -n \"def \\|clawback\\|invalid\" web_ent/jusprin/ledger/reports.py | head -14 | cut -c1-100; grep -n \"note\\|FREE_APP\" web_ent/jusprin/v2/credits.py | head -8 | cut -c1-110; grep -n \"note\" web_ent/jusprin/v2/gateway.py | head -3 | cut -c1-90; grep -n \"'balance'\\|'lots'\\|'activity'\\|\\\"activity\\\"\" web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py | head -5 | cut -c1-100; grep -n \"images\" web_ent/jusprin/v2/upstream.py | head -3 | cut -c1-100; grep -n \"invalid\\|def \" web_ent/jusprin/admin.py | head -10 | cut -c1-100","description":"Write commit messages and check their gateway claims against the code","timeout":20000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5648,"cache_read_input_tokens":272804,"output_tokens":3022,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":55},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemera