k ops config and update the plan doc","status":"pending"},{"content":"Build and run all test suites","status":"pending"},{"content":"Run the three live chats and capture screens","status":"pending"},{"content":"Report in the four-part shape","status":"pending"}],"scope":"continuation"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgeZEA3JCutkz11iSFcmQ","requestRef":"d5ef6fda-d43c-4ab5-a512-c91aa0ae7c21","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c9c4452f-74b0-4c29-99c7-cff9093dfd99","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:14:39.690Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
{"parentUuid":"c9c4452f-74b0-4c29-99c7-cff9093dfd99","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6b3f9665-7f28-483d-84d9-db7ace5fe0b2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VbZsT8TAgyj5bPtqXnBeiD","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan shown (7 steps)."}]}]},"uuid":"414573b8-c7fa-4ce9-a040-7bc590ddb795","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:14:39.730Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan shown (7 steps)."}],"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c9c4452f-74b0-4c29-99c7-cff9093dfd99","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
{"parentUuid":"414573b8-c7fa-4ce9-a040-7bc590ddb795","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgeZEB1Lm2Ru1t3AryQjn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MT4BcKPvqaVpgyVZoKNv7i","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin; for f in pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md pricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md credits-and-onboarding-handoff-2026-11.md; do echo \"#### $f\"; wc -l $f; sed -n 1,45p $f | cut -c1-500; done; echo; cat design-captures/credits-2026-11/MANIFEST.md | cut -c1-220 | head -70; ls design-captures/credits-2026-11 | head -60","description":"Read the decision blocks and the board manifest","timeout":15000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11153,"cache_read_input_tokens":287141,"output_tokens":2133,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":771},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11153,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2133,"cache_read_input_tokens":287141,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11153,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11153},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}},"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MT4BcKPvqaVpgyVZoKNv7i":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin; for f in pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md pricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md credits-and-onboarding-handoff-2026-11.md; do echo \"#### $f\"; wc -l $f; sed -n 1,45p $f | cut -c1-500; done; echo; cat design-captures/credits-2026-11/MANIFEST.md | cut -c1-220 | head -70; ls design-captures/credits-2026-11 | head -60","description":"Read the decision blocks and the board manifest","timeout":15000}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgeZEA3JCutkz11iSFcmQ","requestRef":"d5ef6fda-d43c-4ab5-a512-c91aa0ae7c21","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d6e7dcf1-8ce3-4abd-833e-c9794e6c9281","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:14:41.590Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
{"parentUuid":"d6e7dcf1-8ce3-4abd-833e-c9794e6c9281","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6b3f9665-7f28-483d-84d9-db7ace5fe0b2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MT4BcKPvqaVpgyVZoKNv7i","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (32.5KB). Full output saved to: /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c/tool-results/bvzcbzazr.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n#### pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md\n     307 pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md\n# JusPrin Cloud credits: implementation plan (working doc, 2026-11-01, order of work and readiness updated 2026-11-02; balances credits only since 2026-11-02 evening)\n\n**Decided 2026-11-02 evening, after Kenneth saw canvas version 73. These override anything below that says otherwise.**\n- Every credit is the same. There is no Standard-only lot. Any mention below of a `basic_only` flag, a \"trickle\" of Standard-only credits, \"Free Standard messages\" or \"Free Standard credits\" is superseded. free accounts (not subscribed) get 50 credits a month, expiring one month after grant, that pay for either tier; Kenneth to the design session: \"the 'everyone gets 50 credits' wording is wrong. I never said that.\" (Kenneth: \"let's just give free users 50/mo use-it-or-loose it credits\").\n- Workshop has no ceiling. Standard messages cost 0 credits on Workshop (Kenneth: \"no ceiling. It's probably easier just to say standard messages cost 0 credits\"). Anything below about 600, fair use, or a notice at 500 or 600 is superseded.\n- A balance is one number of credits, never a count of messages beside it. The panel shows one bar per lot, grouped only by when the credits expire: \"First-month credits · 62 of 500 left · Expires 1 Dec\", \"Bought credits · 500 of 500 left · Never expire\". Bought credits get a bar like the others (decision 13 closed).\n- \"New Standard chat\" and board 3d are gone: the case only existed because a Standard-only lot could not pay for an Expert chat. A chat that cannot be paid offers \"Get more credits\" only.\n- Prices in messages appear only on the picker options, the stop card for the chat's own tier, the pricing page's one sentence, the low-balance notice, and one scale line under the first-month offer (\"An Expert message is 5 credits\").\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f0291d97-4cf0-4c2e-a424-faf1d2565ef1","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:14:42.866Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"#### pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md\n     307 pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md\n# JusPrin Cloud credits: implementation plan (working doc, 2026-11-01, order of work and readiness updated 2026-11-02; balances credits only since 2026-11-02 evening)\n\n**Decided 2026-11-02 evening, after Kenneth saw canvas version 73. These override anything below that says otherwise.**\n- Every credit is the same. There is no Standard-only lot. Any mention below of a `basic_only` flag, a \"trickle\" of Standard-only credits, \"Free Standard messages\" or \"Free Standard credits\" is superseded. free accounts (not subscribed) get 50 credits a month, expiring one month after grant, that pay for either tier; Kenneth to the design session: \"the 'everyone gets 50 credits' wording is wrong. I never said that.\" (Kenneth: \"let's just give free users 50/mo use-it-or-loose it credits\").\n- Workshop has no ceiling. Standard messages cost 0 credits on Workshop (Kenneth: \"no ceiling. It's probably easier just to say standard messages cost 0 credits\"). Anything below about 600, fair use, or a notice at 500 or 600 is superseded.\n- A balance is one number of credits, never a count of messages beside it. The panel shows one bar per lot, grouped only by when the credits expire: \"First-month credits · 62 of 500 left · Expires 1 Dec\", \"Bought credits · 500 of 500 left · Never expire\". Bought credits get a bar like the others (decision 13 closed).\n- \"New Standard chat\" and board 3d are gone: the case only existed because a Standard-only lot could not pay for an Expert chat. A chat that cannot be paid offers \"Get more credits\" only.\n- Prices in messages appear only on the picker options, the stop card for the chat's own tier, the pricing page's one sentence, the low-balance notice, and one scale line under the first-month offer (\"An Expert message is 5 credits\").\n- Kenneth reviewed the list of mechanisms that were mine, not his (2026-11-02, late evening). **Kept:** the launch offer (double credits on packs until a date); the low-balance notice, reworded to \"About 25 credits left\" (credits, not messages); \"Expiring credits are used first\" in the panel; the \"Alert me when a subscription would save me money\" switch, on by default; the Account page shape (30-day total, bar chart per day, table of chats); Standard as the default tier for a new chat after the \n- Free credits, ruled 2026-11-02 late: \"no 50 credits for first month. only 500 initial credits. pack holders also get 50 credits a month.\" So the 50 a month goes to every account not on a subscription, starting after the first month; a pack holder gets it; during the first month there is only the 500. The balance example on 2a, 4a and 4b is 62 first-month + 500 bought = 562, with no Free credits bar. Footer: \"After your first month, accounts without a plan get 50 free credits a month.\"\n\nUntracked working document. It turns the pricing plan Kenneth settled on 2026-11-01 into concrete work on the three codebases involved: the gateway in `tsd-enterprise` (`web_ent/jusprin/v2/`), the Obico server it is built on (`obico-server`, where the v1 credit table lives), and the desktop app (`src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/` and the Agent page under `AgentUI/`). Companion docs: `pricing-mental-model-2026-10.md`, `journey-cost-2026-10.md`, `obico-pro-pricing-data-2026-10.md`, `v1-pricing-data-2\n\nEvery \"recommend\" below is my opinion; every \"decided\" is Kenneth's. Code facts were read from the checkouts on 2026-11-01 (tsd-enterprise master, JusPrin `jusprin-newui` at 69780c7af4, ops master).\n\n## 1. The plan being implemented\n\n- The unit is a **credit**, about 2 cents (decided 2026-11-01: \"credits\", not the placeholder \"coins\"). Credits pay per message, not per token. A **Standard** message (DeepSeek V4 Flash class) costs 1 credit; an **Expert** message (Claude Sonnet 5.5 class, not Opus) costs 5 credits. The 1:5 ratio is decided. A balance is shown in credits only, \"562 credits left\", never with a count of messages beside it (Kenneth, 2026-11-02: the two numbers together are confusing). Prices in messages appear only\n- **Pay as you go** (the pack): 500 credits for $10, never expire. Optional auto-reload at a discount.\n- **Hobby, $10 a month:** 750 credits, Standard messages cost credits, unused credits lost at the end of each month.\n- **Workshop, $20 a month:** 1,000 credits plus unlimited Standard messages, unused credits lost each month. Needs fair-use wording.\n- Plan names decided 2026-11-01: Hobby, Workshop, Pay as you go. No Pro, Plus or Premium, because Obico Pro exists next door.\n- **Obico subscribers:** 20% off both subscriptions.\n- **Your first month** (the sign-up grant, never called a trial): about $10 of credits (500), expiring after one month. **Trickle:** a free monthly Standard allowance for light users.\n- **Rewards:** credits of real value for a print report with a photo and detailed text, with a human review flag for bad ones.\n- **Launch period:** discounted, not free, credits.\n- **Alert:** tell the person when their usage has grown to where a subscription saves them money.\n- **BYOK** (the person's own API key) stays free with no sign-in.\n\n### The cost figures the margins rest on\n\nMeasured per user message, one run per journey, from `journey-cost-2026-10.md` (Sonnet added 2026-11-01, so the peer session's \"Sonnet still unmeasured\" is out of date):\n\n| Tier | Model | Cost per user message | Price at 2¢ a credit | Gross margin |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Standard | DeepSeek V4 Flash (OpenRouter) | 0.4¢ to 1¢; 5¢ when the agent polled the slicer 75 times | 2¢ (1 credit) | 50% to 80%; negative in the polling case |\n| Expert | Claude Sonnet 5.5 | 5.6¢ to 7.4¢, mean 6.3¢ over 14 messages | 10¢ (5 credits) | 26% to 44%, 37% at the mean |\n| (not offered) | Claude Opus 5.5 | 10¢ to 21¢ | 10¢ | negative |\n\n\"Per user message\" divides a whole session's cost, including the turns the app starts by itself (file opened, slice finished), by the messages the person typed. So the margins above already assume app-started turns are not charged (see section 3.3). Two cost prerequisites move these: Anthropic's 5-minute cache expiry during a slow slice rewrote 72k tokens for $0.36 on Opus (section 7.1), and the slicer polling tripled one basic session (section 7.2).\n\n## 2. What exists today\n\n**Gateway.** `web_ent/jusprin/v2/gateway.py` is a raw ASGI endpoint on daphne (`tsdws-prod`) that streams `POST /ent/jusprin/v2/messages` (Anthropic format) and `/responses` (OpenAI format) to an upstream model. `credits.py` admits each turn: a Redis rate limit of 60 turns a minute per person (`JUSPRIN_V2_TURNS_PER_MINUTE`), then one v1 credit per turn through `consume_credit_for_pipeline` in `obico-server/backend/app/jusprin/ai_credits.py`, which decrements `JusPrinAICredit.ai_credit_used_curre\n\n#### pricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md\n     145 pricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md\n# Where a person meets the credits, and how each point should feel (working doc, 2026-11-01, synced to canvas version 71; balances changed to credits only on 2026-11-02 evening, canvas update pending on 2026-11-02)\n\n**Decided 2026-11-02 evening, after Kenneth saw canvas version 73. These override anything below that says otherwise.**\n- Every credit is the same. There is no Standard-only lot. Any mention below of a `basic_only` flag, a \"trickle\" of Standard-only credits, \"Free Standard messages\" or \"Free Standard credits\" is superseded. free accounts (not subscribed) get 50 credits a month, expiring one month after grant, that pay for either tier; Kenneth to the design session: \"the 'everyone gets 50 credits' wording is wrong. I never said that.\" (Kenneth: \"let's just give free users 50/mo use-it-or-loose it credits\").\n- Workshop has no ceiling. Standard messages cost 0 credits on Workshop (Kenneth: \"no ceiling. It's probably easier just to say standard messages cost 0 credits\"). Anything below about 600, fair use, or a notice at 500 or 600 is superseded.\n- A balance is one number of credits, never a count of messages beside it. The panel shows one bar per lot, grouped only by when the credits expire: \"First-month credits · 62 of 500 left · Expires 1 Dec\", \"Bought credits · 500 of 500 left · Never expire\". Bought credits get a bar like the others (decision 13 closed).\n- \"New Standard chat\" and board 3d are gone: the case only existed because a Standard-only lot could not pay for an Expert chat. A chat that cannot be paid offers \"Get more credits\" only.\n- Prices in messages appear only on the picker options, the stop card for the chat's own tier, the pricing page's one sentence, the low-balance notice, and one scale line under the first-month offer (\"An Expert message is 5 credits\").\n- Kenneth reviewed the list of mechanisms that were mine, not his (2026-11-02, late evening). **Kept:** the launch offer (double credits on packs until a date); the low-balance notice, reworded to \"About 25 credits left\" (credits, not messages); \"Expiring credits are used first\" in the panel; the \"Alert me when a subscription would save me money\" switch, on by default; the Account page shape (30-day total, bar chart per day, table of chats); Standard as the default tier for a new chat after the \n- Free credits, ruled 2026-11-02 late: \"no 50 credits for first month. only 500 initial credits. pack holders also get 50 credits a month.\" So the 50 a month goes to every account not on a subscription, starting after the first month; a pack holder gets it; during the first month there is only the 500. The balance example on 2a, 4a and 4b is 62 first-month + 500 bought = 562, with no Free credits bar. Footer: \"After your first month, accounts without a plan get 50 free credits a month.\"\n\nUntracked design notes. The pricing plan is in `pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md`; this document is about the person, not the ledger. It lists every point in the product where someone meets credits, says what goes wrong there in other products, and gives one opinion per point. Kenneth reviewed the boards on the JusPrin v2 canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ) between versions 54 and 70; the boards are now the source of truth and this document follows them. Captures are\n\nWhere the boards live on the canvas (decided 2026-11-02: boards sit with the flow they change, not on a feature page): the onboarding boards (1a to 1d, 6a, 6b) on \"On boarding experience\"; the composer states (2a to 2c, 3a to 3d, 7a to 7c) on \"Compositions\" beside the Composer; the Account boards (4a to 4c) on \"Agent setup & Preferences\"; the report boards (8a to 8d) on \"Print history\". \"Credits & plans\" keeps only what has no flow of its own: the five rules (board 0), the pricing page (5a, 5b) \n\nWhat the survey of other products (`pricing-case-studies-2026-10.md`) says goes wrong, in one list: people cannot picture what an abstract credit buys; two kinds of credit with different expiry rules confuse everyone; the anger is at the boundary, when something they were doing stops; a balance that drops for reasons they did not cause breeds distrust; \"unlimited\" with an unstated ceiling is read as a lie once reached.\n\n## Five rules that apply at every point (board 0)\n\n1. **One word, one unit, credits only.** \"Credits\" (decided 2026-11-01), never coins, never tokens. A balance is a number of credits and nothing else: \"562 credits left.\" Kenneth, 2026-11-02: showing a count of messages beside the credits is confusing; consolidate everything into credits. (Canvas versions up to 71 and my earlier drafts put \"That is 612 Standard or 112 Expert messages\" under every balance; that was my addition, never his decision, and it is gone.) The translation into messages ap\n2. **Credits only move when the person sends a message.** Turns the app starts (the file-opened report, the slice-finished note) are free, and the balance never changes without a message from the person. That one fact is what makes the balance trustworthy; it is stated on the pricing page in one sentence: \"Only messages you send cost credits.\"\n3. **Expiring credits are named by what they are, with a date. Bought credits are just \"credits\" and never expire.** \"First-month credits · 62 of 500 left · Expires 1 Dec.\" \"Free Standard credits · 50 of 50 left · Resets 1 Dec · Standard only.\" \"Bought credits · 500 left · Never expire.\" Never a bare number that mixes them. The draw rule is stated once, in the breakdown: \"Expiring credits are used first.\"\n4. **Say the number before the boundary, not at it.** Every ceiling (balance, fair use, expiry) is shown on the way there with a count, so reaching it is never news.\n5. **Nothing typed is lost and nothing stops silently.** A message that cannot be sent stays in the composer. (The earlier draft added \"with a way to send it anyway\"; the design session dropped the phrase on board 0 because a chat now keeps its model, so there is no way to send. That follows from Kenneth's decision but he has not reviewed the wording. The ways forward are to get more credits or, when free Standard messages remain, to start a Standard chat with the typed text carried over.)\n\n## Decisions from the review that shape several points\n\n- **The cheap tier is \"Standard\".** Kenneth, 2026-11-02, in the brainstorm session: not \"Basic\" (the first boards' word, which sells the tier on being the lesser one) and not \"Quick\" (my suggestion). Every surface uses it: \"Standard · 1 credit a message\", \"Unlimited Standard messages\", \"Free Standard credits\", \"50 free Standard credits this month\", \"New Standard chat\", and rule 1's explanation. Canvas version 71 says Standard on every board.\n\n- **A chat keeps its model.** Kenneth, 2026-11-02, board 3b: for now a person cannot switch the model mid-chat. The model and thinking pickers stay in the composer once a chat has a message, greyed, and hovering either shows a two-line tooltip: \"A chat keeps the model and thinking level it started with. Start a new chat to change them.\" and \"Each message you send in this chat costs 5 credits.\" (board 2c). So there is no \"Send with Standard\" and no \"Switch this chat to Standard\" anywhere.\n- **The app's own turns run on Expert, cost nothing, and do not fix the chat's model.** Kenneth, 2026-11-02, brainstorm session. The turn the app starts when a file opens has to read the plate picture, so it runs on Expert whatever the person would pick; it is free under rule 2; and it does not count as the chat's first message. The person's first message fixes the chat's model, and the greyed pickers follow that message, not the app's note. Without this, every chat that begins with a file would\n- **A picture in a Standard chat is dropped, and the attachment row says so.** Kenneth, 2026-11-02, brainstorm session: the Standard model cannot see pictures, and he rejected a long clause in the picker option. The notice lives on the staged attachment itself (point 2).\n- **One action outside the pricing page: \"Get more credits\".** Kenneth, board 3c: at the moment someone runs out they cannot judge a pack against a plan from a button label, so there is no \"Buy\" beside \"Subscribe\" in the app. \"Get more credits\" opens the pricing page, which explains the difference. The one exception is the savings alert (point 7), whose \"Subscribe\" names one plan and shows the sums.\n\n## The points, in the order a person meets them\n\n### 1. First launch: own key or JusPrin account (boards 1a to 1d)\n\nWhere: the Agent setup in Preferences › Agent (the one setup flow, decided 2026-10-23) and the welcome screen.\n\nKenneth's reaction to the first draft, which put the offer as a small line under \"Set up JusPrin\": \"the most non-obvious way to urge user to sign up\". Opinion, as drawn: the offer is the headline on its own surface, \"Your first month: 500 credits\", with the translation under it, \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\", and the button names the reward, \"Sign in for 500 credits\". \"Explore first\" moves below it. Never \"trial\" (decided): a trial promises a wall at the end. No \n\nv1 subscribers (Kenneth, board 1c: \"make it clear that JusPrin v1 subscribers grandfathered to the $10/mo tier with the original price\", \"in addition to getting 500 credits\"). 1c adds the line \"Subscribed to JusPrin v1? You get these 500 credits and keep your original price, on the $10 Hobby plan.\", conditional because the app cannot know until sign-in. Board 1d is what that person sees once signed in: \"Hobby, at your original $6.99 a month. 750 credits a month. Plus 500 more for your first mont\n\n### 2. Picking Standard or Expert for a chat (boards 2b, 2c)\n#### credits-and-onboarding-handoff-2026-11.md\n      85 credits-and-onboarding-handoff-2026-11.md\n# Handoff: build JusPrin Cloud credits and finish the first-run onboarding\n\n**Decided 2026-11-02 evening, after Kenneth saw canvas version 73. These override anything below that says otherwise.**\n- Every credit is the same. There is no Standard-only lot. Any mention below of a `basic_only` flag, a \"trickle\" of Standard-only credits, \"Free Standard messages\" or \"Free Standard credits\" is superseded. free accounts (not subscribed) get 50 credits a month, expiring one month after grant, that pay for either tier; Kenneth to the design session: \"the 'everyone gets 50 credits' wording is wrong. I never said that.\" (Kenneth: \"let's just give free users 50/mo use-it-or-loose it credits\").\n- Workshop has no ceiling. Standard messages cost 0 credits on Workshop (Kenneth: \"no ceiling. It's probably easier just to say standard messages cost 0 credits\"). Anything below about 600, fair use, or a notice at 500 or 600 is superseded.\n- A balance is one number of credits, never a count of messages beside it. The panel shows one bar per lot, grouped only by when the credits expire: \"First-month credits · 62 of 500 left · Expires 1 Dec\", \"Bought credits · 500 of 500 left · Never expire\". Bought credits get a bar like the others (decision 13 closed).\n- \"New Standard chat\" and board 3d are gone: the case only existed because a Standard-only lot could not pay for an Expert chat. A chat that cannot be paid offers \"Get more credits\" only.\n- Prices in messages appear only on the picker options, the stop card for the chat's own tier, the pricing page's one sentence, the low-balance notice, and one scale line under the first-month offer (\"An Expert message is 5 credits\").\n- Kenneth reviewed the list of mechanisms that were mine, not his (2026-11-02, late evening). **Kept:** the launch offer (double credits on packs until a date); the low-balance notice, reworded to \"About 25 credits left\" (credits, not messages); \"Expiring credits are used first\" in the panel; the \"Alert me when a subscription would save me money\" switch, on by default; the Account page shape (30-day total, bar chart per day, table of chats); Standard as the default tier for a new chat after the \n- Free credits, ruled 2026-11-02 late: \"no 50 credits for first month. only 500 initial credits. pack holders also get 50 credits a month.\" So the 50 a month goes to every account not on a subscription, starting after the first month; a pack holder gets it; during the first month there is only the 500. The balance example on 2a, 4a and 4b is 62 first-month + 500 bought = 562, with no Free credits bar. Footer: \"After your first month, accounts without a plan get 50 free credits a month.\"\n\nWritten 2026-11-02 for a coding agent who has not seen the design sessions. This is a working doc: keep it untracked, never commit it, never add it to `.gitignore` or `.git/info/exclude`. Kenneth tracks unfinished work by the untracked files in `git status`.\n\n## 1. What you are building, in one paragraph\n\nJusPrin 2 is a fork of OrcaSlicer with an in-app AI agent. The agent can run on the person's own API key (free, no account) or on JusPrin's hosted gateway (an Obico-server endpoint, `app.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/…`, live in production since 2026-10-25). The gateway is about to start charging in credits: a Standard message costs 1 credit, an Expert message 5. People get 500 credits in their first month, can buy packs that never expire, or subscribe (Hobby $10, Workshop $20). This work adds the c\n\n## 2. Read these first, in this order\n\n1. `pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md` (same folder). The whole technical plan: ledger tables, the charging algorithm, the `/account` JSON, the 402 body, alias config, Chargebee, rewards, section 11 \"Order of work and tests\", section 12 \"Decisions still Kenneth's\". Build from it.\n2. `pricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md`. Each point where a person meets credits, the five rules that apply everywhere, and the exact wording. When the plan and this doc disagree on words, this doc wins.\n3. The boards. Captures in `design-captures/credits-2026-11/` (one PNG per board, `credits-<board>-<slug>.png`, `-dark` variants where they exist). `MANIFEST.md` there lists every board with its canvas page and name; `CHANGELOG-v54-to-v69.md` records why each board looks the way it does. The live canvas is the JusPrin v2 design artifact, https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, at version 71. Figma is retired; do not design from it.\n4. `AGENTS.md` and `agent-docs/jusprin/README.md`, `fork-stewardship.md`, `design-system.md`. House rules; the ones that bite most often are repeated in section 7 below.\n\n## 3. Where the code lives\n\nYou run on Kenneth's Mac, the machine the design sessions ran on, so every path below is live. The three repositories are checked out here and on GitHub: the app at `~/Projects/JusPrin` (`git@github.com:TheSpaghettiDetective/JusPrin.git`, branch `jusprin-newui`), the gateway at `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise` (`git@github.com:kennethjiang/tsd-enterprise.git`, branch `master`, with `obico-server` as a submodule), and deployment at `~/Projects/ops` (`git@github.com:kennethjiang/ops.git`). Other agent \n\n**App (this repository).** Branch `jusprin-newui` at `69780c7af4`, in sync with `origin`. Work in your own worktree and branch; never reuse another session's worktree.\n- Composer, pickers, attachments, Preferences page: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/` (`Composer.tsx`, `ModelPickers.tsx`, `AttachmentChip.tsx`, `Preferences.tsx`, `WelcomeBack.tsx`).\n- Host side of the agent: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/` (`AgentHost.cpp` holds `chat_model_choice`, `use_chat_model`, `start_turn`; `ProviderAgent` sends the gateway headers and maps HTTP errors; `CloudAccount.cpp` and `ModelCatalog.cpp` hold the account's model list).\n- Home page and onboarding: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/` and `HomeUI/src/`. Preferences window: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Preferences/`. The v1 import and the welcome-back window: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/V1Import/`.\n- Tests: Catch2 under `tests/jusprin/` and `tests/brand/`; Vitest beside each TypeScript file; the shell harness under `tests/shell/` drives the built app without a screen.\n- Build: `cmake --build build/arm64 --config RelWithDebInfo --target all -- -j4`. The Mac is shared by several agent sessions: check `uptime` and `pgrep -fl ninja` first, one build per build directory, never restart a running build. Editing a CMake file rebuilds everything.\n\n**Gateway (tsd-enterprise).** Repository `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise`, branch from `master` (it moved 12 commits past the gateway merge, including the Python 3.12 / Django 5.2 bump), in your own worktree. The gateway is `web_ent/jusprin/v2/` (`aliases.py`, `upstream.py`, `gateway.py`, `stream.py`, `credits.py`, `auth.py`, `errors.py`, `views.py`, `urls.py`; tests in `tests/test_gateway.py` and `tests/test_aliases.py`, using the MockTransport injection the file already uses). `obico-server` is a g\n\n**Deployment (ops).** `~/Projects/ops`: the alias ConfigMap is `tsd/prod/jusprin-v2-gateway.yaml` and `tsd/stg/jusprin-v2-gateway.yaml`. Staging is `https://app-stg.obico.io` and runs the same image as production. Production is live for real users: do not change it. For any `gcloud` or `kubectl` command, first run `gcloud config set account ai-agent@tsdtechnology.iam.gserviceaccount.com`, and stay read-only on production.\n\n## 4. Step 0: the onboarding branch\n\n`onboarding-frontend-only` (one commit, `8f4588beae`, Kenneth, 2026-10-06; `origin/onboarding-frontend-only` is identical) adds the local first-run path to Home: welcome, import presets from an existing OrcaSlicer install, confirm or choose a printer setup, open a project or the bundled example. Its commit message is a good spec of what it does and what it deliberately left out. It is 139 commits behind `jusprin-newui`.\n\nA dry-run rebase on 2026-11-02 conflicted in 18 of its 27 files. Expect to resolve `HomeBackend.hpp`, `HomeHost.cpp`, `HomeHost.hpp`, `HomeSnapshot.hpp`, `OrcaHomeBackend.cpp`, `OrcaHomeBackend.hpp`, `resources/jusprin/home/protocol.json`, `HomeUI/src/App.tsx`, `App.test.tsx`, `bridge/protocol.ts`, `bridge/protocol.test.ts`, `state/store.ts`, `styles.css`, `styles.test.ts`, `tokens.ts`, `sources.cmake`, `tests/jusprin/test_home_host.cpp` and `test_home_snapshot.cpp`. Nine files apply cleanly, am\n\n\n# Credits & plans boards, 2026-11-01\n\nThe boards are on the JusPrin v2 canvas, https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ (version 79, 1793642611-3f5d), each on the page of its flow: 1a to 1d, 6a and 6b on \"On boarding experience\"; 2a to 2c, 3a to 3c,\n\n| PNG | Board | What it shows |\n|---|---|---|\n| credits-00-rules | 0 | The five rules from pricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md |\n| credits-01a-agent-setup | 1a | Preferences › Agent over a first-run Home, with the pitch on the account row (also -dark) |\n| credits-01b-welcome | 1b | The canvas's proposed welcome screen, pitch under Set up JusPrin (also -dark) |\n| credits-01c-welcome-back | 1c | The welcome window the app builds today, pitch in the account box (also -dark) |\n| credits-01d-welcome-back-v1-subscriber | 1d | Welcome window for a signed-in JusPrin v1 subscriber: Hobby at their original price (also -dark) |\n| credits-02a-balance-hover | 2a | Greyed model and thinking pickers, ring only, hover usage panel with a bar per kind of credit |\n| credits-02b-tier-picker | 2b | New chat, picker open: Basic and Expert with price per message and clause, own-key models without price |\n| credits-02c-pickers-greyed-tooltip | 2c | Chat under way: tooltip on the greyed pickers with the reason and the price |\n| credits-03a-low-notice | 3a | \"About 25 credits left\", ring in the warning colour |\n| credits-03b-send-with-basic | 3b | 3 credits: Send disabled, note, Get more credits, typed text kept (file name kept for the comment anchor) |\n| credits-03c-failed-card | 3c | Gateway 402 card at 3 credits with Get more credits |\n| credits-03e-picture-in-standard-chat | 3e | Standard chat with a photo staged: the row's second line warns it won't be sent, Remove is the only action, Send enabled |\n| credits-04a-account-over-prepare | 4a | Preferences › Account at window size over Prepare |\n| credits-04b-account-first-month | 4b | Whole Account section, first month plus a pack (also -dark) |\n| credits-04c-account-workshop | 4c | Whole Account section on Workshop as an Obico member, with the clawback row (also -dark) |\n| credits-05a-pricing | 5a | Pricing page, three cards, launch note (also -dark) |\n| credits-05b-pricing-obico | 5b | Same page with the member price as the price |\n| credits-06a-first-month-ended | 6a | First launch after the first month: new chat on Standard, with the ring, no thinking picker and no line about free credits |\n| credits-06b-first-month-ended-picker | 6b | Same new chat with the picker open on Expert |\n| credits-07a-alert-hobby | 7a | Savings alert, Pay as you go to Hobby |\n| credits-07b-alert-hobby-sums | 7b | Same with the arithmetic open |\n| credits-08a-report-button | 8a | \"Tell us how it printed · 25 credits\" on the Print history entry, beside Print again and Export |\n| credits-08b-report-form | 8b | Report form over Print history: photo, a few sentences, outcome |\n| credits-08c-report-sent | 8c | The button replaced by a \"Report sent · 25 credits added\" row on the entry |\n| credits-08d-home-way-in | 8d | Home with the report line on a project card, opening Print history filtered to that project |\n| credits-09-states | 9 | Balance and tier label states, light and dark panels |\n\n## Numbers corrected in canvas version 70\n\n1. The translation of the balance now reads \"612 Basic or 112 Expert messages\", because the 50 free Basic messages can't pay for Expert: (612 − 50) / 5 = 112.\n2. The savings alert now says $5.00. 820 credits cost $16.40 Pay as you go, against $10 + 70 × 2¢ = $11.40 on Hobby.\n3. The balance is now 62 first-month + 50 free Basic + 500 bought = 612. A 500 pack can't stand at 450 while first-month credits remain, because expiring credits are used first. Usage is 438 credits (500 − 62), and 4b'\n\n## Kenneth's decisions applied in canvas version 71 (2026-11-02)\n\n1. The cheap tier is \"Standard\", on every board. Older lines in this file say \"Basic\" because they describe what was true then. The file names credits-03b-send-with-basic and credits-03d-expert-chat-free-basic keep the o\n2. New board 3e. Kenneth then changed it directly, 2026-11-02: \"remove 'new expert chat' button\" and \"style it as warning. with color and icon.\" So the row is the usual thumbnail, name, second line and Remove, and the se\n3. The turn the app starts when a file opens runs on Expert, is free, and doesn't fix the chat's model. 2b's caption says so, and 2b, 6b and board 9 now say \"the person's first message\". 2c's tooltip is unchanged.\n\n## Kenneth's decision applied in canvas version 73 (2026-11-02)\n\nBalances are shown in credits only. He said that showing a number of messages and credits at the same time is confusing. The rule he agreed with: a number of messages appears only where the person chooses or is stopped, \n\n- 2a, 4a, 4b, 4c: the headline stands alone, \"612 credits left\" (\"640 credits left\" on 4c). The free lot is \"Free Standard credits\", and its note line starts \"Standard only\". No board","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c/tool-results/bvzcbzazr.txt","persistedOutputSize":33234},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d6e7dcf1-8ce3-4abd-833e-c9794e6c9281","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
