{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","hash":"dff97f5acaa3f32d97a3c967dd6efa4b1f049073f253c2e01d2fc186b4acc5bc","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ExBxFkMP3jWCwiMuRqcczm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/credits-2026-11/MANIFEST.md | cut -c1-420; ls /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/credits-2026-11 | tr '\\n' ' ' | cut -c1-1200; cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding; git status --short | cut -c1-60; cd src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin; grep -rnE \"basic_only|basicOnly|basic_used|basic_fair|fair.use|affordable|unlimited_basic|unlimitedBasic|offerStandardChat|free Standard|Free Standard|Standard messages|Expert messages|trickle|New Standard|month.end|credits_exhausted|free_app|Standard or\" Agent Home Shell V1Import AgentUI/src HomeUI/src ../../../../resources/jusprin ../../../../tests/agent ../../../../tests/jusprin ../../../../tests/shell --include='*' 2>/dev/null | grep -v \"BalancePanel\\|Composer.credits.test\\|credits.ts:\" | cut -c1-170","description":"Read the board manifest and list app code mentioning the old rules","timeout":15000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Am1JZ74fz1vu2NjYvhacfz","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/credits.ts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XjPSpnNUVehuyJD5dfGxGS","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/BalancePanel.tsx"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014ZH4FT7fGCyk9uiXiktJbs","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/BalancePanel.test.tsx"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018ownXF4GecNUY9JbBkdLmr","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/Composer.credits.test.tsx"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PQk9ZVC9NhQKjKTAi3zvfH","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/ModelPickers.tsx"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WxDVY3tZtxjy61jMcxQ93Y","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/WelcomeBack.tsx"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","hash":"15fa46c4c0a46f5f9866bc8e0165466102bf93662af26be59ac90d1e466638d7","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ExBxFkMP3jWCwiMuRqcczm","type":"tool_result","content":"# Credits & plans boards, 2026-11-01\n\nThe boards are on the JusPrin v2 canvas, https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ (version 79, 1793642611-3f5d), each on the page of its flow: 1a to 1d, 6a and 6b on \"On boarding experience\"; 2a to 2c, 3a to 3c, 3e, 7a and 7b on \"Compositions\" beside the Composer; 4a to 4c on \"Agent setup & Preferences\"; 8a to 8d on \"Print history\"; 0 (the five rules), 5a, 5b and 9 on \"Credits & plans\". Nothing is committed.\n\n| PNG | Board | What it shows |\n|---|---|---|\n| credits-00-rules | 0 | The five rules from pricing-touchpoints-design-2026-11.md |\n| credits-01a-agent-setup | 1a | Preferences › Agent over a first-run Home, with the pitch on the account row (also -dark) |\n| credits-01b-welcome | 1b | The canvas's proposed welcome screen, pitch under Set up JusPrin (also -dark) |\n| credits-01c-welcome-back | 1c | The welcome window the app builds today, pitch in the account box (also -dark) |\n| credits-01d-welcome-back-v1-subscriber | 1d | Welcome window for a signed-in JusPrin v1 subscriber: Hobby at their original price (also -dark) |\n| credits-02a-balance-hover | 2a | Greyed model and thinking pickers, ring only, hover usage panel with a bar per kind of credit |\n| credits-02b-tier-picker | 2b | New chat, picker open: Basic and Expert with price per message and clause, own-key models without price |\n| credits-02c-pickers-greyed-tooltip | 2c | Chat under way: tooltip on the greyed pickers with the reason and the price |\n| credits-03a-low-notice | 3a | \"About 25 credits left\", ring in the warning colour |\n| credits-03b-send-with-basic | 3b | 3 credits: Send disabled, note, Get more credits, typed text kept (file name kept for the comment anchor) |\n| credits-03c-failed-card | 3c | Gateway 402 card at 3 credits with Get more credits |\n| credits-03e-picture-in-standard-chat | 3e | Standard chat with a photo staged: the row's second line warns it won't be sent, Remove is the only action, Send enabled |\n| credits-04a-account-over-prepare | 4a | Preferences › Account at window size over Prepare |\n| credits-04b-account-first-month | 4b | Whole Account section, first month plus a pack (also -dark) |\n| credits-04c-account-workshop | 4c | Whole Account section on Workshop as an Obico member, with the clawback row (also -dark) |\n| credits-05a-pricing | 5a | Pricing page, three cards, launch note (also -dark) |\n| credits-05b-pricing-obico | 5b | Same page with the member price as the price |\n| credits-06a-first-month-ended | 6a | First launch after the first month: new chat on Standard, with the ring, no thinking picker and no line about free credits |\n| credits-06b-first-month-ended-picker | 6b | Same new chat with the picker open on Expert |\n| credits-07a-alert-hobby | 7a | Savings alert, Pay as you go to Hobby |\n| credits-07b-alert-hobby-sums | 7b | Same with the arithmetic open |\n| credits-08a-report-button | 8a | \"Tell us how it printed · 25 credits\" on the Print history entry, beside Print again and Export |\n| credits-08b-report-form | 8b | Report form over Print history: photo, a few sentences, outcome |\n| credits-08c-report-sent | 8c | The button replaced by a \"Report sent · 25 credits added\" row on the entry |\n| credits-08d-home-way-in | 8d | Home with the report line on a project card, opening Print history filtered to that project |\n| credits-09-states | 9 | Balance and tier label states, light and dark panels |\n\n## Numbers corrected in canvas version 70\n\n1. The translation of the balance now reads \"612 Basic or 112 Expert messages\", because the 50 free Basic messages can't pay for Expert: (612 − 50) / 5 = 112.\n2. The savings alert now says $5.00. 820 credits cost $16.40 Pay as you go, against $10 + 70 × 2¢ = $11.40 on Hobby.\n3. The balance is now 62 first-month + 50 free Basic + 500 bought = 612. A 500 pack can't stand at 450 while first-month credits remain, because expiring credits are used first. Usage is 438 credits (500 − 62), and 4b's \"+25\" print report row became \"Bought 500 credits, +500\", because an unspent reward would be a never-expiring lot the balance doesn't show.\n\n## Kenneth's decisions applied in canvas version 71 (2026-11-02)\n\n1. The cheap tier is \"Standard\", on every board. Older lines in this file say \"Basic\" because they describe what was true then. The file names credits-03b-send-with-basic and credits-03d-expert-chat-free-basic keep the old word, so comment anchors and capture names hold. \"Bambu PLA Basic\" is a filament and stays. The orange note lost its item about the docs allowing a mid-chat switch; its Thinking picker item is stil\n2. New board 3e. Kenneth then changed it directly, 2026-11-02: \"remove 'new expert chat' button\" and \"style it as warning. with color and icon.\" So the row is the usual thumbnail, name, second line and Remove, and the second line is the design system's warning: the triangle-alert glyph in status-warning beside Body Small in primary ink. The colour is on the glyph only, because #D49A2A as text is hard to read on the l\n3. The turn the app starts when a file opens runs on Expert, is free, and doesn't fix the chat's model. 2b's caption says so, and 2b, 6b and board 9 now say \"the person's first message\". 2c's tooltip is unchanged.\n\n## Kenneth's decision applied in canvas version 73 (2026-11-02)\n\nBalances are shown in credits only. He said that showing a number of messages and credits at the same time is confusing. The rule he agreed with: a number of messages appears only where the person chooses or is stopped, never on a balance. This replaces the translations described in the older lines of this file, including item 1 under \"Numbers corrected in canvas version 70\".\n\n- 2a, 4a, 4b, 4c: the headline stands alone, \"612 credits left\" (\"640 credits left\" on 4c). The free lot is \"Free Standard credits\", and its note line starts \"Standard only\". No board has a tag component, so the marker is words on the note line.\n- 1a, 1b, 1c: the line under the offer is \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\"\n- 1d: \"750 credits a month.\"\n- 5a, 5b: the translation line is gone from all three cards. The launch offer ends \"$10 buys 1,000 credits.\"\n- Not in the brief, changed because they would be false otherwise: the captions of 4c (\"on free Standard credits\") and 5a (no longer says the cards state the price in messages).\n- Boards 0, 1a's kept \"Your text here\" box, 2b, 2c, 3a to 3e, 6a, 6b, 7a to 7c, 8a to 8d and 9 are unchanged. Board 9 moved up 40 px on the canvas because 5b above it got shorter.\n\n## Canvas version 74 (2026-11-02), the pricing session's follow-up to version 73\n\nChanged: 6a and 6b's composer line is \"50 free Standard credits this month\"; 3d's title, caption and notice say \"free Standard credits\"; board 0's rule 1 is headed \"One word, one unit, credits only.\" and says a balance is a number of credits and nothing else. On 6b the line sits behind the open menu, as it did before.\n\nKept, because the pricing session says they describe allowances or ceilings, not a balance: 5a and 5b's \"Everyone also gets 50 free Standard messages a month.\"; board 9's \"used 500 of 600 free Standard messages this month\" and the notice at 600; 2c's caption \"while free messages last\".\n\nRule 1 now says prices in messages appear only on the picker options, the stop card, the pricing page sentence and one scale line under the first-month offer. Three things drawn elsewhere don't fit that list, left as they are because both briefs kept them: 3a's \"About 5 Expert messages left\" (a low-balance count in messages), 2c's tooltip \"Each message you send in this chat costs 5 credits.\", and 4c's note \"After 600\n\n## Kenneth's decisions applied in canvas version 75 (2026-11-02)\n\nHis words, relayed by the pricing session: \"no ceiling. It's probably easier just to say standard messages cost 0 credits\" (Workshop) and \"let's just give free users 50/mo use-it-or-loose it credits\". He also agreed that bought credits get a bar like the others. These replace the Standard-only lot, the 600 ceiling and the plain number for bought credits described in the older lines of this file.\n\n1. Every credit is the same. The free allowance is 50 credits a month that expire at month end and pay for either tier. 2a, 4a, 4b show \"First-month credits 62 of 500 left, Expires 1 Dec\", \"Free credits 50 of 50 left, Resets 1 Dec\", \"Bought credits 500 of 500 left, Never expire\". The total stays 612.\n2. Workshop is 1,000 credits a month, and Standard messages cost 0 credits. 4c has one bar, \"Workshop credits 640 of 1,000 left\", because this subscriber has no bought credits and the total stays 640. 5a and 5b's Workshop card and footer changed as asked. Board 9 lost the notices at 500 and 600. 2b's caption gives \"Standard · 0 credits a message\" for a Workshop subscriber; no board draws that menu.\n3. Board 3d is removed, its PNG too, and 3e moved left into its place. New Standard chat is gone from the captions of 3b and 3c.\n\nChanged beyond the brief, because the new rules make them false:\n- 6b's menu showed \"Standard · free\". It now shows \"Standard · 1 credit a message\", because a Standard message spends a free credit.\n- Captions: 2a, 2c (\"free this month\" is gone), 4b, 4c, 6a (pointed at 3d, now 3b), 6b.\n- Board 0: rule 3 lost \"Never a bare number that mixes kinds\", because the total is a plain sum; rule 4 lost \"fair use\". Rule 5 never mentioned New Standard chat, and board 0 had no Workshop line, so the Workshop sentence went into rule 2.\n- The blue note on the credits page lost its items about 188 of 600, New Standard chat, Standard · free and the Workshop 600 line.\n\nOpen questions:\n- Closed in version 76, from Kenneth directly: \"No. the \"everyone gets 50 credits\" wording is wrong. I never sadi that.\" A Workshop subscriber doesn't get the 50, so 4c is right as drawn. 5a and 5b's footer now reads \"Free accounts get 50 credits a month. Unused ones don't carry over. Your own API key stays free and never uses credits.\" `pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md` line 142 still says \"Everyone\".\n- New, asked of Kenneth: 2a, 4a and 4b show a Free credits bar for someone in their first month who also bought a pack. If that person isn't a free account, the bar goes and the total is 562, not 612.\n- Closed in version 77, from Kenneth directly: \"ring for free credits. No reason to make exception to show free 50 free credits this month.\" 6a and 6b have the ring, full at 50 of 50, and the line above the box is gone.\n- Closed in version 77, from Kenneth directly: \"say \"25 credits left\" instead of \"About 5 Expert messages left\"\". 3a's notice and title changed, which also ends 3a's conflict with rule 1.\n- Closed in version 78: 7c is gone, so its sums no longer matter.\n- One conflict with rule 1 from the version 74 list still stands: 2c's tooltip. 3a and 4c's note are gone.\n\n## Kenneth's review applied in canvas version 78 (2026-11-02)\n\nHis keep list and \"The expiration should be One month from the day when the credits were granted\", relayed by the pricing session, which read what he didn't keep as dropped and said so to him at 17:46:58. These replace \"expire at month end\" and the notices described in the older lines of this file.\n\n1. Dropped: board 7c and its PNG, the 7-day expiry notice and the month-end notice on board 9, the thinking picker on Standard (3e, 6a, 6b, board 9's Standard row). 2b's caption says a Standard chat has no thinking picker. The sentence \"It also says when a plan isn't paying off.\" is gone from the Alerts section of 4a, 4b and 4c.\n2. Changed: 3a reads \"About 25 credits left\". Kenneth said \"25 credits left\" at 17:40:58 and \"About 25 credits left\" in his keep list at 17:46:15; the later one is used. The free lot reads \"Expires 2 Dec\" on 2a, 4a, 4b. 4c's plan bar reads \"Expires 1 Dec\" instead of \"Resets 1 Dec\", and \"Renews 1 Dec\" stays on the plan line.\n3. Board 0: rule 3 states the expiry rule, rule 4 is only the low-balance notice, so there are still five rules.\n4. Not applied: the brief's \"everyone gets the 50 free credits, Workshop subscribers too, so 4c gets a 'Free credits' bar and reads 690\", and its \"Everyone also gets\" footer. The pricing session asked him at 17:28:56 with that as its own pick and no answer is in its transcript. At 17:30:08 he told this session directly: \"No. the \"everyone gets 50 credits\" wording is wrong. I never sadi that.\" 4c stays one bar at 640 \n\n## Kenneth's decision applied in canvas version 79 (2026-11-02)\n\nHis words, 18:01:06 in the pricing session: \"no 50 credits for first month. only 500 initial credits. pack holders also get 50 credits a month.\" So the 50 free credits a month go to every account not on a subscription, starting after the first month, and that includes pack holders. This replaces the 612 total and the Free credits bar in the first-month state described in the older lines of this file.\n\n- 2a, 4a, 4b: no Free credits bar. The total is 562 (62 first-month + 500 bought). The ring's hidden label on 2a, 2b, 2c, 3e, 4a and board 9 also says 562; those boards look the same otherwise, and their ring fill is unchanged because the ring still has no agreed total.\n- 5a, 5b footer: \"After your first month, accounts without a plan get 50 free credits a month. Your own API key stays free and never uses credits.\" The old footer's \"Unused ones don't carry over\" went with it, as the brief's wording has no such sentence, so the page no longer says free credits expire.\n- Board 0's rule 3 says the same.\n- 6a and 6b are unchanged: they show someone after the first month on the ring at 50 of 50. The brief mentions a line \"50 free credits this month\" there, but Kenneth removed that line in version 77 and it is not on the boards.\n- Board 9 has no bar and needed no change beyond the hidden label.\n\n## Choices of mine that Kenneth may want to change\n\n- The Thinking picker is drawn on JusPrin entries with today's Fast and Thorough, one price per tier; the plan does not say whether Thorough costs more. Expert defaulting to Thorough and Basic to Fast are mine.\n- \"Basic · free\" as the label for a Basic message that costs nothing. The design doc only defines \"Basic · 1 credit\".\n- Wording of the Workshop 600 notice, the reverse alert's arithmetic, \"Workshop credits\" as the lot's name, and the report form's copy.\n- 31 Jan is a placeholder for the launch end date.\n- The savings alert's control is the Preferences checkbox the app already has; there is no switch token.\n- 1a, 1b and 1c (redrawn 2026-11-02, canvas version 55, after Kenneth's comment that the pitch was too easy to miss): the pitch is split into the headline \"Your first month: 500 credits\" and the line \"That is 500 Basic or 100 Expert messages. Your own key stays free.\", on the selected surface, with the button \"Sign in for 500 credits\". On 1c signing in is the primary button and Continue the secondary one.\n- 1c drops the warning triangle from the account box, because an offer is not a warning.\n- 2026-11-02, canvas version 56, from Kenneth's three comments on 2a, 2b and 3b. (1) Usage: composer ring plus \"612 left\"; panel and Account use one row per kind with a bar of what is left, count and date; bought credits have no bar; Workshop's \"412 of 600\" became \"188 of 600 left\" so every bar means the same. (2) Price: \"1 credit a message\", \"5 credits a message\". (3) A chat keeps its model: the tier is a menu only \n- 2026-11-02, canvas version 57, from Kenneth's comments on 4a and 3c, replacing the per-kind bars of version 56. Account and the 2a panel follow Lovable's screens: plan card, one meter \"612 / 1,000 left\", a Type / Expires / Left table, Usage as a per-day chart with totals per chat. Outside the pricing page, \"Get more credits\" replaces Buy credits and Subscribe; New Basic chat stays. The chart's numbers are drawn to \n- 2026-11-02, canvas version 58, from Kenneth's comment on 3c (\"if a user has <5 credits, no point for new basic chat here\"): New Basic chat is gone from 3b and 3c. It appears only with 5 or more credits that only Basic can spend, drawn as new board 3d; that board and its wording are my choice.\n- 2026-11-02, canvas version 59, from Kenneth's Claude and ChatGPT screenshots: Account and the 2a panel now show the total, then a bar per kind of credit (\"112 of 500 left\", Expires or Resets), replacing the one meter \"612 / 1,000\" and the table. Bought credits are a plain number. The 1,000 placeholder is gone from those boards; the composer's ring still has no real total. Usage per day stays.\n- 2026-11-02, canvas version 60, from Kenneth's comment on 5b: \"Obico member\" became \"Obico Premium Subscriber\" on 4c and 5b. The pricing notes and plan call that plan Obico Pro; asked in the thread which name is right. The design doc section 12 still says \"Obico member\".\n- 2026-11-02, canvas version 64, from Kenneth's comment on 1a: \"Your own key\" became \"Your own API key\" on 1a, 1b and 1c. Kenneth saves from the canvas now, so read the live files before publishing; a stray \"Your text here\" box from such a save is kept on 1a, and running the builder overwrites it unless it is carried over.\n- 2026-11-02, from Kenneth's comment on 1c: JusPrin v1 subscribers are grandfathered to the $10 tier at their original price. 1c gains a line, new board 1d shows the signed-in case. $6.99 and $59.99 are v1's Chargebee prices; reading \"$10 tier\" as Hobby and \"while you stay subscribed\" are mine, asked in the thread. Replaces the plan's Workshop until term end. Kenneth then added \"in additiona to getting 500 credits\": \n- 2026-11-02, canvas version 67, from Kenneth's comment on 8a pointing at the print history lesson (\"don't assume users can easily go back to the original chat and find the card\"): the print report button left the chat for the Print history entry; 8c and 8d are new, and the \"+25 credits\" composer state is gone from board 9. Mine, asked in the thread: the Home line's rule and its two-week limit, and the button on expo\n- 2026-11-02, from Kenneth's two comments on 7a: the composer shows only the ring, with no count, and once a chat has a message the model and thinking pickers stay in place, greyed, with a tooltip giving the reason and the price (new board 2c). The two-line tooltip needs a design-system change, since the tooltip is one line today. The ring still has no agreed total.\n- The report form's outcome is the person's answer on the report. It does not add a failure state to print history, which was decided against on 2026-10-27.\n\n## Not drawn\n\n- Dark Prepare boards: the viewport is a light screenshot, and design-system.md rule 1 keeps one canonical mode per screen. The canvas's theme switch still works on them.\n\n## Tooling\n\n`figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_credits_page.py` builds the boards. `figma-mirror/tools/composer/render_dc.py` renders them through the canvas's own runtime, because `render.py` draws `<dc-import>` blank. Work copies are in `figma-mirror/work-credits/`.\nCHANGELOG-v54-to-v69.md MANIFEST.md credits-00-rules.png credits-01a-agent-setup-dark.png credits-01a-agent-setup.png credits-01b-welcome-dark.png credits-01b-welcome.png credits-01c-welcome-back-dark.png credits-01c-welcome-back.png credits-01d-welcome-back-v1-subscriber-dark.png credits-01d-welcome-back-v1-subscriber.png credits-02a-balance-hover.png credits-02b-tier-picker.png credits-02c-pickers-greyed-tooltip.png credits-03a-low-notice.png credits-03b-send-with-basic.png credits-03c-failed-card.png credits-03e-picture-in-standard-chat.png credits-04a-account-over-prepare.png credits-04b-account-first-month-dark.png credits-04b-account-first-month.png credits-04c-account-workshop-dark.png credits-04c-account-workshop.png credits-05a-pricing-dark.png credits-05a-pricing.png credits-05b-pricing-obico.png credits-06a-first-month-ended.png credits-06b-first-month-ended-picker.png credits-07a-alert-hobby.png credits-07b-alert-hobby-sums.png credits-08a-report-button.png credits-08b-report-form.png credits-08c-report-sent.png credits-08d-home-way-in.png credits-09-states-dark.png credits-09-states.png ?? live-check-2026-11-02/\nAgent/AgentProtocol.hpp:230:    // credits_exhausted: the gateway's account of what the turn needed (JSON),\nAgent/ProviderAgent.cpp:639:        if (answer.is_object() && answer.contains(\"error\") && answer[\"error\"].value(\"code\", \"\") == \"credits_exhausted\") {\nAgent/ProviderAgent.cpp:643:            return {\"credits_exhausted\", answer[\"error\"].value(\"message\", \"\"), false, details.dump()};\nAgent/AgentHost.cpp:2169:    // \"New Standard chat\" and \"New Expert chat\": the new chat is on that model,\nAgent/AgentHost.cpp:3047:    if (stream.message.error->code == \"credits_exhausted\")\nAgentUI/src/PreferencesApp.test.tsx:119:    expect(screen.getByTestId('first-month-offer')).toHaveTextContent('That is 500 Standard or 100 Expert messages. Your own API k\nAgentUI/src/WelcomeApp.test.tsx:136:      expect(box).toHaveTextContent('750 credits a month: 750 Standard or 150 Expert messages.');\nAgentUI/src/bridge/protocol.ts:123:  // A gateway refusal's own numbers; basic_only_credits on credits_exhausted.\nAgentUI/src/bridge/protocol.ts:124:  details?: { basic_only_credits?: number };\nAgentUI/src/bridge/protocol.ts:258:  basic_only?: boolean;\nAgentUI/src/bridge/protocol.ts:268:    unlimited_basic: boolean;\nAgentUI/src/bridge/protocol.ts:269:    basic_used_this_term?: number;\nAgentUI/src/bridge/protocol.ts:270:    basic_fair_use?: number;\nAgentUI/src/components/AgentConnection.tsx:40:        <p>That is 500 Standard or 100 Expert messages. Your own API key stays free.</p>\nAgentUI/src/components/WelcomeBack.tsx:136:        <p>750 credits a month: 750 Standard or 150 Expert messages.</p>\nAgentUI/src/components/MessageList.tsx:398:              {message.error.code === 'credits_exhausted' && creditActions && <>\nAgentUI/src/components/MessageList.tsx:401:                {(message.error.details?.basic_only_credits ?? 0) >= 5 &&\nAgentUI/src/components/MessageList.tsx:402:                  <button className=\"secondary\" onClick={creditActions.onNewStandardChat}>New Standard chat</button>}\nAgentUI/src/components/Composer.tsx:47:  // \"About 5 Expert messages left\" is said once: it stands until the person\nAgentUI/src/components/Composer.tsx:290:          {block.offerStandardChat && <button type=\"button\" className=\"link\" onClick={() => newChatOn('basic')}>New Standard chat<\nHomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx:114:            <p>That is 500 Standard or 100 Expert messages. Your own API key stays free.</p>\nHomeUI/src/App.test.tsx:473:    expect(screen.getByText('That is 500 Standard or 100 Expert messages. Your own API key stays free.')).toBeInTheDocument();\n../../../../resources/jusprin/agent/index.html:46:`+s.stack}return{value:e,source:t,stack:i,digest:null}}function cl(e,t,n){return{value:e,source:null,stack:n??null,diges\n../../../../resources/jusprin/agent/index.html:81:`);return{before:t.slice(0,n+1),line:t.slice(n+1)}}function ey(e){const{before:t,line:n}=Zg(e),r=Xg.exec(n);if(!r)return\n../../../../resources/jusprin/agent/index.html:375:What should we do with this in the current project?`;w.send(\"switch_conversation\",{conversationId:o.activeConversationI\n../../../../resources/jusprin/home/index.html:47:`).toLocaleLowerCase().includes(t.toLocaleLowerCase()):!0}function Dp(e,t=new Date){const n=new Date(e);if(Number.isNaN(n\n../../../../tests/agent/test_cloud_account.cpp:554:    const json body = json::parse(R\"({\"type\":\"error\",\"error\":{\"code\":\"credits_exhausted\",\"message\":\"This message needs \n../../../../tests/agent/test_cloud_account.cpp:555:                                      \"balance\":3,\"cost\":5,\"basic_only_credits\":49,\"affordable_aliases\":[\"slicer-basic\"\n../../../../tests/agent/test_cloud_account.cpp:560:    CHECK(event->error->code == \"credits_exhausted\");\n../../../../tests/agent/test_cloud_account.cpp:563:    CHECK(json::parse(event->error->details)[\"basic_only_credits\"] == 49);\n../../../../tests/agent/test_agent_bridge.cpp:2451:            events.push_back(AgentEvent::failed(AgentError{\"credits_exhausted\", \"This message needs 5 credits; you have\n../../../../tests/agent/test_agent_bridge.cpp:2452:                                                           R\"({\"balance\":3,\"cost\":5,\"basic_only_credits\":49})\"}));\n../../../../tests/agent/test_agent_bridge.cpp:2489:    CHECK((*failed)[\"payload\"][\"error\"][\"details\"][\"basic_only_credits\"] == 49);","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Am1JZ74fz1vu2NjYvhacfz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// What the account's credits mean for the chat in front of the person: what\n2\t// can pay for its model, whether the next message can be paid, and the words\n3\t// for a price. The gateway keeps the ledger and still decides; this only lets\n4\t// the page say so before sending.\n5\t\n6\timport { ChatModelChoice, CreditAccount, ModelCatalogPayload, ModelOptionInfo } from './bridge/protocol';\n7\t\n8\texport type Tier = 'basic' | 'expert';\n9\t\n10\tconst plural = (count: number, one: string, many: string) => `${count} ${count === 1 ? one : many}`;\n11\t\n12\texport const creditCount = (count: number) => plural(count, 'credit', 'credits');\n13\t\n14\t// Free Standard messages only pay for Standard, so Expert leaves them out.\n15\texport function basicOnlyCredits(account: CreditAccount): number {\n16\t  return account.credits.lots.reduce((sum, lot) => sum + (lot.basic_only ? lot.credits : 0), 0);\n17\t}\n18\t\n19\texport function spendable(account: CreditAccount, tier: string): number {\n20\t  return tier === 'expert' ? account.credits.total - basicOnlyCredits(account) : account.credits.total;\n21\t}\n22\t\n23\t// Workshop's Standard messages cost nothing up to the plan's fair-use count.\n24\tfunction basicFreeOnPlan(account: CreditAccount): boolean {\n25\t  const { plan } = account;\n26\t  return !!plan?.unlimited_basic && (plan.basic_used_this_term ?? 0) < (plan.basic_fair_use ?? 0);\n27\t}\n28\t\n29\t// A Standard message is \"free this month\" while something other than the\n30\t// person's own credits pays for it.\n31\texport function basicFree(account: CreditAccount | null | undefined): boolean {\n32\t  return !!account && (basicFreeOnPlan(account) || basicOnlyCredits(account) > 0);\n33\t}\n34\t\n35\texport function priceWords(model: ModelOptionInfo, account: CreditAccount | null | undefined): string | undefined {\n36\t  if (model.credits === undefined) return undefined;\n37\t  if (model.tier === 'basic' && basicFree(account)) return 'free this month';\n38\t  return `${creditCount(model.credits)} a message`;\n39\t}\n40\t\n41\t// The second sentence on the greyed pickers' tooltip.\n42\texport function messageCostSentence(model: ModelOptionInfo | undefined, account: CreditAccount | null | undefined): string | undefined {\n43\t  if (model?.credits === undefined) return undefined;\n44\t  if (model.tier === 'basic' && basicFree(account)) return 'Each message you send in this chat is free this month.';\n45\t  return `Each message you send in this chat costs ${creditCount(model.credits)}.`;\n46\t}\n47\t\n48\tconst TIER_NAMES: Record<string, string> = { basic: 'Standard', expert: 'Expert' };\n49\t\n50\texport interface SendBlock {\n51\t  sentence: string;\n52\t  // Free Standard messages are left that this chat's model cannot spend.\n53\t  offerStandardChat: boolean;\n54\t}\n55\t\n56\t// Why the next message of this chat cannot be paid, or nothing when it can.\n57\texport function sendBlock(account: CreditAccount | null | undefined, model: ModelOptionInfo | undefined): SendBlock | undefined {\n58\t  if (!account || !model || model.credits === undefined || !model.tier) return undefined;\n59\t  if (model.tier === 'basic' && basicFreeOnPlan(account)) return undefined;\n60\t  const available = spendable(account, model.tier);\n61\t  if (available >= model.credits) return undefined;\n62\t  const name = TIER_NAMES[model.tier] ?? model.label;\n63\t  // Under 5 there is no point in a new Standard chat: it would run out within\n64\t  // a few messages.\n65\t  if (model.tier === 'expert' && basicOnlyCredits(account) >= 5)\n66\t    return { sentence: `This ${name} chat needs ${creditCount(model.credits)} a message. Your free Standard messages can only pay for Standard.`,\n67\t      offerStandardChat: true };\n68\t  return { sentence: `You have ${creditCount(available)}; this ${name} chat needs ${model.credits} a message.`, offerStandardChat: false };\n69\t}\n70\t\n71\t// \"About 5 Expert messages left\", once the balance is under one session's\n72\t// worth of the chat's model. A session of about five messages is the design's\n73\t// placeholder (from four harness sessions, not from engaged use).\n74\tconst LOW_MESSAGES = 5;\n75\t\n76\texport function lowNotice(account: CreditAccount | null | undefined, model: ModelOptionInfo | undefined): string | undefined {\n77\t  if (!account || !model || model.credits === undefined || !model.tier) return undefined;\n78\t  if (model.tier === 'basic' && basicFree(account)) return undefined;\n79\t  const messages = Math.floor(spendable(account, model.tier) / model.credits);\n80\t  if (messages < 1 || messages > LOW_MESSAGES) return undefined;\n81\t  return `About ${plural(messages, `${TIER_NAMES[model.tier] ?? model.label} message`, `${TIER_NAMES[model.tier] ?? model.label} messages`)} left`;\n82\t}\n83\t\n84\texport function aliasOfTier(catalog: ModelCatalogPayload | undefined, tier: Tier): ChatModelChoice | undefined {\n85\t  for (const provider of catalog?.providers ?? [])\n86\t    for (const model of provider.models)\n87\t      if (model.tier === tier)\n88\t        return { provider: provider.id, model: model.id, effort: model.defaultEffort ?? '' };\n89\t  return undefined;\n90\t}\n91\t\n92\texport function tierPrice(catalog: ModelCatalogPayload | undefined, tier: Tier): number | undefined {\n93\t  for (const provider of catalog?.providers ?? [])\n94\t    for (const model of provider.models)\n95\t      if (model.tier === tier && model.credits !== undefined)\n96\t        return model.credits;\n97\t  return undefined;\n98\t}\n99\t"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjPSpnNUVehuyJD5dfGxGS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// The composer's credits ring and the panel it opens (board 2a on the \"JusPrin\n2\t// v2\" canvas): a small ring of what is left, no number and no animation;\n3\t// hovering or tapping opens the total, translated into messages, then a bar per\n4\t// kind of credit that expires, soonest first. Credits that never expire have no\n5\t// limit to measure against, so they are a plain number.\n6\t//\n7\t// What the ring measures against is open (plan decision 13): the sum of what\n8\t// each lot started with, the board's placeholder.\n9\t\n10\timport { useEffect, useRef, useState } from 'react';\n11\timport { CreditAccount, CreditLot } from '../bridge/protocol';\n12\timport { basicOnlyCredits, creditCount, spendable } from '../credits';\n13\t\n14\tconst RING = 16;\n15\tconst STROKE = 3;\n16\t\n17\tfunction shortDate(iso: string): string {\n18\t  return new Date(iso).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'short' });\n19\t}\n20\t\n21\tfunction lotName(lot: CreditLot, account: CreditAccount): string {\n22\t  switch (lot.kind) {\n23\t    case 'signup': return 'First-month credits';\n24\t    case 'trickle': return 'Free Standard messages';\n25\t    case 'subscription': return `${account.plan?.name ?? 'Plan'} credits`;\n26\t    case 'pack': return 'Bought credits';\n27\t    // What to call a reward is open (plan decision 13).\n28\t    case 'reward': return 'Report credits';\n29\t    default: return 'Credits';\n30\t  }\n31\t}\n32\t\n33\tinterface Row { key: string; name: string; left: number; of?: number; date: string }\n34\t\n35\tfunction rows(account: CreditAccount): Row[] {\n36\t  const expiring: (Row & { at: string })[] = [];\n37\t  const never = new Map<string, number>();\n38\t  for (const lot of account.credits.lots) {\n39\t    if (lot.expires_at) {\n40\t      expiring.push({ key: `${lot.kind}-${lot.expires_at}`, name: lotName(lot, account), left: lot.credits, of: lot.granted, at: lot.expires_at,\n41\t        date: `${lot.kind === 'trickle' ? 'Resets' : 'Expires'} ${shortDate(lot.expires_at)}` });\n42\t    } else if (lot.credits > 0) {\n43\t      const name = lotName(lot, account);\n44\t      never.set(name, (never.get(name) ?? 0) + lot.credits);\n45\t    }\n46\t  }\n47\t  const { plan } = account;\n48\t  if (plan?.unlimited_basic && plan.basic_fair_use && plan.renews_at) {\n49\t    const left = Math.max(plan.basic_fair_use - (plan.basic_used_this_term ?? 0), 0);\n50\t    expiring.push({ key: 'fair-use', name: 'Free Standard messages', left, of: plan.basic_fair_use, at: plan.renews_at,\n51\t      date: `Resets ${shortDate(plan.renews_at)}. After ${plan.basic_fair_use}, Standard is 1 credit a message until then.` });\n52\t  }\n53\t  expiring.sort((a, b) => a.at.localeCompare(b.at));\n54\t  return [...expiring, ...[...never].map(([name, left]) => ({ key: name, name, left, date: 'Never expire' }))];\n55\t}\n56\t\n57\t// The ring's share: what is left of what the lots started with.\n58\texport function ringShare(account: CreditAccount): number {\n59\t  const started = account.credits.lots.reduce((sum, lot) => sum + lot.granted, 0);\n60\t  return started > 0 ? Math.min(account.credits.total / started, 1) : 0;\n61\t}\n62\t\n63\tfunction Ring({ share, low }: { share: number; low: boolean }) {\n64\t  const radius = (RING - STROKE) / 2;\n65\t  const circumference = 2 * Math.PI * radius;\n66\t  return <svg className={low ? 'credit-ring credit-ring--low' : 'credit-ring'} viewBox={`0 0 ${RING} ${RING}`} aria-hidden=\"true\">\n67\t    <circle className=\"credit-ring-track\" cx={RING / 2} cy={RING / 2} r={radius} fill=\"none\" strokeWidth={STROKE} />\n68\t    <circle className=\"credit-ring-fill\" cx={RING / 2} cy={RING / 2} r={radius} fill=\"none\" strokeWidth={STROKE}\n69\t      strokeDasharray={`${share * circumference} ${circumference}`} transform={`rotate(-90 ${RING / 2} ${RING / 2})`} />\n70\t  </svg>;\n71\t}\n72\t\n73\texport function BalancePanel({ account, expertPrice, low, onGetMore, onSeeUsage }: {\n74\t  account: CreditAccount;\n75\t  expertPrice: number;\n76\t  low: boolean;\n77\t  onGetMore: () => void;\n78\t  onSeeUsage: () => void;\n79\t}) {\n80\t  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);\n81\t  const closing = useRef<ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null>(null);\n82\t  useEffect(() => () => { if (closing.current !== null) clearTimeout(closing.current); }, []);\n83\t  const keepOpen = () => {\n84\t    if (closing.current !== null) clearTimeout(closing.current);\n85\t    closing.current = null;\n86\t    setOpen(true);\n87\t  };\n88\t  // The pointer crosses a gap on its way from the ring to the panel's actions.\n89\t  const closeSoon = () => { closing.current = setTimeout(() => setOpen(false), 200); };\n90\t\n91\t  const total = account.credits.total;\n92\t  const expert = Math.floor(spendable(account, 'expert') / expertPrice);\n93\t  return <div className=\"credit-balance\" onMouseEnter={keepOpen} onMouseLeave={closeSoon}\n94\t    onKeyDown={(event) => { if (event.key === 'Escape') setOpen(false); }}>\n95\t    <button type=\"button\" className=\"credit-ring-button\" aria-label=\"Credits left\" aria-expanded={open}\n96\t      onClick={keepOpen}>\n97\t      <Ring share={ringShare(account)} low={low} />\n98\t    </button>\n99\t    {open && <div className=\"credit-panel\" role=\"dialog\" aria-label=\"Credits\">\n100\t      <div className=\"credit-panel-total\">\n101\t        <strong>{creditCount(total)} left</strong>\n102\t        <span>That is {total} Standard or {expert} Expert {expert === 1 ? 'message' : 'messages'}.</span>\n103\t      </div>\n104\t      <div className=\"credit-panel-lots\">\n105\t        {rows(account).map((row) => <div key={row.key} className=\"credit-lot\">\n106\t          <div className=\"credit-lot-line\">\n107\t            <strong>{row.name}</strong>\n108\t            <span>{row.of === undefined ? `${row.left} left` : `${row.left} of ${row.of} left`}</span>\n109\t          </div>\n110\t          {row.of !== undefined && <div className=\"credit-lot-bar\">\n111\t            <div className=\"credit-lot-fill\" style={{ width: `${row.of > 0 ? Math.min(row.left / row.of, 1) * 100 : 0}%` }} />\n112\t          </div>}\n113\t          <span className=\"credit-lot-date\">{row.date}</span>\n114\t        </div>)}\n115\t        <p className=\"credit-panel-rule\">Expiring credits are used first.</p>\n116\t      </div>\n117\t      <div className=\"credit-panel-actions\">\n118\t        <button type=\"button\" className=\"link\" onClick={onGetMore}>Get more credits</button>\n119\t        <button type=\"button\" className=\"link\" onClick={onSeeUsage}>See usage</button>\n120\t      </div>\n121\t    </div>}\n122\t  </div>;\n123\t}\n124\t\n125\t// A person with only free Standard messages has no balance on the toolbar\n126\t// (boards 3d and 6a); the message box says what is there instead.\n127\texport function showsRing(account: CreditAccount): boolean {\n128\t  return account.credits.total > basicOnlyCredits(account);\n129\t}\n130\t"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014ZH4FT7fGCyk9uiXiktJbs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// The credits ring and the panel it opens: the translated total, a bar per kind\n2\t// of credit that expires, soonest first, and the plain number for credits that\n3\t// never do (board 2a).\n4\t\n5\timport { cleanup, render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';\n6\timport userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event';\n7\timport { afterEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest';\n8\timport { CreditAccount } from '../bridge/protocol';\n9\timport { BalancePanel, ringShare, showsRing } from './BalancePanel';\n10\t\n11\tafterEach(cleanup);\n12\t\n13\tconst board2a: CreditAccount = {\n14\t  credits: {\n15\t    total: 612,\n16\t    lots: [\n17\t      { kind: 'pack', credits: 500, granted: 500, expires_at: null },\n18\t      { kind: 'trickle', credits: 50, granted: 50, expires_at: '2026-12-01T12:00:00+00:00', basic_only: true },\n19\t      { kind: 'signup', credits: 62, granted: 500, expires_at: '2026-11-30T12:00:00+00:00' },\n20\t    ],\n21\t  },\n22\t  plan: null,\n23\t  v1_subscription: null,\n24\t};\n25\t\n26\tfunction open(account: CreditAccount, onGetMore = vi.fn(), onSeeUsage = vi.fn()) {\n27\t  render(<BalancePanel account={account} expertPrice={5} low={false} onGetMore={onGetMore} onSeeUsage={onSeeUsage} />);\n28\t  return userEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Credits left' }));\n29\t}\n30\t\n31\tdescribe('the balance panel', () => {\n32\t  it('shows no number until it is opened', () => {\n33\t    render(<BalancePanel account={board2a} expertPrice={5} low={false} onGetMore={vi.fn()} onSeeUsage={vi.fn()} />);\n34\t    expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Credits left' })).toHaveTextContent('');\n35\t    expect(screen.queryByText(/credits left/)).toBeNull();\n36\t  });\n37\t\n38\t  it('translates the total, leaving free Standard messages out of the Expert count', async () => {\n39\t    await open(board2a);\n40\t    expect(screen.getByText('612 credits left')).toBeTruthy();\n41\t    expect(screen.getByText('That is 612 Standard or 112 Expert messages.')).toBeTruthy();\n42\t  });\n43\t\n44\t  it('lists what expires soonest first and never-expiring credits as a plain number', async () => {\n45\t    await open(board2a);\n46\t    const rows = [...document.querySelectorAll('.credit-lot')].map((row) => row.textContent);\n47\t    expect(rows).toEqual([\n48\t      'First-month credits62 of 500 leftExpires 30 Nov',\n49\t      'Free Standard messages50 of 50 leftResets 1 Dec',\n50\t      'Bought credits500 leftNever expire',\n51\t    ]);\n52\t    expect(document.querySelectorAll('.credit-lot-bar')).toHaveLength(2);\n53\t    expect(screen.getByText('Expiring credits are used first.')).toBeTruthy();\n54\t  });\n55\t\n56\t  it('offers Get more credits and See usage', async () => {\n57\t    const onGetMore = vi.fn();\n58\t    const onSeeUsage = vi.fn();\n59\t    await open(board2a, onGetMore, onSeeUsage);\n60\t    await userEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Get more credits' }));\n61\t    await userEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'See usage' }));\n62\t    expect(onGetMore).toHaveBeenCalledOnce();\n63\t    expect(onSeeUsage).toHaveBeenCalledOnce();\n64\t  });\n65\t\n66\t  it('shows Workshop’s fair-use count as one more bar', async () => {\n67\t    await open({\n68\t      credits: { total: 1500, lots: [{ kind: 'subscription', credits: 1500, granted: 1500, expires_at: '2026-12-01T12:00:00+00:00' }] },\n69\t      plan: { id: 'workshop', name: 'Workshop', renews_at: '2026-12-01T12:00:00+00:00', unlimited_basic: true,\n70\t        basic_used_this_term: 412, basic_fair_use: 600 },\n71\t      v1_subscription: null,\n72\t    });\n73\t    expect(screen.getByText('Workshop credits')).toBeTruthy();\n74\t    expect(screen.getByText('188 of 600 left')).toBeTruthy();\n75\t    expect(screen.getByText('Resets 1 Dec. After 600, Standard is 1 credit a message until then.')).toBeTruthy();\n76\t  });\n77\t\n78\t  it('measures the ring against what the lots started with', () => {\n79\t    expect(ringShare(board2a)).toBeCloseTo(612 / 1050);\n80\t  });\n81\t\n82\t  it('is left off when only free Standard messages remain', () => {\n83\t    expect(showsRing(board2a)).toBe(true);\n84\t    expect(showsRing({ ...board2a, credits: { total: 50, lots: [board2a.credits.lots[1]] } })).toBe(false);\n85\t  });\n86\t});\n87\t"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018ownXF4GecNUY9JbBkdLmr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// The message box with an account: prices in the model menu, greyed pickers once\n2\t// the person has sent a message, Send held back when the next message cannot be\n3\t// paid, and a picture a Standard chat would not send (boards 2b, 2c, 3a, 3b, 3d, 3e).\n4\t\n5\timport { cleanup, render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';\n6\timport userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event';\n7\timport { afterEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest';\n8\timport { AttachmentInfo, ChatModelChoice, CreditAccount, ModelCatalogPayload } from '../bridge/protocol';\n9\timport { messageCostSentence, priceWords, sendBlock } from '../credits';\n10\timport { Composer, ComposerCredits } from './Composer';\n11\timport { modelMenu } from './ModelPickers';\n12\t\n13\tafterEach(cleanup);\n14\t\n15\tconst standard = { id: 'slicer-basic', label: 'Standard', efforts: ['fast', 'thorough'], defaultEffort: 'fast', tier: 'basic', credits: 1, images: false };\n16\tconst expert = { id: 'slicer-1', label: 'Expert', efforts: ['fast', 'thorough'], defaultEffort: 'thorough', tier: 'expert', credits: 5 };\n17\tconst own = { id: 'gpt-5.4', label: 'gpt-5.4', efforts: [] };\n18\tconst catalog: ModelCatalogPayload = {\n19\t  defaultProvider: 'jusprin',\n20\t  providers: [\n21\t    { id: 'jusprin', label: 'JusPrin', defaultModel: 'slicer-1', state: 'ready', models: [standard, expert] },\n22\t    { id: 'openai', label: 'OpenAI', defaultModel: 'gpt-5.4', state: 'ready', models: [own] },\n23\t  ],\n24\t};\n25\tconst onExpert: ChatModelChoice = { provider: 'jusprin', model: 'slicer-1', effort: 'thorough' };\n26\tconst onStandard: ChatModelChoice = { provider: 'jusprin', model: 'slicer-basic', effort: 'fast' };\n27\tconst onOwn: ChatModelChoice = { provider: 'openai', model: 'gpt-5.4', effort: '' };\n28\t\n29\tconst lot = (kind: string, credits: number, basicOnly = false) => ({\n30\t  kind, credits, granted: credits, expires_at: '2026-12-01T12:00:00+00:00', ...(basicOnly ? { basic_only: true } : {}),\n31\t});\n32\tconst balance = (...lots: ReturnType<typeof lot>[]): CreditAccount => ({\n33\t  credits: { total: lots.reduce((sum, one) => sum + one.credits, 0), lots },\n34\t  plan: null,\n35\t  v1_subscription: null,\n36\t});\n37\t\n38\tfunction credits(account: CreditAccount | null, extra: Partial<ComposerCredits> = {}): ComposerCredits {\n39\t  return { account, lowNoticeSeen: () => false, onLowNoticeSeen: vi.fn(), onGetMore: vi.fn(), onSeeUsage: vi.fn(), onNewChat: vi.fn(), ...extra };\n40\t}\n41\t\n42\tfunction renderComposer(props: {\n43\t  account?: CreditAccount | null; choice?: ChatModelChoice; started?: boolean; text?: string;\n44\t  attachments?: AttachmentInfo[]; composerCredits?: ComposerCredits; onSend?: (text: string) => void;\n45\t}) {\n46\t  render(<Composer disabled={false} streaming={false} attachments={props.attachments ?? []} initialText={props.text}\n47\t    started={props.started} onSend={props.onSend ?? vi.fn()} onStop={vi.fn()} onAttachFiles={vi.fn()} onRemoveAttachment={vi.fn()}\n48\t    models={catalog} chatModel={props.choice ?? onExpert} onChooseModel={vi.fn()}\n49\t    credits={props.composerCredits ?? credits(props.account ?? balance(lot('signup', 500)))} />);\n50\t}\n51\t\n52\tconst send = () => screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Send message' });\n53\t\n54\tdescribe('prices', () => {\n55\t  it('always carry \"a message\", and only on the account’s models', () => {\n56\t    const entries = modelMenu(catalog, onExpert, vi.fn(), balance(lot('signup', 500)));\n57\t    expect(entries.flatMap((entry) => ('section' in entry ? [] : [[entry.label, entry.detail]]))).toEqual([\n58\t      ['Standard · 1 credit a message', 'setting up an ordinary print'],\n59\t      ['Expert · 5 credits a message', 'troubleshooting, tricky models, anything you’d ask a person'],\n60\t      ['gpt-5.4', undefined],\n61\t    ]);\n62\t  });\n63\t\n64\t  it('read \"free this month\" while free Standard messages last', () => {\n65\t    const account = balance(lot('trickle', 50, true));\n66\t    expect(priceWords(standard, account)).toBe('free this month');\n67\t    expect(priceWords(expert, account)).toBe('5 credits a message');\n68\t    expect(messageCostSentence(standard, account)).toBe('Each message you send in this chat is free this month.');\n69\t    expect(messageCostSentence(expert, account)).toBe('Each message you send in this chat costs 5 credits.');\n70\t    expect(messageCostSentence(own, account)).toBeUndefined();\n71\t  });\n72\t});\n73\t\n74\tdescribe('the pickers', () => {\n75\t  it('work until the person sends a message', () => {\n76\t    renderComposer({});\n77\t    expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /^Model/ })).toBeEnabled();\n78\t    expect(screen.queryByRole('tooltip', { hidden: true })).toBeNull();\n79\t  });\n80\t\n81\t  it('are greyed afterwards and say why and what a message costs', () => {\n82\t    renderComposer({ started: true });\n83\t    expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /^Model/ })).toBeDisabled();\n84\t    expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /^Thinking/ })).toBeDisabled();\n85\t    const tooltip = screen.getByRole('tooltip', { hidden: true });\n86\t    expect(tooltip).toHaveTextContent('A chat keeps the model and thinking level it started with. Start a new chat to change them.');\n87\t    expect(tooltip).toHaveTextContent('Each message you send in this chat costs 5 credits.');\n88\t  });\n89\t\n90\t  it('name no price on the person’s own key, and draw no ring', () => {\n91\t    renderComposer({ started: true, choice: onOwn });\n92\t    const tooltip = screen.getByRole('tooltip', { hidden: true });\n93\t    expect(tooltip).toHaveTextContent('A chat keeps the model');\n94\t    expect(tooltip).not.toHaveTextContent('credit');\n95\t    expect(screen.queryByRole('button', { name: 'Credits left' })).toBeNull();\n96\t  });\n97\t});\n98\t\n99\tdescribe('the check before sending', () => {\n100\t  it('leaves Send alone when the message can be paid', () => {\n101\t    renderComposer({ text: 'Hello', account: balance(lot('signup', 5)) });\n102\t    expect(send()).toBeEnabled();\n103\t    expect(screen.queryByRole('button', { name: 'Get more credits' })).toBeNull();\n104\t  });\n105\t\n106\t  it('disables Send, says why, offers one action and keeps the words', () => {\n107\t    const composerCredits = credits(balance(lot('pack', 3)));\n108\t    renderComposer({ text: 'The tip curled up', composerCredits });\n109\t    expect(send()).toBeDisabled();\n110\t    expect(screen.getByText('You have 3 credits; this Expert chat needs 5 a message.')).toBeTruthy();\n111\t    expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Get more credits' })).toBeTruthy();\n112\t    expect(screen.queryByRole('button', { name: 'New Standard chat' })).toBeNull();\n113\t    expect(screen.getByRole('textbox')).toHaveValue('The tip curled up');\n114\t  });\n115\t\n116\t  it('adds New Standard chat only when free Standard messages are what is left', async () => {\n117\t    const composerCredits = credits(balance(lot('trickle', 50, true)));\n118\t    renderComposer({ text: 'The tip curled up', composerCredits });\n119\t    expect(send()).toBeDisabled();\n120\t    expect(screen.getByText('This Expert chat needs 5 credits a message. Your free Standard messages can only pay for Standard.')).toBeTruthy();\n121\t    await userEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'New Standard chat' }));\n122\t    expect(composerCredits.onNewChat).toHaveBeenCalledWith(onStandard, 'The tip curled up');\n123\t  });\n124\t\n125\t  it('offers no New Standard chat under 5 credits', () => {\n126\t    expect(sendBlock(balance(lot('trickle', 4, true)), expert)).toEqual({\n127\t      sentence: 'You have 0 credits; this Expert chat needs 5 a message.', offerStandardChat: false });\n128\t  });\n129\t\n130\t  it('lets free Standard messages pay for a Standard chat', () => {\n131\t    expect(sendBlock(balance(lot('trickle', 4, true)), standard)).toBeUndefined();\n132\t  });\n133\t\n134\t  it('never blocks a model on the person’s own key', () => {\n135\t    expect(sendBlock(balance(), own)).toBeUndefined();\n136\t  });\n137\t\n138\t  it('says once that few messages are left, in the warning colour', async () => {\n139\t    const seen = new Set<string>();\n140\t    const composerCredits = credits(balance(lot('pack', 25)), {\n141\t      lowNoticeSeen: (notice) => seen.has(notice),\n142\t      onLowNoticeSeen: (notice) => { seen.add(notice); },\n143\t    });\n144\t    const onSend = vi.fn();\n145\t    renderComposer({ text: 'Hello', composerCredits, onSend });\n146\t    expect(screen.getByText('About 5 Expert messages left')).toBeTruthy();\n147\t    expect(document.querySelector('.credit-ring--low')).toBeTruthy();\n148\t    await userEvent.click(send());\n149\t    expect(onSend).toHaveBeenCalledWith('Hello');\n150\t    expect(seen.has('About 5 Expert messages left')).toBe(true);\n151\t  });\n152\t});\n153\t\n154\tdescribe('a picture in a Standard chat', () => {\n155\t  const picture: AttachmentInfo = { id: 'a1', name: 'curl.jpg', kind: 'image', mime: 'image/jpeg', sizeBytes: 2048, state: 'staged', summary: '' } as AttachmentInfo;\n156\t\n157\t  it('says it will not be sent, with New Expert chat beside Remove, and Send stays enabled', async () => {\n158\t    const composerCredits = credits(balance(lot('signup', 500)));\n159\t    renderComposer({ text: 'Why?', choice: onStandard, attachments: [picture], composerCredits });\n160\t    expect(screen.getByText('Standard can’t see pictures, so this one will not be sent.')).toBeTruthy();\n161\t    expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Remove curl.jpg' })).toBeTruthy();\n162\t    expect(send()).toBeEnabled();\n163\t    await userEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'New Expert chat' }));\n164\t    expect(composerCredits.onNewChat).toHaveBeenCalledWith(onExpert, 'Why?');\n165\t  });\n166\t\n167\t  it('says nothing in an Expert chat', () => {\n168\t    renderComposer({ text: 'Why?', attachments: [picture] });\n169\t    expect(screen.queryByText(/can’t see pictures/)).toBeNull();\n170\t    expect(screen.queryByRole('button', { name: 'New Expert chat' })).toBeNull();\n171\t  });\n172\t});\n173\t"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PQk9ZVC9NhQKjKTAi3zvfH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// The composer's model and thinking pickers (the Composer proposal on the\n2\t// \"JusPrin v2\" canvas, states 5 to 8). The model menu lists every model of\n3\t// every provider with a key, under the provider's name when there is more\n4\t// than one; the thinking menu lists the levels the chosen model accepts and\n5\t// is left out when it accepts none. A choice belongs to the active chat and\n6\t// applies from its next turn. A model menu of more than SEARCH_FROM models\n7\t// (OpenRouter's runs to hundreds) starts with a search field, and a provider\n8\t// with that many shows its count beside its name.\n9\t//\n10\t// An account's models carry their price and what they are for; models on the\n11\t// person's own key name no price. A chat keeps the model and thinking level it\n12\t// started with, so once the person has sent a message both pickers are greyed,\n13\t// and hovering either says why and what a message costs.\n14\t\n15\timport { ChatModelChoice, CreditAccount, ModelCatalogPayload, ModelOptionInfo } from '../bridge/protocol';\n16\timport { messageCostSentence, priceWords } from '../credits';\n17\timport { ActionMenu, MenuItem, MenuSearch, MenuSection } from './ChatNavigation';\n18\t\n19\tconst EFFORT_LABELS: Record<string, string> = {\n20\t  none: 'Off', minimal: 'Minimal', low: 'Low', medium: 'Medium', high: 'High', xhigh: 'Extra high', max: 'Max',\n21\t  // JusPrin's own levels, which its gateway maps to the model's.\n22\t  fast: 'Fast', thorough: 'Thorough',\n23\t};\n24\t\n25\texport const SEARCH_FROM = 12;\n26\t\n27\tconst TIER_USES: Record<string, string> = {\n28\t  basic: 'setting up an ordinary print',\n29\t  expert: 'troubleshooting, tricky models, anything you’d ask a person',\n30\t};\n31\t\n32\tconst MODEL_SEARCH: MenuSearch = { label: 'Search models', noMatch: (query) => `No models match “${query}”.` };\n33\t\n34\texport function effortLabel(effort: string): string {\n35\t  return EFFORT_LABELS[effort] ?? effort;\n36\t}\n37\t\n38\t// The catalog's entry for the chosen model, if its list has arrived.\n39\texport function findModel(catalog: ModelCatalogPayload, choice: ChatModelChoice): ModelOptionInfo | undefined {\n40\t  return catalog.providers.find((provider) => provider.id === choice.provider)?.models\n41\t    .find((model) => model.id === choice.model);\n42\t}\n43\t\n44\t// Switching model keeps the thinking level when the new model has it, and\n45\t// otherwise leaves the level to the new model's default.\n46\texport function switchModel(choice: ChatModelChoice, provider: string, model: ModelOptionInfo): ChatModelChoice {\n47\t  return { provider, model: model.id, effort: model.efforts.includes(choice.effort) ? choice.effort : '' };\n48\t}\n49\t\n50\texport function modelMenu(catalog: ModelCatalogPayload, choice: ChatModelChoice,\n51\t  onChoose: (choice: ChatModelChoice) => void, account?: CreditAccount | null): (MenuItem | MenuSection)[] {\n52\t  const grouped = catalog.providers.length > 1;\n53\t  const entries: (MenuItem | MenuSection)[] = [];\n54\t  for (const provider of catalog.providers) {\n55\t    if (grouped)\n56\t      entries.push({ section: provider.label,\n57\t        detail: provider.models.length > SEARCH_FROM ? `${provider.models.length} models` : undefined });\n58\t    const models = [...provider.models];\n59\t    // The chat's model stays choosable even before its list arrives, or when\n60\t    // the list leaves it out.\n61\t    if (provider.id === choice.provider && !models.some((model) => model.id === choice.model))\n62\t      models.unshift({ id: choice.model, label: choice.model, efforts: [] });\n63\t    for (const model of models) {\n64\t      const price = priceWords(model, account);\n65\t      entries.push({\n66\t        key: `${provider.id}/${model.id}`,\n67\t        label: price ? `${model.label} · ${price}` : model.label,\n68\t        detail: model.tier ? TIER_USES[model.tier] : undefined,\n69\t        current: provider.id === choice.provider && model.id === choice.model,\n70\t        matches: [model.label, provider.label],\n71\t        onSelect: () => onChoose(switchModel(choice, provider.id, model)),\n72\t      });\n73\t    }\n74\t    if (provider.state === 'loading')\n75\t      entries.push({ key: `${provider.id}/loading`, label: 'Loading models…', disabled: true,\n76\t        matches: [provider.label], onSelect: () => {} });\n77\t    if (provider.state === 'failed')\n78\t      entries.push({ key: `${provider.id}/failed`, label: 'Couldn’t load the model list', disabled: true,\n79\t        matches: [provider.label], onSelect: () => {} });\n80\t  }\n81\t  return entries;\n82\t}\n83\t\n84\texport function ModelPickers({ catalog, choice, disabled, locked = false, account, onChoose }: {\n85\t  catalog: ModelCatalogPayload;\n86\t  choice: ChatModelChoice;\n87\t  disabled: boolean;\n88\t  // The person has sent a message in this chat.\n89\t  locked?: boolean;\n90\t  account?: CreditAccount | null;\n91\t  onChoose: (choice: ChatModelChoice) => void;\n92\t}) {\n93\t  const model = findModel(catalog, choice);\n94\t  const efforts = model?.efforts ?? [];\n95\t  // An unset level shows the model's own default where the provider names\n96\t  // it; where it does not, it reads \"Default\".\n97\t  const shownEffort = choice.effort || model?.defaultEffort || '';\n98\t  const models = modelMenu(catalog, choice, onChoose, account);\n99\t  const cost = messageCostSentence(model, account);\n100\t  const priced = catalog.providers.some((provider) => provider.models.some((option) => option.credits !== undefined));\n101\t  const modelCount = models.filter((entry) => !('section' in entry) && !entry.disabled).length;\n102\t  // Only the model picker gives up width in a narrow pane; the thinking\n103\t  // picker drops its \"Thinking:\" instead (Composer measures which).\n104\t  return <div className={locked ? 'composer-pickers composer-pickers--locked' : 'composer-pickers'}>\n105\t    <ActionMenu label=\"Model\" className={priced ? 'composer-model-menu composer-model-menu--priced' : 'composer-model-menu'}\n106\t      text={model?.label ?? choice.model} above\n107\t      disabled={disabled || locked} items={models} search={modelCount > SEARCH_FROM ? MODEL_SEARCH : undefined} />\n108\t    {efforts.length > 0 && <ActionMenu label=\"Thinking\" above disabled={disabled || locked} prefixed\n109\t      text={shownEffort ? effortLabel(shownEffort) : 'Default'}\n110\t      items={efforts.map((effort) => ({\n111\t        key: effort,\n112\t        label: effortLabel(effort),\n113\t        current: effort === shownEffort,\n114\t        onSelect: () => onChoose({ ...choice, effort }),\n115\t      }))} />}\n116\t    {locked && <div className=\"composer-pickers-tooltip\" role=\"tooltip\">\n117\t      <p>A chat keeps the model and thinking level it started with. Start a new chat to change them.</p>\n118\t      {cost && <p>{cost}</p>}\n119\t    </div>}\n120\t  </div>;\n121\t}\n122\t"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WxDVY3tZtxjy61jMcxQ93Y","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// The welcome-back window: what JusPrin copied from JusPrin v1 on this\n2\t// computer, and the JusPrin account v1 was signed in to (canvas \"JusPrin v2\",\n3\t// onboarding page, row \"When JusPrin v1 is on this computer\": V1-01 imported,\n4\t// V1-02 partly imported, V1-03 sign-in expired). Shown once, after the first\n5\t// start that imported it.\n6\t\n7\timport { useEffect, useRef, useState } from 'react';\n8\timport { AccountStatusPayload, CreditAccount, SavedKeyInfo, WelcomeBackPayload } from '../bridge/protocol';\n9\timport { FirstMonthOffer } from './AgentConnection';\n10\t\n11\texport interface WelcomeBackActions {\n12\t  checkAccount: () => void;\n13\t  signIn: () => void;\n14\t  cancelSignIn: () => void;\n15\t  close: () => void;\n16\t}\n17\t\n18\texport interface WelcomeBackProps {\n19\t  report: WelcomeBackPayload;\n20\t  // The account v1 was signed in to, from setup_keys; absent when v1 was not.\n21\t  account?: SavedKeyInfo;\n22\t  status: AccountStatusPayload;\n23\t  actions: WelcomeBackActions;\n24\t  // The JusPrin v1 subscription the person keeps the price of, once the\n25\t  // account has been read (board 1d).\n26\t  subscription?: CreditAccount['v1_subscription'];\n27\t  priceCarriesOver?: boolean;\n28\t}\n29\t\n30\t// Billing moves JusPrin v1 subscribers to Hobby at their original price in\n31\t// step 3 of the pricing plan. Until it does, nothing here promises that price,\n32\t// whatever the account reports.\n33\tconst V1_PRICE_CARRIES_OVER = false;\n34\t\n35\t// \"Generic PLA, Silk PETG, 0.20 mm Strong and 7 more\".\n36\tfunction someOf(names: string[], shown: number, separator: string): string {\n37\t  if (names.length <= shown) return names.join(separator);\n38\t  return `${names.slice(0, shown).join(separator)} and ${names.length - shown} more`;\n39\t}\n40\t\n41\tfunction ImportedRow({ title, detail, count, partial = false }: {\n42\t  title: string; detail: string; count?: string; partial?: boolean;\n43\t}) {\n44\t  return (\n45\t    <div className=\"welcome-row\">\n46\t      <span className={`jp-icon ${partial ? 'jp-icon-triangle-alert welcome-icon--warning' : 'jp-icon-check welcome-icon--done'}`}\n47\t        aria-hidden=\"true\" />\n48\t      <div className=\"welcome-row-copy\">\n49\t        <span className=\"welcome-row-title\">{title}</span>\n50\t        <span className=\"welcome-row-detail\">{detail}</span>\n51\t      </div>\n52\t      {count && <span className=\"welcome-row-count\">{count}</span>}\n53\t    </div>\n54\t  );\n55\t}\n56\t\n57\tfunction AccountBox({ account, status, actions, priceCarriesOver }: Pick<WelcomeBackProps, 'account' | 'status' | 'actions' | 'priceCarriesOver'>) {\n58\t  const [copied, setCopied] = useState(false);\n59\t  if (status.phase === 'browser') {\n60\t    return (\n61\t      <div className=\"welcome-account\">\n62\t        <div className=\"welcome-account-line\">\n63\t          <div className=\"welcome-row-copy\">\n64\t            <span className=\"welcome-account-title\">Finish signing in in your browser</span>\n65\t            <span className=\"welcome-row-detail\">\n66\t              A JusPrin tab just opened. Sign in there, or create an account, and come back. This notices on its own.\n67\t            </span>\n68\t          </div>\n69\t          <button type=\"button\" className=\"link\" onClick={actions.cancelSignIn}>Cancel</button>\n70\t        </div>\n71\t        {status.url && (\n72\t          <p className=\"agent-row-note\">\n73\t            Didn’t open?{' '}\n74\t            <button type=\"button\" className=\"link\" onClick={() => {\n75\t              navigator.clipboard.writeText(status.url!).then(() => setCopied(true), () => setCopied(false));\n76\t            }}>{copied ? 'Link copied' : 'Copy link'}</button>\n77\t          </p>\n78\t        )}\n79\t      </div>\n80\t    );\n81\t  }\n82\t  if (status.phase === 'checking') {\n83\t    return (\n84\t      <div className=\"welcome-account\" data-testid=\"welcome-account\">\n85\t        <span className=\"welcome-account-title\">Checking your JusPrin v1 sign-in…</span>\n86\t      </div>\n87\t    );\n88\t  }\n89\t  if (account && !account.rejected) {\n90\t    return (\n91\t      <div className=\"welcome-account\" data-testid=\"welcome-account\">\n92\t        <div className=\"welcome-account-line\">\n93\t          <span className=\"jp-icon jp-icon-check welcome-icon--done\" aria-hidden=\"true\" />\n94\t          <div className=\"welcome-row-copy\">\n95\t            <span className=\"welcome-account-title\">{account.account ? `Signed in as ${account.account}` : 'Signed in'}</span>\n96\t            <span className=\"welcome-row-detail\">The same account you used in JusPrin v1</span>\n97\t          </div>\n98\t        </div>\n99\t      </div>\n100\t    );\n101\t  }\n102\t  // Until they sign in, a v1 subscriber can't be told from anyone else, so the\n103\t  // offer also says what signing in means for them (board 1c).\n104\t  if (!account) {\n105\t    return (\n106\t      <div className=\"welcome-offer\" data-testid=\"welcome-account\">\n107\t        <FirstMonthOffer note={priceCarriesOver ? \"Subscribed to JusPrin v1? You get these 500 credits and keep your original price, on the $10 Hobby plan.\" : undefined}\n108\t          onSignIn={actions.signIn} />\n109\t        {status.error && <p className=\"agent-key-error\" role=\"alert\">{status.error.message}</p>}\n110\t      </div>\n111\t    );\n112\t  }\n113\t  return (\n114\t    <div className=\"welcome-account\" data-testid=\"welcome-account\">\n115\t      <div className=\"welcome-account-line\">\n116\t        <span className=\"jp-icon jp-icon-triangle-alert welcome-icon--warning\" aria-hidden=\"true\" />\n117\t        <div className=\"welcome-row-copy\">\n118\t          <span className=\"welcome-account-title\">Sign in again to use the agent</span>\n119\t          <span className=\"welcome-row-detail\">\n120\t            {`Your JusPrin v1 sign-in${account.account ? ` for ${account.account}` : ''} has expired.`}\n121\t          </span>\n122\t        </div>\n123\t      </div>\n124\t      {status.error && <p className=\"agent-key-error\" role=\"alert\">{status.error.message}</p>}\n125\t      <button type=\"button\" className=\"secondary welcome-account-action\" onClick={actions.signIn}>Continue with JusPrin</button>\n126\t    </div>\n127\t  );\n128\t}\n129\t\n130\t// Nothing to choose and no upgrade prompt: they stay on the price they pay.\n131\tfunction KeptPrice({ subscription }: { subscription: NonNullable<CreditAccount['v1_subscription']> }) {\n132\t  return (\n133\t    <div className=\"credit-offer\" data-testid=\"welcome-kept-price\">\n134\t      <div className=\"credit-offer-copy\">\n135\t        <h2 className=\"credit-offer-title\">Hobby, at your original ${(subscription.cents / 100).toFixed(2)} a {subscription.period}</h2>\n136\t        <p>750 credits a month: 750 Standard or 150 Expert messages.</p>\n137\t        <p>Plus 500 more for your first month.</p>\n138\t        <p>New subscribers pay $10. You keep this price while subscribed.</p>\n139\t      </div>\n140\t    </div>\n141\t  );\n142\t}\n143\t\n144\texport function WelcomeBack({ report, account, status, actions, subscription, priceCarriesOver = V1_PRICE_CARRIES_OVER }: WelcomeBackProps) {\n145\t  // The sign-in v1 left is checked once, when the window opens: it may have\n146\t  // been revoked or ended since v1 last used it.\n147\t  const checked = useRef(false);\n148\t  useEffect(() => {\n149\t    if (account && !checked.current) {\n150\t      checked.current = true;\n151\t      actions.checkAccount();\n152\t    }\n153\t  }, [account, actions]);\n154\t\n155\t  const unusable = new Set(report.unusable);\n156\t  const usablePrinters = report.printers.filter((name) => !unusable.has(name));\n157\t  const usablePresets = report.presets.filter((name) => !unusable.has(name));\n158\t  const partial = report.unusable.length > 0 || report.failed.length > 0;\n159\t  const count = (usable: string[], all: string[]) => usable.length === all.length ? `${all.length}` : `${usable.length} of ${all.length}`;\n160\t\n161\t  return (\n162\t    <div className=\"welcome\" data-testid=\"welcome-back\">\n163\t      <div className=\"welcome-card\">\n164\t        <div className=\"welcome-head\">\n165\t          <span className=\"welcome-eyebrow\">WELCOME BACK</span>\n166\t          <h1 className=\"welcome-title\">{partial ? 'Most of your JusPrin v1 setup is here' : 'Your JusPrin v1 setup is here'}</h1>\n167\t          <p className=\"welcome-intro\">We copied it from JusPrin v1 on this computer. JusPrin v1 itself is unchanged.</p>\n168\t        </div>\n169\t\n170\t        <AccountBox account={account} status={status} actions={actions} priceCarriesOver={priceCarriesOver} />\n171\t        {priceCarriesOver && subscription && account && !account.rejected && <KeptPrice subscription={subscription} />}\n172\t\n173\t        <div className=\"welcome-list\" aria-label=\"Imported\">\n174\t          <span className=\"welcome-eyebrow\">IMPORTED</span>\n175\t          {report.printers.length > 0 && (\n176\t            <ImportedRow title=\"Printers\" detail={someOf(usablePrinters.length ? usablePrinters : report.printers, 2, ' · ')}\n177\t              count={count(usablePrinters, report.printers)} partial={usablePrinters.length < report.printers.length} />\n178\t          )}\n179\t          {report.presets.length > 0 && (\n180\t            <ImportedRow title=\"Filament and process presets\" detail={someOf(usablePresets.length ? usablePresets : report.presets, 3, ', ')}\n181\t              count={count(usablePresets, report.presets)} partial={usablePresets.length < report.presets.length} />\n182\t          )}\n183\t          {report.connections.length > 0 && (\n184\t            <ImportedRow title=\"Printer connections\" detail={someOf(report.connections, 2, ' · ')} count={`${report.connections.length}`} />\n185\t          )}\n186\t          {report.preferences && <ImportedRow title=\"Preferences\" detail=\"Units, language and recent files\" />}\n187\t          <p className=\"agent-row-note\">\n188\t            {report.unusable.length > 0 &&\n189\t              `“${report.unusable[0]}”${report.unusable.length > 1 ? ` and ${report.unusable.length - 1} more` : ''} can’t be used here: ${report.unusable.length > 1 ? 'they are' : 'it is'} based on a printer JusPrin doesn’t have. `}\n190\t            {report.failed.length > 0 && `${report.failed.length} ${report.failed.length > 1 ? 'files' : 'file'} couldn’t be copied. `}\n191\t            Chats from JusPrin v1 stay in JusPrin v1.\n192\t          </p>\n193\t        </div>\n194\t\n195\t        {/* Signing in is the screen's primary button while the offer stands (board 1c). */}\n196\t        <button type=\"button\" className={`${account ? 'primary' : 'secondary'} welcome-continue`} onClick={actions.close}>Continue</button>\n197\t        <p className=\"agent-row-note\">Imported presets are in your printer and filament menus. Rename or delete them there.</p>\n198\t      </div>\n199\t    </div>\n200\t  );\n201\t}\n202\t"}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","hash":"1fa4ec8be72d9492dec4b30b2961d2c02bfff406966086597a088a0d237587b2","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Environment update\n - Primary working directory: /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin (was /Users/kenneth/Projects/ops/.claude/worktrees/credits-gateway-config)\n\nPlain output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style."}]}}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","id":"aba650af-2644-4572-a91d-e9e4b965ab83","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:15:39.066Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"8d45efdc67b5065b826b225c6fae0a4acb4aba598709c43f8feaca22fa764775","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"c7211fa5-f47d-45c9-bf87-9aa71e467d24","keep":176,"tail":["dff97f5acaa3f32d97a3c967dd6efa4b1f049073f253c2e01d2fc186b4acc5bc","15fa46c4c0a46f5f9866bc8e0165466102bf93662af26be59ac90d1e466638d7","1fa4ec8be72d9492dec4b30b2961d2c02bfff406966086597a088a0d237587b2"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",178,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"38d7cf0f720a00cddd02c0eaa647b8efe3359ee82898dabe271b89f5a7225aef"}
