streams `POST /ent/jusprin/v2/messages` (Anthropic format) and `/responses` (OpenAI format) to an upstream model. `credits.py` admits each turn: a Redis rate l\n50:**Billing.** Chargebee, site `obico`. v1 sells `jusprin-unlimited-monthly` ($6.99) and `jusprin-unlimited-annual` ($59.99) through `web_ent/jusprin/jusprin_cb_views.py`: hosted checkout pages, a callback, a webhook that upserts `JusPrinPlan` and flips the v\n70:  user, kind {pack, subscription, signup, trickle, reward, launch_bonus, adjustment}\n73:  basic_only          bool (trickle lots pay basic turns only)\n75:                      signup, trickle:<yyyy-mm>, report:<print report id>\n80:  alias, tier {basic, expert}, credits (0 for a turn covered by unlimited basic or a free app turn)\n88:`JusPrinPlan` (already there, one row per user) becomes the v2 subscription record too: add `current_term_start`, `current_term_end`, `external_resource_version` as Obico's `Subscription` has, and treat `plan_id` prefixes `jusprin-credits-` as v2 plans. v1'\n94:1. Cost = the alias's `credits` (section 3.4). Origin `app` costs 0 (section 3.3). Tier basic on an active Workshop costs 0 until the fair-use ceiling (section 6), then 1.\n95:2. Lazy trickle: if no `trickle:<this month>` lot exists for the person, create it first (section 3.5). This replaces a monthly sweep over 250k accounts.\n96:3. Draw order: lots that expire soonest first, never-expiring lots last. Among lots with the same expiry, oldest first. `basic_only` lots are skipped for expert turns. So a sign-up lot (30 days) is spent before a subscription lot (term end), and both before\n97:4. Not enough credits: raise so `admit` returns a new `Admission.CREDITS_EXHAUSTED`, which the gateway answers as 402 with code `credits_exhausted` and a body the client can act on: `{\"balance\": 3, \"cost\": 5, \"basic_only_credits\": 0, \"affordable_aliases\": [\n106:Guard: the Redis minute limit already caps 60 turns a minute. Add a daily counter of free app turns per person (Redis, 24 h) and charge them as basic past a daily ceiling. 50 a day is a placeholder: the four harness sessions started 2 to 4 app turns each, \n128:- **Trickle** (decided in principle; size to choose): a monthly lot of `basic_only` credits expiring at the end of the calendar month, created lazily (3.2 step 2). The size, 50, is a placeholder: v1's free-user figures (median 2 chats a month, 90th percent\n141:- **Subscriptions:** plans `jusprin-hobby-monthly` (Hobby, $10, 750 credits) and `jusprin-workshop-monthly` (Workshop, $20, 1,000 credits, unlimited Standard); the `jusprin-credits-` prefix in 3.1 becomes a check on these two ids. The existing `jusprin_cb_\n144:- **Pricing page:** `web_ent/frontend/src/views/jusprin/JusPrinPricingPage.vue` is rewritten to boards 5a and 5b: \"Credits and plans\", three cards (Pay as you go, Hobby, Workshop) each with its expiry rule and its price in messages, the fair-use text (sect\n147:- **v1 subscribers** (decided by Kenneth 2026-11-02 on board 1c: \"grandfathered to the $10/mo tier with the original price\", \"in addition to getting 500 credits\"): people on `jusprin-unlimited-*` move to Hobby and keep their v1 price, $6.99 a month or $59.\n157:  \"credits\": {\"total\": 562, \"lots\": [  // no trickle lot in the first month (2026-11-02)\n160:  \"plan\": {\"id\": \"jusprin-workshop-monthly\", \"name\": \"Workshop\", \"renews_at\": \"...\", \"unlimited_basic\": true,\n161:           \"basic_used_this_term\": 212, \"basic_fair_use\": 600, \"obico_discount\": true,\n165:                       {\"id\": \"jusprin-workshop-monthly\", \"name\": \"Workshop\", \"cents\": 2000, \"credits\": 1000, \"unlimited_basic\": true}]},\n174:`days` and `activity` feed the Account page's usage chart and table (boards 4b, 4c: a total for 30 days, a bar per day, a row per chat with tier, messages and credits, plus reward and clawback rows with their reason). The composer's hover panel needs only \n182:- **A chat keeps its model** (Kenneth, 2026-11-02, \"for now\"): the tier is chosen before the person's first message in a chat and never changes after. A turn the app started (the file-opened report) does not count: it runs on Expert and leaves the pickers \n183:- **Model picker** (`ModelPickers.tsx`): each option shows its price from `ModelOptionInfo.credits` with its unit, \"Expert · 5 credits a message\" and \"Standard · 1 credit a message\" (never \"1 credit\" alone), plus one clause on when to use it. On Standard\n185:- **Balance** (a new `account` host message with the JSON above): the composer shows only a small ring of what is left, no number, no animation (board 2a, \"just like how claude code behaves\"). Hover or tap opens the panel: \"562 credits left.\" (credits only\n186:- **Before sending** (boards 3b, 3d): the app knows the balance and the chat's tier, so when the next message cannot be paid, Send is disabled and one line says why: \"You have 3 credits; this Expert chat needs 5 a message.\" The one action is \"Get more cred\n187:- **Exhaustion** (board 3c, reached only by a race between two sends): the 402 body drives the failed-message card with the same words, \"This message needs 5 credits; you have 3.\", the same single action, and the message returned to the composer. `basic_on\n188:- **\"Get more credits\" everywhere** (Kenneth, board 3c): outside the pricing page there is no \"Buy\" beside \"Subscribe\", because nobody can judge a pack against a plan from a button label. The savings alert (5.3) keeps \"Subscribe\" because it names one plan \n189:- **Preferences › Account** (boards 4a to 4c): the signed-in email and sign out; the plan line (\"Workshop · $16 a month. Renews 1 Dec. Obico Premium Subscriber: 20% off subscriptions.\") with \"Manage plan\" and \"Get more credits\"; the same balance panel a\n191:- **Design:** every colour, size and radius through the token file and `ShellTheme` or CSS variables per `agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md`. The boards exist (canvas version 71, captures in `design-captures/credits-2026-11/`); the tooltip on 2c needs tw\n199:- cost on Workshop = $20 + max(0, expert credits − 1,000) × 2¢ (basic turns free up to fair use);\n220:## 6. Fair use for unlimited basic\n224:- **Ceiling:** a monthly number of Standard messages at no credits; past it, a Standard message costs 1 credit from the balance like on Hobby. 600 is a placeholder chosen from the cost side alone: it caps the worst case at about $6 to $30 of cost on $20 of\n225:- **Rate:** the existing 60 turns a minute, plus the 50 free app turns a day (3.3).\n227:- **Page wording:** \"Unlimited Standard messages for one person using JusPrin by hand; after 600 in a month, Standard messages cost 1 credit each. Expert messages always cost 5 credits.\" Say the number. Every surveyed vendor hides it and gets the anger at \n229:The polling fix (7.2) is what makes the 5¢ case go away; until it ships, the ceiling is the only protection.\n270:- Alerts: margin per tier below 20% for three days; free app turns per person above the daily cap; reward invalid share above 10%.\n274:0. **Port the onboarding branch onto `jusprin-newui`** (app only; no dependency on the ledger). The branch `onboarding-frontend-only` (one commit, `8f4588beae`, 2026-10-06, same on `origin`) adds the first-run path to Home: welcome, import presets from an \n275:1. **Ledger and charging** (gateway + obico-server migration): tables, `charge_turn`, draw order, lazy trickle, sign-up lot, `credits_exhausted` 402 body, `tier`/`credits`/`images` in aliases, `slicer-basic` alias with image stripping, `/account`. Tests in\n276:2. **App:** `X-JusPrin-Request: note`, `credits` in `ModelOptionInfo` and the pickers with \"a message\", pickers greyed once a chat has a message from the person with the tooltip, app-started turns on the Expert alias without storing the chat's model, the a\n293:4. **Trickle size:** CLOSED 2026-11-02: 50 ordinary credits a month, expiring a month after grant. 50 basic-only credits a month as the launch placeholder (recommend), reset from charge records after a month.\n294:5. **Fair-use ceiling on Workshop:** CLOSED 2026-11-02 evening, no ceiling. 600 Standard messages a month as the launch placeholder, stated on the page (recommend), reset from charge records.\n297:8. **v1 unlimited subscribers:** decided, Hobby at their original price plus the 500 (section 4). Still open: the move at sign-in or at term end (recommend sign-in, since the v2 app is where they will be), and the wording about v1's \"unlimited\".\n303:14. **\"New Standard chat\"** CLOSED 2026-11-02 evening, removed with board 3d. carrying only the typed text, and whether board 3d stays at all.\n304:15. **A picture staged in a new Standard chat** before its first message, while the picker still works: the full 3e row, or only the sentence (not drawn).\n305:16. **Thinking picker on Standard:** CLOSED 2026-11-02: Expert only. show it only on Expert (the brainstorm session's suggestion, since Standard has one price) or on both tiers.\n307:Decided during the review (2026-11-02), so no longer here: a chat keeps its model; prices always say \"a message\"; the composer shows only a ring; a bar per expiring lot; \"Get more credits\" is the one action outside the pricing page; no \"New Standard chat\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c2b7a85e-1a05-40ce-bc2b-7b9e6bfbb2de","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
