{"parentUuid":"123d1814-72b3-4299-98f7-5576da6a778b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgea3vEAgp3pjDe5kJaEP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019GjrXvLw5AwE1VLuiLPwZZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin; cp pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md /private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c/scratchpad/plan.before.md; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md'; L=open(p).read().split('\\n')\ndef sub(n,old,new):\n    assert old in L[n-1],(n,old)\n    L[n-1]=L[n-1].replace(old,new)\ndef line(n,startswith,new):\n    assert L[n-1].startswith(startswith),(n,L[n-1][:60])\n    L[n-1]=new\nline(21,'- **Workshop','- **Workshop, $20 a month:** 1,000 credits, and Standard messages cost 0 credits with no ceiling. Expert messages cost 5. Unused credits lost each month.')\nsub(24,'expiring after one month. **Trickle:** a free monthly Standard allowance for light users.','expiring one month after sign-in. During that month the 500 is all there is. **Free credits:** after the first month, every account not on a subscription, pack holders included, gets 50 ordinary credits a month.')\nsub(70,'signup, trickle, reward','signup, free, reward')\ndel_73=L[72]; assert 'basic_only' in del_73\nsub(75,'signup, trickle:<yyyy-mm>,','signup, free:<n>,')\nsub(80,'credits (0 for a turn covered by unlimited basic or a free app turn)','credits (0 for a basic turn on Workshop or a turn the app started)')\nsub(92,'with `select_for_update()` on the person\\'s live lots:','with a row lock on the person (`lock_person`: a person may hold no live lot, so the lots cannot be what serialises charges):')\nline(94,'1. Cost','1. Cost = the alias\\'s `credits` (section 3.4). Origin `app` costs 0 (section 3.3). Tier basic on an active Workshop costs 0 (section 6).')\nline(95,'2. Lazy','2. Lazy free credits: when the first month is over, the person is not subscribed and their last free lot has expired, create the next one first (section 3.5). This replaces a monthly sweep over 250k accounts.')\nline(96,'3. Draw','3. Draw order: lots that expire soonest first, never-expiring lots last. Among lots with the same expiry, oldest first. Every credit is the same, so every lot pays every turn. So a sign-up lot (one month) is spent before a subscription lot if it expires first, and both before a pack.')\nline(97,'4. Not enough','4. Not enough credits: raise, which the gateway answers as 402 with code `credits_exhausted` and the body `{\"balance\": 3, \"cost\": 5, \"plan\": null}`. `errors.py` grows that entry; the old `quota_exhausted` text stays for v1.')\nline(106,'Guard:','Guard: the Redis minute limit caps 60 turns a minute. There is no daily cap on app turns (Kenneth, 2026-11-02).')\nsub(112,'Fast and Thorough cost the same within a tier, as the boards draw it (Expert defaults to Thorough, Standard to Fast).','Only Expert offers Fast and Thorough, at one price, defaulting to Thorough. Standard\\'s `efforts` list is empty, so it has no thinking picker and the request sends no effort.')\nsub(121,'Whether a new chat should default to Expert or Standard is a product decision; I recommend Expert while the person has credits, because the sign-up grant is meant to show the best version, and the picker makes Standard one click away.','Decided (decision 1): a new chat defaults to Expert during the first month and to Standard after it.')\nsub(127,'`expires_at = now + 30 days`','`expires_at` one calendar month after the grant')\nline(128,'- **Trickle','- **Free credits** (decided 2026-11-02): 50 ordinary credits, `kind = free`, `source_ref = free:<n>`, expiring one calendar month after the day of the grant. Granted lazily (3.2 step 2) to an account past its first month with no active subscription, once the previous free lot has expired. A pack holder gets them too; during the first month nobody does. An active v1 plan counts as a subscription, which is my reading, not stated. At 50 the cost is at most about 50¢ a month per person.')\nsub(141,'1,000 credits, unlimited Standard)','1,000 credits, Standard messages cost 0 credits)')\nsub(144,'three cards (Pay as you go, Hobby, Workshop) each with its expiry rule and its price in messages, the fair-use text (section 6), the launch offer on the pack card,','one sentence on what a message costs, three cards (Pay as you go, Hobby, Workshop) each with its expiry rule and no price in messages (Workshop reads \"1,000 credits a month. Standard messages cost 0 credits.\"), the launch offer on the pack card,')\nsub(157,'  // no trickle lot in the first month (2026-11-02)','  // no free lot in the first month')\nsub(161,'\"basic_used_this_term\": 212, \"basic_fair_use\": 600, \"obico_discount\": true,','\"obico_discount\": true,')\nsub(180,'canvas version 71','canvas version 79')\nsub(183,' On Standard the price reads \"free this month\" while free Standard messages last.',' On Workshop the Standard option reads \"Standard · 0 credits a message\". Only Expert has a thinking picker.')\nsub(184,', and a \"New Expert chat\" button beside Remove starts an Expert chat with the typed text and the attachment (board 3d\\'s shape). Send stays enabled;',', styled as the design system\\'s warning (triangle-alert glyph in status-warning beside primary ink), and Remove is the only action on the row (Kenneth: \"remove \\'new expert chat\\' button\"). Send stays enabled;')\na=L[184]; i=a.index('then a bar per expiring lot'); j=a.index('; what the ring measures against is open')\nL[184]=a[:i]+'then a bar per lot, grouped only by expiry, soonest first, labelled by kind with what is left and its date (\"First-month credits · 62 of 500 left · Expires 1 Dec\"; \"Free credits · 50 of 50 left · Expires 2 Dec\"; \"Bought credits · 500 of 500 left · Never expire\"; on Workshop \"Workshop credits · 640 of 1,000 left · Expires 1 Dec. Unused credits don\\'t carry over.\"), fill = what is left; \"Expiring credits are used first.\"; actions \"Get more credits\" and \"See usage\". Free credits get the same ring as any others (Kenneth, board 6a), with no line about them in the composer. The bars need each lot\\'s original size, so `lots[]` carries `granted`; a `reward` lot never expires but is not bought, so the panel needs a label for it (no board shows one yet, decision 13)'+a[j:]\nline(186,'- **Before sending**','- **Before sending** (board 3b): the app knows the balance and the chat\\'s tier, so when the next message cannot be paid, Send is disabled and one line says why: \"You have 3 credits; this Expert chat needs 5 a message.\" The one action is \"Get more credits\", which opens the pricing page. There is no \"New Standard chat\", no \"Send with Standard\" and no \"Switch this chat to Standard\". Earlier than that (board 3a), once, the composer says \"About 25 credits left\" with \"Get more credits\".')\nline(187,'- **Exhaustion**','- **Exhaustion** (board 3c, reached only by a race between two sends): the 402 drives the failed-message card with the same words, \"This message needs 5 credits; you have 3.\", the same single action, and the message returned to the composer. `ProviderAgent::http_error` passes the gateway\\'s message through instead of its fixed text when the code is `credits_exhausted`.')\nsub(189,'the same balance panel as the composer, where the Workshop fair-use count is one more bar (\"Free Standard messages · 188 of 600 left · Resets 1 Dec. After 600, Standard is 1 credit a message until then.\");','the same balance panel as the composer;')\nsub(189,'the alert switch.','the alert switch, whose sub-line is \"Once, above the message box.\"')\nsub(191,'canvas version 71','canvas version 79')\nsub(199,'(basic turns free up to fair use)','(basic turns cost 0)')\nsub(201,'(pack, or current plan).','(pack, or current plan). It never names Pay as you go: the reverse alert, telling a subscriber that Pay as you go would cost less, was removed with board 7c.')\nsub(203,'re-evaluated when','re-evaluated when')\n# section 6\nassert L[219].startswith('## 6.')\nL[219]=\"## 6. Workshop's Standard messages\"\nL[221]='Decided 2026-11-02: no ceiling. A Standard message on an active Workshop subscription costs 0 credits, however many there are. Numbers for the record: a basic message cost 0.4¢ to 1¢ normally and 5¢ when the agent polled the slicer, so Workshop loses money past 400 to 2,000 Standard messages a month after its 1,000 credits of expert are also used. The only limits left are the following:'\nL[223]='- **Rate:** the existing 60 turns a minute.'\nL[224]='- **Automation:** the ledger gives the numbers to act on, and acting is a human step through the admin, not a detector.'\nL[225]=None\nL[226]=None\nL[228]='The polling fix (7.2) is what makes the 5¢ case go away.'\nsub(270,'; free app turns per person above the daily cap;',';')\nsub(275,'lazy trickle,','lazy free credits,')\nsub(275,'draw order (expiring first, basic-only skipped for expert, never-expiring last)','draw order (expiring first, never-expiring last), free credits (none in the first month, pack holders get them, subscribers do not, the next only after the last expired), expiry one calendar month from the grant')\nsub(275,'against one lot (`select_for_update`)','against one lot (the row lock)')\nsub(275,'free app turns and their daily cap,','app turns free with no cap, Workshop Standard always 0,')\nsub(276,'the attachment row\\'s picture notice and \"New Expert chat\" button,','the attachment row\\'s picture notice,')\nsub(276,'the pre-send check with \"Get more credits\" and the conditional \"New Standard chat\",','the pre-send check with \"Get more credits\", the low-balance notice,')\nline(293,'4. **Trickle','4. **Free credits size:** CLOSED 2026-11-02: 50 ordinary credits a month, expiring a month after grant.')\nline(294,'5. **Fair-use','5. **Ceiling on Workshop:** CLOSED 2026-11-02 evening, no ceiling.')\nline(296,'7. **Launch','7. **Launch discount form:** CLOSED 2026-11-02: kept, double credits on packs by server flag.')\nline(290,'1. **Default','1. **Default tier for a new chat:** CLOSED 2026-11-02: Expert during the first month, Standard after it (board 6a).')\nline(302,'13. **Bought','13. **Bought credits:** CLOSED 2026-11-02: a bar, grouped by expiry. Still open: what the composer\\'s ring measures against, and what the panel calls reward credits, which never expire but are not bought.')\nline(303,'14. **\"New','14. **\"New Standard chat\":** CLOSED 2026-11-02 evening, removed everywhere.')\nline(305,'16. **Thinking','16. **Thinking picker on Standard:** CLOSED 2026-11-02: Expert only.')\nsub(307,'no \"New Standard chat\" under 5 spendable credits;','no \"New Standard chat\";')\nL[72]=None\nout=[x for x in L if x is not None]\nopen(p,'w').write('\\n'.join(out))\nEOF\nsed -n 219,228p pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md | cut -c1-120; awk 'NR>12' pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md | grep -n -i \"trickle\\|fair.use\\|\\b600\\b\\|New Standard\\|basic_only\\|free this month\\|Standard or\\|daily cap\\|unlimited\" | cut -c1-170; git status --short pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md; cd .claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin; grep -n \"defaultModel\\|use_chat_model\\|default_model\" Agent/AgentHost.cpp Agent/ProviderProfile.hpp Agent/ModelCatalog.cpp AgentUI/src/state/*.ts AgentUI/src/App.tsx 2>/dev/null | cut -c1-170 | head -20","description":"Rewrite stale plan sections and find the new-chat default","timeout":20000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20903,"cache_read_input_tokens":250108,"output_tokens":6287,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1758},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2