{"parentUuid":"eba0420d-a043-4d5e-a5c1-0495686b3b00","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6b3f9665-7f28-483d-84d9-db7ace5fe0b2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019GjrXvLw5AwE1VLuiLPwZZ","type":"tool_result","content":"## 6. Workshop's Standard messages\n\nDecided 2026-11-02: no ceiling. A Standard message on an active Workshop subscription costs 0 credits, however many ther\n\n- **Rate:** the existing 60 turns a minute.\n- **Automation:** the ledger gives the numbers to act on, and acting is a human step through the admin, not a detector.\n\nThe polling fix (7.2) is what makes the 5¢ case go away.\n\n## 7. The two cost prerequisites\n32:**Gateway.** `web_ent/jusprin/v2/gateway.py` is a raw ASGI endpoint on daphne (`tsdws-prod`) that streams `POST /ent/jusprin/v2/messages` (Anthropic format) and `/resp\n38:**Billing.** Chargebee, site `obico`. v1 sells `jusprin-unlimited-monthly` ($6.99) and `jusprin-unlimited-annual` ($59.99) through `web_ent/jusprin/jusprin_cb_views.py\n75:`JusPrinPlan` (already there, one row per user) becomes the v2 subscription record too: add `current_term_start`, `current_term_end`, `external_resource_version` as Ob\n93:Guard: the Redis minute limit caps 60 turns a minute. There is no daily cap on app turns (Kenneth, 2026-11-02).\n134:- **v1 subscribers** (decided by Kenneth 2026-11-02 on board 1c: \"grandfathered to the $10/mo tier with the original price\", \"in addition to getting 500 credits\"): pe\n147:  \"plan\": {\"id\": \"jusprin-workshop-monthly\", \"name\": \"Workshop\", \"renews_at\": \"...\", \"unlimited_basic\": true,\n152:                       {\"id\": \"jusprin-workshop-monthly\", \"name\": \"Workshop\", \"cents\": 2000, \"credits\": 1000, \"unlimited_basic\": true}]},\n173:- **Before sending** (board 3b): the app knows the balance and the chat's tier, so when the next message cannot be paid, Send is disabled and one line says why: \"You \n264:5. **Rewards:** endpoint, storage, admin, the Print history button and form, the Home card line. Tests: duplicate hash rejected, text too short rejected, daily cap, i\n277:3. **App-started turns:** CLOSED 2026-11-02: free, on Expert, no daily cap.\n282:8. **v1 unlimited subscribers:** decided, Hobby at their original price plus the 500 (section 4). Still open: the move at sign-in or at term end (recommend sign-in, s\n288:14. **\"New Standard chat\":** CLOSED 2026-11-02 evening, removed everywhere.\n289:15. **A picture staged in a new Standard chat** before its first message, while the picker still works: the full 3e row, or only the sentence (not drawn).\n292:Decided during the review (2026-11-02), so no longer here: a chat keeps its model; prices always say \"a message\"; the composer shows only a ring; a bar per expiring l\n?? pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md\nAgentUI/src/state/store.test.ts:179:      providers: [{ id: 'openai', label: 'OpenAI', defaultModel: 'gpt-5.4-mini', state: 'loading', models: [] }],\nAgent/AgentHost.cpp:2772:    if (!use_chat_model(conversation_id, by_person))\nAgent/AgentHost.cpp:3398:            // account is given now; use_chat_model() fixes it at the first.\nAgent/AgentHost.cpp:3454:        providers.push_back(json{{\"id\", provider}, {\"label\", profile->display_name}, {\"defaultModel\", profile->model},\nAgent/AgentHost.cpp:3551:bool AgentHost::use_chat_model(const std::string& conversation_id, bool by_person)\n[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: ../../../../../../../pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"98f37bdc-bc55-408d-871f-2c231a8d6ea4","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:26:08.746Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## 6. Workshop's Standard messages\n\nDecided 2026-11-02: no ceiling. A Standard message on an active Workshop subscription costs 0 credits, however many ther\n\n- **Rate:** the existing 60 turns a minute.\n- **Automation:** the ledger gives the numbers to act on, and acting is a human step through t