place(\"\"\"- Low notice: threshold 5 messages, once per session past it.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"- Low notice: shown at or below 5 messages' worth for the chat's model (25 credits on Expert, 5 on Standard), number rounded to the nearest 5, once per app session, closable, as on board 3a. The threshold and rounding are my fill-in.\n- An active v1 plan counts as a subscription for the free 50. My reading, not stated.\n- Two bought packs share one bar, because they share an expiry (\"grouped only by expiry\"). \"One per lot\" could also mean two bars.\n\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- New-chat default after the first month and \"50 free Standard messages this month\" (board 6a, decision 1).\n- The 7-day expiry notice.\n\"\"\",\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"Thinking picker on Standard (shown). Two-week report limit\"\"\",\"\"\"Two-week report limit\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- Board 3e capture vs design doc on New Expert chat: followed the doc.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"- Rule 10 of Kenneth's rules message says the composer after the first month says \"50 free credits this month\"; MANIFEST versions 77 and 79 record him directly removing it (\"ring for free credits. No reason to make exception\"). Followed the boards: ring, no line.\n- The rules message lists \"the low-balance notice\" among places with message prices in the decision block, while rules 4 and 7 use credits. Followed \"About 25 credits left\".\n- Board 2c tooltip \"Each message you send in this chat costs 5 credits.\" is outside rule 4's list of places with message prices. Kept it, as drawn.\n\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- \"Resets 30 Nov\" in the panel vs board \"1 Dec\": the date is midnight UTC shown in local time.\n\"\"\",\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"Not built\" -A5 \"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md\" | cut -c1-100; ls src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/visual 2>/dev/null | head -3; grep -rn \"credit\\|Credit\" src