{"parentUuid":"fefe944e-9736-439e-88e6-180a8e6f6094","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6b3f9665-7f28-483d-84d9-db7ace5fe0b2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012XYoFtdaCRUxsBsC6WSx16","type":"tool_result","content":"598\n---\nname: live-checks-can-run-on-local-gateway\ndescription: \"Kenneth 2026-11-02: a blocked staging check should run on the local gateway with real keys and come back with screenshots; don't park it waiting for a deploy.\"\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nWhen I reported three approved live chats as blocked because staging lacked the code, Kenneth asked: \"Do you have to deploy the staging test? Why can't you use a local dev test?\" and asked for screenshots to review.\n\n**Why:** the code under test is the same on the local gateway. A deploy is a far bigger step than a compose override, and text checks missed what one screenshot showed at once: a false \"from the file\" warning and a print issue on an example I had reported as working.\n\n**How to apply:** before calling a live check blocked on an environment, ask whether the local stack can run the same code. Real keys for test runs are in `~/.config/jusprin/prompt-test.env`; never print them, and spend limits still need his approval ([[prompt-eval-spend-budget]]). Capture real windows with `app_screenshot`; each one saves a file in the session's `tool-results` folder that can be copied and sent. Recipe: [[real-app-signed-in-without-screen-control]].\n---\nname: real-app-signed-in-without-screen-control\ndescription: \"Drive the real app signed in to a local gateway through an injected page script; which conf keys, why a copied binary dies, and what still needs the screen.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c\n  modified: 2026-11-02T13:45:04.141Z\n---\n\nBuilds on [[live-host-check-via-instrumented-dev-page]]; used 2026-11-02 when screen control of the app was denied.\n\n- Signed-in conf needs all of: `jusprin_agent.{provider=jusprin, jusprin_api_key, enabled=true, cloud_consent=true, jusprin_model_formats=<JSON id→format from GET /ent/jusprin/v2/models>}`, `jusprin_server.base_url`, `jusprin_onboarding.status=completed`. Without the formats the Agent says \"not set up\".\n- An installed printer is `\"models\":[{\"vendor\":\"Custom\",\"model\":\"Generic Klipper Printer\",\"nozzle_diameter\":\"0.4\"}]`, not `vendors`.\n- Kill the app before editing the conf. Replace a scratch binary with `rm` then `cp`: `cp` over a binary that has run gets the new process killed at launch.\n- `Contents/Resources` in the build is a symlink to the worktree. Replace it with a real folder of links before corrupting a resource, or the worktree gets corrupted.\n- Bringing the app forward triggers an account refresh, so to race the gateway (a real 402), change the ledger and send without refocusing.\n- Page text input: native value setter plus an `input` event. A modal Preferences window's page polls as `agent-preferences`.\n- A test preset needs a `version` field or import rejects it.\n- A compose recreate drops env set by a wrapper; check `JUSPRIN_MODEL_ALIASES` before any chat so only the fake upstream is reachable.\n\nStill needs the screen: pointer hover, native file dialogs, Orca's wizard.\n1-free-file-opened-turn.jpg\n2-expert-to-standard-crossing.jpg\n3-cache-check-and-balance-panel.jpg\n4-welcome-back-v1-subscriber.jpg\n5-fresh-install-example.jpg\n6-fresh-install-example-sliced.jpg\n7-fresh-install-home.jpg\n/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c/scratchpad:\nOrcaHomeBackend.keep\nWelcomeBack.keep\nagent-tests.log\naliases-live.json\naliases-prod.json\naliases-stg.json\naliases.json\nartifact-files\nbase-050130\nbase-050147\nbase-050154\nbuild-a.log\nbuild-benchy.log\nbuild-blank.log\nbuild-blank.pid\nbuild-fix.log\nbuild-fresh.log\nbuild-guard.log\nbuild-guard2.log\nbuild-restore.log\nbuild-rules.log\nbuild1.log\nbuild_app.log\nbuild_app2.log\nbuild_app3.log\nbuild_final.log\nbuild_full.log\nbuild_h.log\nbuild_h2.log\nbuild_h3.log\nbuild_h4.log\nbuild_h5.log\nchat3-first.txt\ncompose.ledger.yml\nconfigure.log\ndc.sh\ndef-074314\ndefault-harness.log\ndenoise.py\ne2e_ledger.py\ne2e_low.py\nedit0.py\nedit0b.py\nedit0c.py\nedit0d.py\nfake_upstream.log\nfakeacct.log\nfakeacct.pid\nfakeacct.py\nfe-074148\nfe-074253\nfinal-harness--fresh-example.log\nfinal-harness.log\nfresh-example-guard.log\nfresh-example.log\ngw-mut.log\ngw-tests.log\nh1.BtNN\nh2.OsCT\n#!/bin/zsh\n# Local gateway on the real models staging would use; keys from Kenneth's test key file, never printed.\nS=/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c/scratchpad\nsource ~/.config/jusprin/prompt-test.env\nexport JUSPRIN_MODEL_ALIASES=\"$(cat $S/aliases-live.json)\"\nexport JUSPRIN_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=\"$ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\" JUSPRIN_OPENAI_API_KEY=\"$OPENAI_API_KEY\" JUSPRIN_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=\"$OPENROUTER_API_KEY\"\nexec $S/dc.sh \"$@\"\n#!/bin/zsh\n# Compose in the credits-ledger worktree's own project.\ncd ~/Projects/tsd-enterprise/.claude/worktrees/credits-ledger\nexec docker compose -p credits-ledger -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.override.yml -f /private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c/scratc\n# Local only, kept out of the repo: runs this worktree beside the other stacks.\nservices:\n  web:\n    image: tsd-enterprise-web:latest\n    ports: !override\n      - \"3534:3334\"\n    environment:\n      GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS: ''\n      LT_FILE_STORAGE_MODULE: lib.fs_file_storage\n      ST_FILE_STORAGE_MODULE: lib.fs_file_storage\n      JUSPRIN_OPENROUTER_API_KEY: ${JUSPRIN_OPENROUTER_API_KEY:-}\n      JUSPRIN_V2_CAPTURE_CONTAINER: local-capture\n  db:\n    ports: !reset []\n  redis:\n    ports: !reset []\nwindow.__type=function(text){var t=document.querySelector('textarea');var set=Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(HTMLTextAreaElement.prototype,\nwindow.__buttons=function(){return Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('button')).map(function(b){return (b.getAttribute('aria-label')||b.i\nwindow.__tail=function(n){var t=document.body.innerText;return t.slice(-(n||500));};\n'ok'\n#!/bin/zsh\n# Blocks until the Agent page shows no running turn for 3 checks in a row, up to $1 seconds.\nP=$1; limit=$2; calm=0; started=0\nfor i in $(seq 1 $((limit/3))); do\n  sleep 3; $P/front.sh >/dev/null\n  busy=$(python3 $P/p.py agent \"(()=>{const b=Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('button')).map(x=>x.getAttribute('aria-label')||x.innerText.trim());return b.\n  if [ \"$busy\" = busy ]; then started=1; calm=0; else calm=$((calm+1)); fi\n  [ $calm -ge 3 ] && [ $started = 1 -o $i -gt 10 ] && break\ndone\necho \"after $((i*3))s started=$started state=$busy\"\n7:- \"New Standard chat\" and board 3d are gone: the case only existed because a Standard-only lot could not pay for an Expert chat. A chat that cannot be paid offers \"Get more credits\" only.\n8:- Prices in messages appear only on the picker options, the stop card for the chat's own tier, the pricing page's one sentence, the low-balance notice, and one scale line under the first-month offer\n9:- Kenneth reviewed the list of mechanisms that were mine, not his (2026-11-02, late evening). **Kept:** the launch offer (double credits on packs until a date); the low-balance notice, reworded to \"\n56:**Desktop app.** `ProviderProfile.hpp` row `jusprin` (default model `slicer-1`, `account_sign_in` true) makes `ProviderAgent` send `X-JusPrin-Turn`, `X-JusPrin-Request` (reply or title) and `X-JusP\n58:**Cache control.** `AnthropicCodec.cpp` sets `cache_control: {type: ephemeral}` with no `ttl` on the last tool, the system text and the last user message. The append-only chat record (commit 163543\n97:4. Not enough credits: raise so `admit` returns a new `Admission.CREDITS_EXHAUSTED`, which the gateway answers as 402 with code `credits_exhausted` and a body the client can act on: `{\"balance\": 3,\n108:**Which model an app-started turn uses (decided by Kenneth, 2026-11-02):** always the account's Expert alias, whatever the chat's model is or will be, because the file-opened report has to read th\n118:| `slicer-1` | Expert | expert | 5 | Anthropic `claude-sonnet-5-5` (unchanged, so every existing chat pinned to it keeps working) |\n121:Keeping the id `slicer-1` avoids an `unknown_model` for chats that already exist; only its label changes. The client's default model is the `ProviderProfile` row's `slicer-1`, so new chats default\n123:DeepSeek work the gateway needs: `upstream.py`'s `prepare()` strips image blocks from a request when the chosen backend has `images: false` (the measurement proxy did this; the model's hosts rejec","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ad694bf6-7426-4c4c-bc72-6b1f1fb1fbce","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:31:57.031Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"598\n---\nname: live-checks-can-run-on-local-gateway\ndescription: \"Kenneth 2026-11-02: a blocked staging check should run on the local gateway with real keys and come back with screenshots; don't park it waiting for a deploy.\"\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nWhen I reported three approved live chats as blocked because staging lacked the code, Kenneth asked: \"Do you have to deploy the staging test? Why can't you use a local dev test?\" and asked for screenshots to review.\n\n**Why:** the code under test is the same on the local gateway. A deploy is a far bigger step than a compose override, and text checks missed what one screenshot showed at once: a false \"from the file\" warning and a print issue on an example I had reported as working.\n\n**How to apply:** before calling a live check blocked on an environment, ask whether the local stack can run the same code. Real keys for test runs are in `~/.config/jusprin/prompt-test.env`; never print them, and spend limits still need his approval ([[prompt-eval-spend-budge