{"parentUuid":"6aa5cc93-a383-4e87-9af3-c97a3d3887ae","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6b3f9665-7f28-483d-84d9-db7ace5fe0b2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UnpYHV8DwPG5cgXerMrVdQ","type":"tool_result","content":"4:- Every credit is the same. There is no Standard-only lot. Any mention below of a `basic_only` flag, a \"trickle\" of Standard-only credits, \"Free Standard messages\" or \"Free Standard credit\n5:- Workshop has no ceiling. Standard messages cost 0 credits on Workshop (Kenneth: \"no ceiling. It's probably easier just to say standard messages cost 0 credits\"). Anything below about 600\n7:- \"New Standard chat\" and board 3d are gone: the case only existed because a Standard-only lot could not pay for an Expert chat. A chat that cannot be paid offers \"Get more credits\" only.\n185:- **Before sending** (board 3b): the app knows the balance and the chat's tier, so when the next message cannot be paid, Send is disabled and one line says why: \"You have 3 credits; this\n300:14. **\"New Standard chat\":** CLOSED 2026-11-02 evening, removed everywhere.\n304:Decided during the review (2026-11-02), so no longer here: a chat keeps its model; prices always say \"a message\"; the composer shows only a ring; a bar per expiring lot; \"Get more credit\n# JusPrin Cloud credits: implementation plan (working doc, 2026-11-01, order of work and readiness updated 2026-11-02; b\n\n**Decided 2026-11-02 evening, after Kenneth saw canvas version 73. These override anything below that says otherwise.**\n1:# JusPrin Cloud credits: implementation plan (working doc, 2026-11-01, order of work and readiness\n16:## 1. The plan being implemented\n42:## 2. What exists today\n62:## 3. Gateway: the credit ledger","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c4d158a8-3b5e-405d-b3bf-b0ea2f35709b","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:55:41.754Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"4:- Every credit is the same. There is no Standard-only lot. Any mention below of a `basic_only` flag, a \"trickle\" of Standard-only credits, \"Free Standard messages\" or \"Free Standard credit\n5:- Workshop has no ceiling. Standard messages cost 0 credits on Workshop (Kenneth: \"no ceiling. It's probably easier just to say standard messages cost 0 credits\"). Anything below about 600\n7:- \"New Standard chat\" and board 3d are gone: the case only existed because a Standard-only lot could not pay for an Expert chat. A chat that cannot be paid offers \"Get more credits\" only.\n185:- **Before sending** (board 3b): the app knows the balance and the chat's tier, so when the next message cannot be paid, Send is disabled and one line says why: \"You have 3 credits; this\n300:14. **\"New Standard chat\":** CLOSED 2026-11-02 evening, removed everywhere.\n304:Decided during the review (2026-11-02), so no longer here: a chat keeps its model; prices always say \"a message\"; the composer shows only a ring; a bar per expiring lot; \"Get more credit\n# JusPrin Cloud credits: implementation plan (working doc, 2026-11-01, order of work and readiness updated 2026-11-02; b\n\n**Decided 2026-11-02 evening, after Kenneth saw canvas version 73. These override anything below that says otherwise.**\n1:# JusPrin Cloud credits: implementation plan (working doc, 2026-11-01, order of work and readiness\n16:## 1. The plan being implemented\n42:## 2. What exists today\n62:## 3. Gateway: the credit ledger","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6aa5cc93-a383-4e87-9af3-c97a3d3887ae","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/credits-onboarding","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
{"parentUuid":"c4d158a8-3b5e-405d-b3bf-b0ea2f35709b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgecN4pqTF3EKmiKWaAxQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0133eQNnt3sZ5iBs1hMc6reo","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md","old_string":"## Harness defects fixed to get the checks running","new_string":"## Found by the live local chats on the final rules, 2026-11-02\n\n- Fixed, gateway. With Standard's efforts empty, `/models` sent `default_effort: null` and the app crashed at launch with a JSON type error, because `ModelCatalog.cpp:163` reads that key as a string. The gateway now leaves the key out, with a test that failed first. Released apps have the same line from `ac55c2961a`, so a null reaching them would be expected to crash them too; that part is my inference, no released build was run.\n- Fixed, app. The two-line Standard and Expert rows in the model menu overlapped, because menu rows have a fixed 36-pixel height. Came in with `48ec76705d`. Vitest does not apply CSS, so only the real-app screenshot could see it. The fix is a `height: auto` override in `styles.css`, checked by measuring the rows and a screenshot; there is no automated guard.\n- Open, not fixed. On a Standard chat the app can show the red error \"The automatic chat title could not be generated.\" The live chat hit it once, 18 seconds after the first message. The Standard model sometimes answers the person's message instead of writing a title, the answer is over 120 characters, and `rename_conversation` refuses it. Sending the app's exact title request to Standard directly with the message \"Print it as is. Which layer height am I on?\": 4 of 12 refused (282, 731, 127 and 429 characters), a further run of 3 returned one answer that fit in 120 characters and would be saved as a wrong title. The title request sends no effort in the old or new config, so removing Standard's effort did not cause this. No fix applied because it changes wording the model reads, which needs a live run Kenneth approves. Options: send titles to Expert, tighten the instruction, or fall back to the start of the person's message. The last needs no model and never fails; it is my pick.\n- App-started turns in a chat the person put on Standard run on Expert, as the rules say. In the live run the slice-finished note on the Standard chat made three Expert requests (Sonnet: about 11,000 new cached tokens and 1,300 output) at 0 credits. So one Standard message that starts a slice costs Expert prices in the background. Not a bug; worth knowing for the unit economics.\n- Standard now sends no effort, so the model uses its default and spends reasoning tokens (264 to 524 per request in the live chat, up to 1,007 on a title). A Standard message made three requests.\n\n## Harness defects fixed to get the checks running"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3636,"cache_read_input_tokens":213204,"output_tokens":2743,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":285},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3636,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2743,"cache_read_input_tokens":213204,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3636,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3636},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0133eQNnt3sZ5iBs1hMc6reo":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md","old_string":"## Harness defects fixed to get the checks running","new_string":"## Found by the live local chats on the final rules, 2026-11-02\n\n- Fixed, gateway. With Standard's efforts empty, `/models` sent `default_effort: null` and the app crashed at launch with a JSON type error, because `ModelCatalog.cpp:163` reads that key as a string. The gateway now leaves the key out, with a test that failed first. Released apps have the same line from `ac55c2961a`, so a null reaching them would be expected to crash them too; that part is my inference, no released build was run.\n- Fixed, app. The two-line Standard and Expert rows in the model menu overlapped, because menu rows have a fixed 36-pixel height. Came in with `48ec76705d`. Vitest does not apply CSS, so only the real-app screenshot could see it. The fix is a `height: auto` override in `styles.css`, checked by measuring the rows and a screenshot; there is no automated guard.\n- Open, not fixed. On a Standard chat the app can show the red error \"The automatic chat title could not be generated.\" The live chat hit it once, 18 seconds after the first message. The Standard model sometimes answers the person's message instead of writing a title, the answer is over 120 characters, and `rename_conversation` refuses it. Sending the app's exact title request to Standard directly with the message \"Print it as is. Which layer height am I on?\": 4 of 12 refused (282, 731, 127 and 429 characters), a further run of 3 returned one answer that fit in 120 characters and would be saved as a wrong title. The title request sends no effort in the old or new config, so removing Standard's effort did not cause this. No fix applied because it changes wording the model reads, which needs a live run Kenneth approves. Options: send titles to Expert, tighten the instruction, or fall back to the start of the person's message. The last needs no model and never fails; it is my pick.\n- App-started turns in a chat the person put on Standard run on Expert, as the rules say. In the live run the slice-finished note on the Standard chat made three Expert requests (Sonnet: about 11,000 new cached tokens and 1,300 output) at 0 credits. So one Standard message that starts a slice costs Expert prices in the background. Not a bug; worth knowing for the unit economics.\n- Standard now sends no effort, so the model uses its default and spends reasoning tokens (264 to 524 per request in the live chat, up to 1,007 on a title). A Standard message made three requests.\n\n## Harness defects fixed to get the checks running"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgecN4VjvZKrSwM7KLtHf","requestRef":"17595781-d7af-4e21-9677-07bbf034c21b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"update_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"f0505558-b8db-4c3d-a2da-06742f43bcbf","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:55:52.189Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/credits-onboarding","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
{"parentUuid":"f0505558-b8db-4c3d-a2da-06742f43bcbf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6b3f9665-7f28-483d-84d9-db7ace5fe0b2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0133eQNnt3sZ5iBs1hMc6reo","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"b368972e-f543-4300-8f51-bcb1ee99ee51","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:55:52.300Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md","oldString":"## Harness defects fixed to get the checks running","newString":"## Found by the live local chats on the final rules, 2026-11-02\n\n- Fixed, gateway. With Standard's efforts empty, `/models` sent `default_effort: null` and the app crashed at launch with a JSON type error, because `ModelCatalog.cpp:163` reads that key as a string. The gateway now leaves the key out, with a test that failed first. Released apps have the same line from `ac55c2961a`, so a null reaching them would be expected to crash them too; that part is my inference, no released build was run.\n- Fixed, app. The two-line Standard and Expert rows in the model menu overlapped, because menu rows have a fixed 36-pixel height. Came in with `48ec76705d`. Vitest does not apply CSS, so only the real-app screenshot could see it. The fix is a `height: auto` override in `styles.css`, checked by measuring the rows and a screenshot; there is no automated guard.\n- Open, not fixed. On a Standard chat the app can show the red error \"The automatic chat title could not be generated.\" The live chat hit it once, 18 seconds after the first message. The Standard model sometimes answers the person's message instead of writing a title, the answer is over 120 characters, and `rename_conversation` refuses it. Sending the app's exact title request to Standard directly with the message \"Print it as is. Which layer height am I on?\": 4 of 12 refused (282, 731, 127 and 429 characters), a further run of 3 returned one answer that fit in 120 characters and would be saved as a wrong title. The title request sends no effort in the old or new config, so removing Standard's effort did not cause this. No fix applied because it changes wording the model reads, which needs a live run Kenneth approves. Options: send titles to Expert, tighten the instruction, or fall back to the start of the person's message. The last needs no model and never fails; it is my pick.\n- App-started turns in a chat the person put on Standard run on Expert, as the rules say. In the live run the slice-finished note on the Standard chat made three Expert requests (Sonnet: about 11,000 new cached tokens and 1,300 output) at 0 credits. So one Standard message that starts a slice costs Expert prices in the background. Not a bug; worth knowing for the unit economics.\n- Standard now sends no effort, so the model uses its default and spends reasoning tokens (264 to 524 per request in the live chat, up to 1,007 on a title). A Standard message made three requests.\n\n## Harness defects fixed to get the checks running","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":26,"oldLines":6,"newStart":26,"newLines":14,"lines":[" - Fixed, and this replaces item 3's example details above. The example no longer opens the OrcaSliced 3MF, which had three stacked objects, three filaments and a collision warning. It opens `resources/handy_models/3DBenchy.drc`. `resources/profiles` holds no printable model. The printer is now saved under its own name, \"Generic Klipper Printer\", the way normal printer setup does, so the chip shows no warning triangle or \"from the file\". There is no rule specific to onboarding. Real-app result on an empty data folder: one object, one filament, ~44 min, 12 g, $0.23, no print issue. Cost: Home shows a printer card \"Generic Klipper Printer, Not connected\"."," - Fixed. Choosing a printer on an empty project wrote change rows, and Home listed any empty project with rows, so a blank \"Untitled\" card appeared beside the opened file. `authored_head` in `Workspace/ProjectAutosave.cpp` no longer lists an empty project whose only history is printer, filament or process choices. A chat on an empty plate stays listed. The empty project's folder stays on disk, hidden. This applies to every path that picks a printer on an empty project, not only the example. Only the example path was run; that other paths left a blank card before is inferred from the code."," ","+## Found by the live local chats on the final rules, 2026-11-02","+","+- Fixed, gateway. With Standard's efforts empty, `/models` sent `default_effort: null` and the app crashed at launch with a JSON type error, because `ModelCatalog.cpp:163` reads that key as a string. The gateway now leaves the key out, with a test that failed first. Released apps have the same line from `ac55c2961a`, so a null reaching them would be expected to crash them too; that part is my inference, no released build was run.","+- Fixed, app. The two-line Standard and Expert rows in the model menu overlapped, because menu rows have a fixed 36-pixel height. Came in with `48ec76705d`. Vitest does not apply CSS, so only the real-app screenshot could see it. The fix is a `height: auto` override in `styles.css`, checked by measuring the rows and a screenshot; there is no automated guard.","+- Open, not fixed. On a Standard chat the app can show the red error \"The automatic chat title could not be generated.\" The live chat hit it once, 18 seconds after the first message. The Standard model sometimes answers the person's message instead of writing a title, the answer is over 120 characters, and `rename_conversation` refuses it. Sending the app's exact title request to Standard directly with the message \"Print it as is. Which layer height am I on?\": 4 of 12 refused (282, 731, 127 and 429 characters), a further run of 3 returned one answer that fit in 120 characters and would be saved as a wrong title. The title request sends no effort in the old or new config, so removing Standard's effort did not cause this. No fix applied because it changes wording the model reads, which needs a live run Kenneth approves. Options: send titles to Expert, tighten the instruction, or fall back to the start of the person's message. The last needs no model and never fails; it is my pick.","+- App-started turns in a chat the person put on Standard run on Expert, as the rules say. In the live run the slice-finished note on the Standard chat made three Expert requests (Sonnet: about 11,000 new cached tokens and 1,300 output) at 0 credits. So one Standard message that starts a slice costs Expert prices in the background. Not a bug; worth knowing for the unit economics.","+- Standard now sends no effort, so the model uses its default and spends reasoning tokens (264 to 524 per request in the live chat, up to 1,007 on a title). A Standard message made three requests.","+"," ## Harness defects fixed to get the checks running"," "," All in `tests/shell/shell_harness.cpp`. None of these came from this work: `--print-history` crashed on the Mac on the base commit too."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f0505558-b8db-4c3d-a2da-06742f43bcbf","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/credits-onboarding","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
{"parentUuid":"b368972e-f543-4300-8f51-bcb1ee99ee51","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgecN4pqTF3EKmiKWaAxQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011J59tNY2HYyR9wB9yzUBeD","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md","old_string":"- Windows and Linux: nothing run.","new_string":"- The screens for the first month ended, three bars, low notice, stop card and Workshop were captured with balances seeded directly in the local database. A real first month ending, a real purchase and a real Workshop subscription through billing were not exercised.\n- The 402 failed card (board 3c) on the final rules: Vitest only.\n- Native suites were last run before the CSS fix and the gateway's `default_effort` change, neither of which touches native code. The Agent page suite was rerun after the CSS fix (654 pass).\n- Windows and Linux: nothing run."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3636,"cache_read_input_tokens":213204,"output_tokens":2743,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":285},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3636,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2743,"cache_read_input_tokens":213204,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3636,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3636},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011J59tNY2HYyR9wB9yzUBeD":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md","old_string":"- Windows and Linux: nothing run.","new_string":"- The screens for the first month ended, three bars, low notice, stop card and Workshop were captured with balances seeded directly in the local database. A real first month ending, a real purchase and a real Workshop subscription through billing were not exercised.\n- The 402 failed card (board 3c) on the final rules: Vitest only.\n- Native suites were last run before the CSS fix and the gateway's `default_effort` change, neither of which touches native code. The Agent page suite was rerun after the CSS fix (654 pass).\n- Windows and Linux: nothing run."}},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgecN4VjvZKrSwM7KLtHf","requestRef":"17595781-d7af-4e21-9677-07bbf034c21b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"update_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"bb40c018-f904-4087-868f-0091f92cec44","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:55:55.992Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/credits-onboarding","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
{"parentUuid":"bb40c018-f904-4087-868f-0091f92cec44","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6b3f9665-7f28-483d-84d9-db7ace5fe0b2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011J59tNY2HYyR9wB9yzUBeD","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"e2f5e529-e51d-4e6e-a92c-2d570529de7c","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:55:56.062Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md","oldString":"- Windows and Linux: nothing run.","newString":"- The screens for the first month ended, three bars, low notice, stop card and Workshop were captured with balances seeded directly in the local database. A real first month ending, a real purchase and a real Workshop subscription through billing were not exercised.\n- The 402 failed card (board 3c) on the final rules: Vitest only.\n- Native suites were last run before the CSS fix and the gateway's `default_effort` change, neither of which touches native code. The Agent page suite was rerun after the CSS fix (654 pass).\n- Windows and Linux: nothing run.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":89,"oldLines":6,"newStart":89,"newLines":9,"lines":[" - Board 3e, the picture row in a Standard chat, in the real app: Vitest only, because attaching needs the native dialog."," - \"Get more credits\" was never pressed in the real app, so as not to open a browser. Sign-in itself was not completed; the account was seeded in the conf."," - Real slice polling guard and 1-hour cache ttl against a live provider. The three approved chats ran on the local gateway with real models on 2026-11-02 instead of staging, at Kenneth's request; screenshots are in `live-check-2026-11-02/` in the app worktree.","+- The screens for the first month ended, three bars, low notice, stop card and Workshop were captured with balances seeded directly in the local database. A real first month ending, a real purchase and a real Workshop subscription through billing were not exercised.","+- The 402 failed card (board 3c) on the final rules: Vitest only.","+- Native suites were last run before the CSS fix and the gateway's `default_effort` change, neither of which touches native code. The Agent page suite was rerun after the CSS fix (654 pass)."," - Windows and Linux: nothing run."," - Dark mode in the real app."," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bb40c018-f904-4087-868f-0091f92cec44","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/credits-onboarding","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
{"parentUuid":"e2f5e529-e51d-4e6e-a92c-2d570529de7c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgecN4pqTF3EKmiKWaAxQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012M6FYziT5AdciDNah5Y8Fo","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/standard-title-answers-instead.md","content":"---\nname: standard-title-answers-instead\ndescription: \"2026-11-02 the Standard model (deepseek-v4-flash) answers the message instead of titling it; 4 of 12 replies refused, red error in the app; null default_effort crashes the app\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nMeasured 2026-11-02 through the local gateway, with the app's exact title request and \"Print it as is. Which layer height am I on?\": 4 of 12 replies were over 120 characters and `rename_conversation` refused them, so the person sees \"The automatic chat title could not be generated.\" A reply that answers but fits in 120 characters is saved as a wrong title. Title requests send no effort, so Standard's effort setting has nothing to do with it. Not fixed as of that date.\n\nSame run: the app reads `default_effort` as a string (`ModelCatalog.cpp`), so a null in `/models` crashes it at launch. The gateway leaves the key out when a model has no effort, on `claude/credits-ledger` (uncommitted that day).\n\n**Why:** Standard is the default model after the first month, so the error would reach many people. A config with `default_effort: null` is valid for the gateway's alias parser, which makes the crash easy to bring back.\n\n**How to apply:** Check whether a title fix landed before repeating this. Any wording fix needs a Kenneth-approved live run ([[prompt-eval-spend-budget]]). Related: [[one-action-to-get-more-credits]], [[credits-one-kind-no-ceiling]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creat