{"parentUuid":"25c9ede3-bd40-49ac-80f0-8ea7b510af79","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgecQ5M9aQqVxJMpK9bA3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ci7YtnRbVLAX3HxYhcu3Ez","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md","old_string":"The live chat hit it once, 18 seconds after the first message. The Standard model sometimes answers the person's message instead of writing a title, the answer is over 120 characters, and `rename_conversation` refuses it. Sending","new_string":"The live chat hit it once, 29 seconds after the first message; the title request itself took 17 seconds and returned HTTP 200. That request's reply was not recorded, so its cause is inferred from the direct tries: the Standard model sometimes answers the person's message instead of writing a title, the answer is over 120 characters, and `rename_conversation` refuses it. Sending"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3768,"cache_read_input_tokens":216840,"output_tokens":1126,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":481},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3768,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1126,"cache_read_input_tokens":216840,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3768,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3768},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Ci7YtnRbVLAX3HxYhcu3Ez":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md","old_string":"The live chat hit it once, 18 seconds after the first message. The Standard model sometimes answers the person's message instead of writing a title, the answer is over 120 characters, and `rename_conversation` refuses it. Sending","new_string":"The live chat hit it once, 29 seconds after the first message; the title request itself took 17 seconds and returned HTTP 200. That request's reply was not recorded, so its cause is inferred from the direct tries: the Standard model sometimes answers the person's message instead of writing a title, the answer is over 120 characters, and `rename_conversation` refuses it. Sending"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgecQ4xadMp81aGfDy7Wj","requestRef":"9d1f651a-7b4d-4971-a57e-6b0c6750fa84","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8255de33-5736-4ccd-958a-759672831b5d","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:56:12.500Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/credits-onboarding","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
{"parentUuid":"8255de33-5736-4ccd-958a-759672831b5d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6b3f9665-7f28-483d-84d9-db7ace5fe0b2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ci7YtnRbVLAX3HxYhcu3Ez","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"231747c0-a419-48cf-b69d-77de5295c3df","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:56:12.542Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md","oldString":"The live chat hit it once, 18 seconds after the first message. The Standard model sometimes answers the person's message instead of writing a title, the answer is over 120 characters, and `rename_conversation` refuses it. Sending","newString":"The live chat hit it once, 29 seconds after the first message; the title request itself took 17 seconds and returned HTTP 200. That request's reply was not recorded, so its cause is inferred from the direct tries: the Standard model sometimes answers the person's message instead of writing a title, the answer is over 120 characters, and `rename_conversation` refuses it. Sending","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":30,"oldLines":7,"newStart":30,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," - Fixed, gateway. With Standard's efforts empty, `/models` sent `default_effort: null` and the app crashed at launch with a JSON type error, because `ModelCatalog.cpp:163` reads that key as a string. The gateway now leaves the key out, with a test that failed first. Released apps have the same line from `ac55c2961a`, so a null reaching them would be expected to crash them too; that part is my inference, no released build was run."," - Fixed, app. The two-line Standard and Expert rows in the model menu overlapped, because menu rows have a fixed 36-pixel height. Came in with `48ec76705d`. Vitest does not apply CSS, so only the real-app screenshot could see it. The fix is a `height: auto` override in `styles.css`, checked by measuring the rows and a screenshot; there is no automated guard.","-- Open, not fixed. On a Standard chat the app can show the red error \"The automatic chat title could not be generated.\" The live chat hit it once, 18 seconds after the first message. The Standard model sometimes answers the person's message instead of writing a title, the answer is over 120 characters, and `rename_conversation` refuses it. Sending the app's exact title request to Standard directly with the message \"Print it as is. Which layer height am I on?\": 4 of 12 refused (282, 731, 127 and 429 characters), a further run of 3 returned one answer that fit in 120 characters and would be saved as a wrong title. The title request sends no effort in the old or new config, so removing Standard's effort did not cause this. No fix applied because it changes wording the model reads, which needs a live run Kenneth approves. Options: send titles to Expert, tighten the instruction, or fall back to the start of the person's message. The last needs no model and never fails; it is my pick.","+- Open, not fixed. On a Standard chat the app can show the red error \"The automatic chat title could not be generated.\" The live chat hit it once, 29 seconds after the first message; the title request itself took 17 seconds and returned HTTP 200. That request's reply was not recorded, so its cause is inferred from the direct tries: the Standard model sometimes answers the person's message instead of writing a title, the answer is over 120 characters, and `rename_conversation` refuses it. Sending the app's exact title request to Standard directly with the message \"Print it as is. Which layer height am I on?\": 4 of 12 refused (282, 731, 127 and 429 characters), a further run of 3 returned one answer that fit in 120 characters and would be saved as a wrong title. The title request sends no effort in the old or new config, so removing Standard's effort did not cause this. No fix applied because it changes wording the model reads, which needs a live run Kenneth approves. Options: send titles to Expert, tighten the instruction, or fall back to the start of the person's message. The last needs no model and never fails; it is my pick."," - App-started turns in a chat the person put on Standard run on Expert, as the rules say. In the live run the slice-finished note on the Standard chat made three Expert requests (Sonnet: about 11,000 new cached tokens and 1,300 output) at 0 credits. So one Standard message that starts a slice costs Expert prices in the background. Not a bug; worth knowing for the unit economics."," - Standard now sends no effort, so the model uses its default and spends reasoning tokens (264 to 524 per request in the live chat, up to 1,007 on a title). A Standard message made three requests."," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8255de33-5736-4ccd-958a-759672831b5d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/credits-onboarding","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
{"parentUuid":"231747c0-a419-48cf-b69d-77de5295c3df","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgecQ5M9aQqVxJMpK9bA3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SmC9f7Uw3AFnsa1xky2jH6","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up","input":{"recap":"All 11 credit rules are applied, uncommitted, in the app, gateway and deploy-config worktrees, and the live chats charged 0, 1 and 5 credits as intended. The local test stack is stopped. One bug is open: Standard chats can show a red chat-title error.","ask":"Should I fix the title error by falling back to the start of the person's message?","actions":[{"label":"Yes, use the fallback","message":"Fix the title error here: when the model's reply can't be used as a title, use the start of the person's message as the title and show no error."},{"label":"Not now","message":"Leave the title error open for now."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3768,"cache_read_input_tokens":216840,"output_tokens":1126,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":481},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3768,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1126,"cache_read_input_tokens":216840,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3768,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3768},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SmC9f7Uw3AFnsa1xky2jH6":{"recap":"All 11 credit rules are applied, uncommitted, in the app, gateway and deploy-config worktrees, and the live chats charged 0, 1 and 5 credits as intended. The local test stack is stopped. One bug is open: Standard chats can show a red chat-title error.","ask":"Should I fix the title error by falling back to the start of the person's message?","actions":[{"label":"Yes, use the fallback","message":"Fix the title error here: when the model's reply can't be used as a title, use the start of the person's message as the title and show no error."},{"label":"Not now","message":"Leave the title error open for now."}]}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgecQ4xadMp81aGfDy7Wj","requestRef":"9d1f651a-7b4d-4971-a57e-6b0c6750fa84","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"961c1599-443c-4843-8db8-4f0ba80b56f1","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:56:14.734Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/credits-onboarding","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
